hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1801","1938 - Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sa'd al-Thaqafi al-Isfahani in Damascus informed us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn al-Haytham al-Sabbagh informed them while he was present: Ubaydullah ibn al-Mu'tazz ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us: Ali ibn Hujr narrated: Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated: Humayd narrated: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah intends good for a servant, He employs him. He said: it was said: And how does He employ him, O Messenger of Allah? He said: He grants him success to do a righteous deed before death. Al-Tirmidhi brought it from Ali ibn Hujr, and said: a sound hadith. And this is part of a longer hadith than this which we wrote in full in the next section; sometimes it comes complete, and sometimes abridged."
"1802","Another 1939 - Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn Mahmud ibn al-Akhdar the hafiz in Baghdad informed us: Abu Mansur Abd al-Jabbar ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Tawbah al-Asadi informed them: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqur informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us: Yahya, who is Ibn Sa'id, narrated: al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Marwazi narrated: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which people are dearest to you? He said: A'ishah. They said: We do not mean women? He said: Then her father."
"1803","1940 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Yahya ibn Ali ibn al-Tarrah in Baghdad informed us: Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Umar al-Urmawi informed them: Abu al-Ghana'im Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn al-Ma'mun informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar al-Daraqutni informed us: Abu Amr Yusuf ibn Ya'qub ibn Yusuf al-Naysaburi narrated: Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi narrated: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: they said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are dearest to you? He said: A'ishah. They said: We mean only men? He said: Her father."
"1804","1941 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr al-Khallal narrated: al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan narrated, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated: from Humayd al-Tawil: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which people are dearest to you? He said: A'ishah. They said: We do not mean women? He said: Then her father. Al-Tirmidhi and Ibn Majah both brought it from Ahmad ibn Abdah. And Ibn Majah narrated it from al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Marwazi, both from al-Mu'tamir. And al-Tirmidhi said: a good, sound hadith. Al-Daraqutni said: Mu'tamir is alone in it. He said: And the correct is from Mu'tamir from Humayd from al-Hasan as mursal. He did not mention who narrated it thus. And Abu Hatim al-Razi said: This is a rejected hadith; it may be: Humayd from al-Hasan from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it in his book from Abu Arubah al-Harrani from al-Musayyab ibn Wadih from Mu'tamir from Humayd from al-Hasan from Anas, and Allah knows best what is correct. And it has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Amr ibn al-As."
"1805","Another 1942 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: my grandfather Ishaq informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us (the hadith). 1943 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Zuhayr narrated, they said: Yazid narrated: Humayd informed us: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come a people softer of hearts than you. Then the Ash'aris came, among them Abu Musa, and they began chanting rajaz and saying. Their wording is one. And he said in Ibn Mani's narration: saying, without the waw."
"1806","1944 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Ibn Abi Adi narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come to you peoples softer of hearts than you. He said: Then the Ash'aris came, among them Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, and when they neared Medina they were chanting rajaz, saying:"
"1807","1945 - And Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: my father narrated: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us: from Humayd, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, and he mentioned the like of it, adding: When they arrived, they shook hands, and they were the first to introduce handshaking. And Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Affan and Abd al-Samad from Hammad from Humayd abridged, with mention of handshaking. And he narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id from Humayd, and Yazid: Humayd informed us, and from Abdullah ibn Bakr: Humayd narrated from Anas similarly, but they did not mention handshaking. Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Idris al-Razi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari from Humayd. And al-Nasa'i brought it in al-Manaqib from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna from Khalid ibn al-Harith from Humayd similarly. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban brought it from Umar ibn Muhammad al-Hamdani from Ahmad ibn Sa'id al-Hamdani from Ibn Wahb from Yahya ibn Ayyub from Humayd."
"1808","Another 1946 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi there informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Ibn Abi Adi narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was resident, he would observe i'tikaf in the last ten of Ramadan, and when he traveled, he would observe i'tikaf of twenty in the following year. Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: my father said: I heard this hadith only from Ibn Abi Adi from Humayd from Anas. Al-Daraqutni said: Ibn Abi Adi is alone in it, while Hammad ibn Salamah narrated it from Humayd from Abu Nadrah from Abu Sa'id. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Bundar from Ibn Abi Adi from Humayd from Anas, and said: a good, sound, strange hadith from Anas's hadith. And Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sami from Ahmad ibn Hanbal."
"1809","Another 1947 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us: Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Wuhban narrated: Khalid narrated: from Humayd: from Anas."
"1810","1948 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Wahb, who is Ibn Baqiyyah, narrated, he said: Khalid informed us: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked, it was as if he leaned forward. Their wording is one. Abu Dawud al-Sijistani brought it in his Sunan from Wahb ibn Baqiyyah, also called Wuhban. And Abu al-Qasim al-Tabarani narrated it from Bakr ibn Sahl from Shu'ayb ibn Yahya from Yahya ibn Ayyub from Humayd from Anas, and said: none narrated it from Humayd except Yahya ibn Ayyub."
"1811","1949 - Abu al-Daw Shihab ibn Mahmud ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Hatimi al-Harawi there informed us: Isma'il ibn Abi al-Fath ibn Isma'il al-Mustamli, Ahmad ibn Abi Sahl ibn Yazdad al-Qayini, and Mansur ibn Hatim ibn Habib al-Habibi informed them: Abu Ata Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us: Abu Mu'adh al-Shah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mun al-Harawi informed us: Ali ibn Abdullah, who is Ibn Dinar ibn Mubashshir al-Wasiti, narrated: Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated: Abd al-Wahhab narrated: Humayd narrated: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of medium stature, of goodly build, neither tall nor short; his hair was neither curly nor straight; brownish in complexion; when he walked, he leaned forward. Al-Tirmidhi brought it from Humayd ibn Mas'adah from Abd al-Wahhab, and said: a good, sound, strange hadith. In it are wordings not in the Sahih, and Allah knows best, namely his saying: brownish in complexion, when he walked as if he leaned forward. The hadith at the end of the section."
"1812","Another 1950 - Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad ibn Yusuf informed us by ijazah, and my maternal uncle the learned Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us from him: Abu Tahir Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Yusuf informed them, he said: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bishran informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mas'ud al-Daraqutni the hafiz narrated: Muhammad ibn Makhlad narrated: Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: from Humayd al-Tawil: from Anas ibn Malik: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Grapes are not to be sold until they turn black, nor grain until it hardens. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Hasan ibn Musa from Hammad."
"1813","1951 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Abd al-A'la narrated: Hammad narrated: Humayd narrated, I think from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1814","1952 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani in Isfahan informed us: Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us: Ahmad ibn Bundar al-Sha''ar informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Abd al-A'la narrated: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruit until it shows ripeness, selling grapes until they turn black, and selling grain until it hardens. The wording is one. His saying: until it shows ripeness, is mentioned in the Sahih. Abu Dawud and al-Tirmidhi both brought his saying: grapes... to the end, from al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Khallal from Abu al-Walid, Affan, and Sulayman ibn Harb. And Ibn Majah brought all of it from Ibn al-Muthanna from Hajjaj, all from Hammad. And al-Tirmidhi said: a good, strange hadith known only from Hammad ibn Salamah's hadith. And Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban brought it in his book through Hammad ibn Salamah from Humayd."
"1815","Another 1953 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi there informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Affan narrated: Hammad narrated: from Humayd: that Anas was asked about the hair of the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: I never saw hair more like the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than Qatadah's hair. So Qatadah rejoiced that day."
"1816","1954 - Zahir ibn Ahmad in Isfahan informed us: Abu Abdullah al-Khallal al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Zuhayr narrated: Affan narrated: Hammad narrated: from Humayd: that Anas was asked about the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: I never saw hair more like the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than Qatadah's hair. So Qatadah rejoiced that day."
"1817","Another 1955 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani in Isfahan informed us: Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Judge Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Wuhban ibn Baqiyyah narrated: Khalid narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brownish in complexion."
"1818","1956 - Zahir ibn Ahmad in Isfahan informed us: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated: Khalid informed us: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the color of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brownish. And al-Thaqafi narrated it from Humayd."
"1819","1957 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr, grandson of Husayn ibn Mandah, informed us: Abu Mansur Mahmud ibn Isma'il informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abu Bakr Abdullah al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Abu Musa narrated: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated: Humayd narrated: from Anas, he said: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brownish in complexion."
"1820","Remaining hadith of Humayd al-Tawil from Anas 1958 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath al-Saydalani in Isfahan informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad al-Muqri informed them while he was present: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Affan narrated: Hammad narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: no person was dearer to them than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), yet when they saw him they would not stand for him, knowing his dislike of that."
"1821","1959 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi in Baghdad informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated: my father narrated to me: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: from Humayd (the hadith). 1960 - And Ahmad said: Affan narrated: Hammad narrated: Humayd informed us: from Anas, he said: no person was dearer to them to see than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), yet when they saw him they would not stand, knowing his dislike of that (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Ibn Mahdi's narration does not contain seeing. And he also narrated it from Abd al-Samad: Hammad narrated: Humayd narrated from Anas similarly, and from Affan: Hammad narrated: Humayd narrated."
"1822","1961 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi in Isfahan informed us: Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh al-Khabbaz, informed us: Abu Bakr Ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated: Hammad narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: no person in the world was dearer to them to see than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when they saw him they would not stand for him, knowing his dislike of that. Al-Tirmidhi brought it from al-Darimi from Affan, and said: a good, sound, strange hadith."
"1823","Another 1962 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fath ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Tahir al-Sa'igh al-Mu'allim in Isfahan informed us: Abu al-Muzahhar al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Saydalani informed them: Abu Talib Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Adib al-Bayyi' informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Milah al-Faqih informed us: Abu Amr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Hakim al-Madini narrated: Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Idris ibn al-Mundhir al-Hanzali in al-Rayy narrated: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated: Humayd narrated to me: from Anas, he said: Thabit ibn Qays addressed upon the arrival of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Medina, saying: We shall protect you as we protect ourselves and our children; what is for us? He said: Paradise. They said: We are pleased, O Messenger of Allah."
"1824","1963 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi the blind informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abdullah al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated: Khalid ibn Abdullah informed us: from Humayd: from Anas: that Thabit ibn Qays al-Ansari addressed upon the arrival of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: We shall protect you as we protect women, and in one copy: ourselves and our children; what is for us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: For you is Paradise. He said: We are pleased. Al-Nasa'i brought it in al-Manaqib from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna from Khalid ibn al-Harith from Humayd similarly."
"1825","Another 1964 - Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Saffar the mufti in Naysabur informed us: Wajih ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Azhari informed us: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Makhladi informed us: Abu Bakr al-Isfarayini, who is Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Muslim, informed us: Muhammad ibn Ghalib, meaning al-Antaki, narrated: Abu al-Jawwab, who is al-Ahwas ibn Jawwab, narrated: Zuhayr narrated: from Humayd: from Anas ibn Malik, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no jallab nor junub, nor shighar in Islam. And Ma'mar narrated it from Thabit from Anas. Al-Nasa'i brought it in marriage from Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali from Muhammad ibn Kathir from al-Fazari from Humayd from Anas."
"1826","Another 1965 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: my grandfather Ishaq informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us: Hushaym narrated: Humayd informed us: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed wearing a garment whose ends he had crossed. Sufyan narrated it from Humayd."
"1827","1966 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us: Ibn al-Husayn informed us: Ibn al-Mudhhib informed us: Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated: Sufyan narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the last prayer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, he wore a cloak wrapped around himself while sitting."
"1828","1967 - And Ahmad said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed behind Abu Bakr in a single garment while sitting."
"1829","1968 - And Ahmad also said: Sulayman narrated: Isma'il narrated: Humayd informed me: from Anas, he said: the last prayer the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with the people, he prayed in a single garment wrapped around himself, behind Abu Bakr."
"1830","1969 - Uthman ibn Mahmud ibn Abi Bakr Jabbuwayh informed us: Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khurshayd informed us of his saying: al-Husayn ibn Isma'il al-Mahamili narrated: Ali ibn Harb narrated: Qasim ibn Yazid narrated: from Sufyan: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the last prayer the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed was in a cloak wrapped around himself. And Mu'tamir also narrated it from him."
"1831","1970 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu al-Fath Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri narrated: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated: Muhammad ibn al-Mutawakkil ibn Abi al-Sari narrated: Mu'tamir narrated: Humayd narrated: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the last prayer he prayed was in a single garment, sitting in the mosque. And Hammad narrated it from him."
"1832","1971 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us: Abu Nasr narrated, he said: Hammad narrated: from Humayd: from Anas and al-Hasan: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out leaning on Usamah, wearing a Qitri garment whose ends he had crossed, and led them in prayer."
"1833","1972 - Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sa'd al-Thaqafi al-Isfahani in Damascus informed us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn al-Haytham al-Sabbagh informed them while he was present: Ubaydullah ibn al-Mu'tazz ibn Mansur al-Naysaburi, who came to us, informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, read to him: my grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us, he said: Ali ibn Hujr narrated: Isma'il ibn Ja'far al-Madani narrated: Humayd narrated: from Anas, he said: the last prayer the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with the people, he prayed in a single garment wrapped around himself, behind Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him. And it has preceded in Humayd's narration from Thabit from Anas. Al-Nasa'i brought it from Ali ibn Hujr al-Sa'di."
"1834","Another 1973 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah in Isfahan informed us: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu al-Qasim al-Qushayri, who is Abd al-Karim ibn Hawazin, and Abu Bakr al-Maghribi, who is Ahmad ibn Mansur, informed us, they said: Abu al-Husayn al-Khaffaf informed us: Abu al-Abbas al-Sarraj informed us: Abu al-Ash'ath narrated: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated, he said: I heard Humayd narrating from Anas, he said: a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the time of the morning prayer; the next morning when dawn split, he commanded and the prayer was established, and he led us; the following day he delayed until it was light, then commanded and the prayer was established, and he led us, saying: Where is the one asking about the prayer time? Between these two is the time. A group narrated it from Humayd."
"1835","1974 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us (the hadith). 1975 - And Zahir also informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Zuhayr narrated, they said: Yazid, who is Ibn Harun, narrated: Humayd informed us: from Anas: that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the time of the Fajr prayer; he commanded Bilal, who called the adhan when dawn rose, then the iqamah was made and he prayed; the next day he delayed the prayer until it was light, then commanded him and the iqamah was made and he prayed; when he finished, he said: Where is the questioner? The man stood, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Between this and this is the time. The wording is Ahmad ibn Mani's."
"1836","1976 - Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sa'd al-Thaqafi in Damascus informed us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn al-Haytham al-Sabbagh informed them while he was present: Ubaydullah ibn al-Mu'tazz ibn Mansur al-Naysaburi informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: my grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us: Ali ibn Hujr narrated: Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated: Humayd narrated: from Anas: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the time of the morning prayer; the next morning when dawn split, he commanded that the prayer be established, and he prayed; the following day he delayed it until it was light, then commanded and the prayer was established, and he led us in prayer, then said: Where is the one asking about the prayer time? Between these two is the time. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Isma'il, Yahya ibn Sa'id, and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari from Humayd. Al-Nasa'i brought it from Ali ibn Hujr al-Sa'di. And it has a witness in Muslim from the hadith of Abu Musa and Buraydah ibn al-Husayb."
"1837","Another 1977 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us: Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Wuhban narrated: Khalid narrated: from Humayd: from Anas ibn Malik (the hadith)."
"1838","1978 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi in Isfahan informed us: al-Husayn al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Wahb narrated: Khalid narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not admire anyone's deed until you see how it ends for him; a worker works for a time of his life or a period of his life doing a righteous deed, upon which had he died he would have entered Paradise, then he changes and does an evil deed. And a servant works for a time of his life doing a deed upon which had he died he would have entered Hell, then he changes and does a righteous deed. When Allah intends good for a servant, He employs him before his death and grants him success to do a righteous deed. Their wording is close, the wording is Ibn Abi Asim's. And in Abu Ya'la's narration: how it ends for him? And with him: had he died he would have entered Paradise. And with him: with an evil deed upon which had he died he would have entered Hell. And with him: when Allah intends good for a servant, He employs him before his death. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and how does He employ him? He said: He grants him success to do a righteous deed, then takes his soul."
"1839","1979 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Ibrahim al-Sami narrated: Hammad narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man works for a period of his life doing the deeds of Paradise's people, then a year before his death he does the deeds of Hell's people and dies and enters Hell. And a man works for a period of his life doing the deeds of Hell's people, then a year before his death he does the deeds of Paradise's people and dies and enters Paradise."
"1840","1980 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qurashi informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us: Yazid narrated: Humayd informed us: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It does you no harm not to admire anyone until you see how it ends for him; a worker works for a time of his life or a period of his age doing a righteous deed upon which had he died he would have entered Paradise, then he changes and does an evil deed. And a servant works for a time of his life doing an evil deed upon which had he died he would have entered Hell, then he changes and does a righteous deed."
"1841","1981 - The hafiz Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Silafi informed us by ijazah, and our shaykh the Imam hafiz Abu Muhammad Abd al-Ghani ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Ali ibn Surur al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us from him: Abu Abdullah al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed them: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Nazif al-Misri informed us: Abu al-Fadl al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Rafi'i informed us: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn Shaddad narrated: Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad al-Narsi narrated: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated: Humayd narrated to me: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It does you no harm not to admire anyone until you see how it ends for him... and he mentioned the like of it. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yazid ibn Harun from Humayd from Anas, and from Affan from Hammad from Humayd from Anas as marfu'. And he narrated it from Ibn Abi Adi from Humayd from Anas as mawquf, with at its end: Humayd once raised it then refrained from it. And Musa ibn Isma'il narrated it from Hammad from Humayd from al-Hasan from Anas, and it has preceded in al-Hasan's narration."
"1842","Another 1982 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf in Baghdad informed us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqqur informed us: Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Daqqaq informed us: Abdullah, who is Ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi, narrated: Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Hushaym narrated, he said: Humayd al-Tawil informed us: from Anas ibn Malik, he said: when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divorced Hafsah, he was commanded to take her back, so he took her back."
"1843","1983 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi in Isfahan informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated: Hushaym narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he divorced Hafsah, was commanded to take her back, so he took her back. Qatadah narrated the like of it from Anas."
"1844","1984 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Saydalani informed us: Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us: Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us: Isma'il ibn Abdullah narrated: Abu Asim Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Asad narrated: Yahya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: that Abu Musa asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a mount and found him busy, so he said: By Allah I shall not mount you, by Allah I shall not mount you. When he turned away, he called him and said: O Messenger of Allah, did you not swear you would not mount me? He said: And now I swear I shall mount you."
"1845","1985 - Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sa'd al-Thaqafi in Damascus informed us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad al-Sabbagh informed them while he was present: Ubaydullah ibn al-Mu'tazz ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: Ali ibn Hujr narrated: Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated: Humayd narrated: from Anas: that Abu Musa al-Ash'ari came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking for a mount while he was as if busy, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah I shall not mount you, by Allah I shall not mount you. He said: When Abu Musa turned away, he called him to mount him, and he said: O Prophet of Allah, you swore you would not mount me. He said: By Allah I shall mount you, by Allah I shall mount you."
"1846","1986 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Qurashi informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us: Yazid narrated, he said: Humayd informed us: from Anas: that Abu Musa asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a mount (the hadith)."
"1847","1987 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us: Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated: Yazid ibn Harun narrated: Humayd al-Tawil informed us: from Anas: that Abu Musa asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a mount and found him busy, so he swore he would not mount him, then he mounted him, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, you swore you would not mount me. He said: And I swear I shall mount you, so he mounted him."
"1848","1988 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harbi informed us: Hibatullah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Ibn Abi Adi narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: that Abu Musa asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a mount and found him busy, so he said: By Allah I shall not mount you. When he turned his back, he called him and mounted him, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, you swore you would not mount me. He said: So I swear I shall mount you. And Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan, Khalid ibn Abdullah, Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah, and Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated it from Humayd similarly. And Affan ibn Muslim narrated it from Hammad from Humayd, he said: I heard Anas: that Abu Musa said: we asked for mounts. I say: similar to this is narrated in the two Sahihs in more than one hadith: a Companion narrating it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), sometimes narrating it from another Companion from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Among that is Anas ibn Malik's narration from Zayd ibn Thabit: that he took suhur with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Bukhari and Muslim brought it from Qatadah's narration from Anas from Zayd ibn Thabit. And al-Bukhari narrated it from Anas's narration: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Zayd ibn Thabit took suhur, from Qatadah's narration from Anas. And al-Bukhari and Muslim narrated it from Shu'bah's narration from Qatadah from Anas from Ubadah ibn al-Samit from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The believer's vision is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood. And Muslim narrated it from Thabit's narration from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And al-Bukhari cited it as evidence, saying: Thabit narrated it from Anas, and saying: Humayd narrated it from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1849","Another 1989 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ya'la narrated: Zuhayr narrated: Abdullah, who is Ibn Bakr, narrated: Humayd narrated: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man of Banu al-Najjar: Accept Islam. He said: I find myself reluctant. He said: Accept Islam even if you are reluctant. Yahya ibn Sa'id, Ibn Abi Adi, Khalid ibn Abdullah, and al-Ansari narrated it from Humayd."
"1850","1990 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Ibn Abi Adi narrated: from Humayd (the hadith). 1991 - Abdullah said: my father narrated: Yahya, who is Ibn Sa'id, narrated: Humayd narrated: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: Accept Islam. He said: I find myself reluctant. He said: Accept Islam even if you are reluctant. Their wording is one."
"1851","1992 - The khatib Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Harrani in Harran informed us: Abu al-Fath Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Salman informed them: Abu al-Fadl Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan ibn Shadhan informed us, he said: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafi'i read to me: Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn Matar narrated: Wahb, meaning Ibn Baqiyyah, narrated: Khalid, meaning Ibn Abdullah, informed us: from Humayd: from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man of Banu al-Najjar: O uncle, accept Islam. He said: I find myself reluctant. He said: Even if you are reluctant to it, you were compelled to it. Abu Hatim al-Razi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari from Humayd. And Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated it from Abu Khalid al-Ahmar from Humayd also."
"1852","Another 1993 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn al-Fakhir al-Qurashi in Isfahan informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: my grandfather Ishaq informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us: Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a boy on the road; when his mother saw him, she feared the beasts would trample him, so she hastened, saying: My son, my son, until she picked him up. The people said: This woman would never cast her son into the Fire. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, He would never cast His beloved into the Fire."
"1853","1994 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Ibn Abi Adi narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed among a group of his Companions."
"1854","1995 - (the hadith) And Hibatullah ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Muzaffar ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sibt in Baghdad informed us: his father al-Hasan informed them: my father al-Muzaffar ibn al-Hasan informed us: Abu al-Khattab, who is al-Husayn ibn Haydarah ibn Umar ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Khattab al-Baghdadi, informed us in Hamadhan: Abu Abdullah the judge, who is al-Husayn ibn Isma'il, narrated: Abu al-Ash'ath Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated: Humayd narrated: from Anas, he said: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed among a group of his Companions, with a boy on the road; when his mother saw the people, she feared for her child being trampled, so she came hastening, saying: My son, my son, and she hastened, meaning she took him. A people said: O Messenger of Allah, this woman would never cast her son into the Fire. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them specifically, saying: Nor would Allah, mighty and majestic, cast His beloved into the Fire. The wording is Abu al-Ash'ath's. And in Ahmad ibn Hanbal's narration: and she hastened and took him. And in it: the people said. And in it: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lowered them and said: Nor would Allah cast; the rest is the same."
"1855","1996 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us: al-Husayn informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Ya'la informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated: Humayd narrated: from Anas, he said: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed among a group of his Companions, and there was a boy on the road; his mother feared the boy would be trampled, and she was heard saying: My son, my son, and she took him like one frantic. The people said: O Messenger of Allah, this woman would never cast her son into the Fire. He said: Nor would Allah cast His beloved into the Fire. And Imam Ahmad also narrated it, and Abu Hatim al-Razi from Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari: Humayd narrated from Anas similarly. And this hadith has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Umar ibn al-Khattab."
"1856","Another 1997 - The judge Abu al-Hasan Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Umari in Baghdad informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Bazzaz informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari informed us: Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Kharaqi informed us: Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Firyabi informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Husayn ibn Ali narrated: from Za'idah: from Humayd: from Anas."
"1857","1998 - (the hadith) And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Ya'la informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Husayn al-Ju'fi narrated: from Za'idah: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: I never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Maghrib until he broke his fast, even with a drink of water. Their wording is one, except that al-Firyabi said: pray until."
"1858","1999 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us: Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated: Abu Bakr narrated: Husayn ibn Ali narrated: from Za'idah: from Humayd: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not pray until he broke his fast, even with a drink of water. Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti brought it from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili."
"1859","Another 2000 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us: Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us: Isma'il ibn Abdullah narrated: Arim ibn al-Fadl narrated: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer's lower garment is to the middle of his shins."
"1860","2001 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali in Baghdad informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated: my father narrated to me: Ali ibn Ishaq narrated: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak informed us: Humayd narrated. 2002 - Abdullah said: my father narrated to me: Abu al-Nadr narrated: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Talhah, narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The lower garment is to the middle of the shin or to the ankles; there is no good in what is below that. The wording is Abu al-Nadr's from Muhammad ibn Talhah, and Ibn al-Mubarak's hadith is similar."
"1861","2003 - My maternal uncle the learned Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us: Abu al-Fath Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Salman informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Narsi informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shafi'i informed us: Ishaq, who is Ibn al-Hasan ibn Maymun, narrated: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated: Abu Shihab narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lower garment is to the middle of the shin. It was hard upon some people. He said: Or to the ankles, and there is no good in what is below that."
"1862","2004 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani, as I see, informed us: Mahmud ibn Isma'il informed them while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated: from Hammad ibn Salamah: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lower garment is from here, meaning the middle of the shin, to here, until it reached the ankles; there is no good in what is below that. And Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated it from Muhammad ibn Salamah from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Humayd from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The believer's lower garment... and he mentioned it."
"1863","Another 2005 - al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Yahya narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: we used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then one of us would come to Banu Salimah while still seeing the sites of his arrows. And Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari from Humayd similarly. And likewise he narrated it from Abd al-Wahid Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad from Humayd."
"1864","2006 - The hafiz Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Silafi informed us in his book, and the Imam Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Khalaf ibn Rajih al-Maqdisi informed us from him: Abu Mas'ud Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Sudharjani and his brother Abu al-Fath informed us, they said: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Milah al-Faradi informed us: Abu Amr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Hakim al-Madini narrated: Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Idris ibn al-Mundhir al-Hanzali in al-Rayy narrated: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Anas narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: we used to pray Maghrib, then one of us would go to Banu Salimah while seeing the site of his arrow."
"1865","2007 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn al-Nu'man informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ishaq ibn Nafi' narrated: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated: Marwan narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: we used to pray Maghrib in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we would come to Banu Salimah, with one of us seeing the sites of his arrows."
"1866","2008 - The Imam Abd al-Razzaq ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Abi Salih al-Jili in Baghdad, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Urmawi informed them: Ali ibn al-Busri informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us: Abdullah, who is Ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi, narrated: Abu al-Rabi' al-Zahrani narrated: Abu Shihab narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: we used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then a man of us would return to Banu Salimah while seeing the site of his arrow."
"1867","2009 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf in Baghdad informed us: al-Mubarak ibn Ahmad ibn Barakah al-Kindi informed them: Asim ibn al-Hasan ibn Asim informed us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Mahdi informed us: Abu Amr Uthman ibn Ahmad ibn Abdullah known as Ibn al-Sammak narrated by dictation: Abu Awf Abd al-Rahman ibn Marzuq narrated: Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated: Humayd al-Tawil narrated: from Anas ibn Malik, he said: we used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we would leave, and one of us would see the site of his arrow. And it has a witness in the Sahih from Rafi' ibn Khadij's narration."
"1868","Another 2010 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah in Isfahan informed us: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abd al-Karim ibn Hawazin al-Qushayri and Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Khalaf al-Maghribi informed us: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Khaffaf informed us: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Jarir narrated: Hafs ibn Umar al-Darir narrated: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Witr: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One."
"1869","2011 - Abu al-Mafakhir Uthman ibn Mahmud ibn Abi Bakr Jabbuwayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khurrashidh informed us of his saying: al-Husayn ibn Isma'il al-Mahamili narrated: Ubaydullah ibn Jarir ibn Jabalah narrated: Abu Umar al-Darir narrated: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Witr: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, the One."
"1870","Another 2012 - al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah, also called Hisham, informed us: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Makhladi informed us: Abu al-Abbas al-Sarraj informed us: Sawwar ibn Abdullah al-Qadi narrated: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated, he said: I heard Humayd narrating from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram for a pain in his head."
"1871","2013 - The Imam Abu Bakr Abd al-Razzaq ibn Abd al-Qadir al-Jili informed us: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Urmawi informed them: Ali ibn al-Busri informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us: Abdullah, who is al-Baghawi, narrated: Muhammad, who is Ibn Abi Saminah, narrated: Mu'tamir narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram for a pain in his head."
"1872","2014 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi there informed us: Hibatullah ibn al-Husayn informed them: Abu Ali Ibn al-Mudhhib informed us: Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us: Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated: my father narrated to me: Ali ibn Abdullah narrated: Mu'tamir narrated, he said: I heard Humayd narrating, he said: Anas was asked about cupping for one in ihram? He said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped for a pain he had. And it is narrated from Qatadah from Anas. And it has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abdullah ibn Buhaynah."
"1873","Another 2015 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Qurashi in Isfahan informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed us: Ubaydullah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani' informed us: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah al-Fazari narrated: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to prayer, let him walk calmly and pray what he catches, and make up what he missed."
"1874","2016 - Abu al-Futuh Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Sa'id Muhammad in Damascus informed us: Hibat al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd al-Karim informed them: my grandfather Abu al-Qasim, meaning Abd al-Karim, informed us: Abu al-Husayn al-Khaffaf informed us: Abu al-Abbas al-Sarraj informed us: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated: Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated: Humayd narrated: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to prayer, let him walk calmly; let him pray what he catches, and make up what he missed."
"1875","2017 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali ibn al-Ma'tush in Baghdad informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated: Humayd informed us: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes to prayer, let him walk calmly; what he catches he prays, and what he missed he completes. And Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Affan from Hammad from Humayd, Qatadah, and Thabit similarly. And he also narrated it from Ibn Abi Adi and Sahl ibn Yusuf from Humayd. And this hadith comes at the end of a hadith whose beginning Muslim narrated but did not narrate this addition, as far as I know, namely he said: The prayer was established, and a man came hurrying and arrived out of breath; when he reached the row he said: Praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed praise, the hadith. And Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated it from Humayd."
"1876","2018 - Abu al-Muzaffar Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Sam'ani in Marw informed us: Abu Ali al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Khalaf al-Shirazi informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmish al-Ziyadi informed us: Abu Uthman Amr ibn Abdullah al-Basri in Naysabur informed us: Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Habib al-Abdi al-Farra al-Naysaburi informed us: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated: Muhammad, who is Ibn Ja'far, brother of Isma'il ibn Ja'far al-Madini, narrated: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to me: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you come to prayer, calmness is upon you; what you catch, pray, and what you miss, make up. And this hadith has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Qatadah and Abu Hurayrah."
"1877","Another 2019 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani in Isfahan informed us: Mahmud ibn Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi informed them while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated: Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated: from Abbad: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loved thufal."
"1878","2020 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi there informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Abdullah narrated: my father narrated to me: Abu Ja'far al-Mada'ini narrated: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated: from Humayd al-Tawil: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked thufal. Abbad said: meaning the residue of broth. Al-Tirmidhi brought it in the Shama'il from al-Darimi from Sa'dawayh, meaning Sa'id ibn Sulayman, from Abbad."
"1879","Another 2021 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd in al-Harbiyyah informed us: Hibatullah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us: Yazid narrated: Humayd informed us: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal has his left eye effaced, with a thick membrane over it, and written between his eyes is: disbeliever. And Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated it."
"1880","2022 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi in Herat informed us: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Ziyadi informed us: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Mazzaz informed us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Bishr narrated: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal is blind in the left eye, with a thick membrane over it; between his eyes is: disbeliever, or k f r. And Marwan narrated it from Humayd."
"1881","2023 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah and A'ishah bint Ma'mar ibn al-Fakhir, the wording is hers, informed us: Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi' informed us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani informed us: Marwan narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Dajjal is blind in the left eye, with a thick membrane over it; between his eyes is written: disbeliever: k f r. And Khalid narrated it from Humayd."
"1882","2024 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad informed us: Abu Ya'la informed us: Wahb ibn Baqiyyah narrated: Khalid ibn Abdullah informed us: from Humayd: from Anas, he said: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal is blind in the left eye, with written between his eyes: disbeliever. It is narrated in the Sahih from Anas's hadith mentioning the Dajjal, except that in this is mention of the left. And it has a witness in the Sahih from a hadith narrated by Ibn al-Yaman."
"1883","Another 2025 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubaydullah al-Sufi in Baghdad informed us: his maternal grandfather Isma'il ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Naysaburi informed them: Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad ibn Ghalib al-Attar informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated: Bundar Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated: Humayd narrated: from Anas, he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands when entering prayer, when bowing, when raising his head from bowing, and when prostrating."
"1884","2026 - The Imam Abu Bakr Abd al-Razzaq ibn Abd al-Qadir al-Jili the hafiz informed us: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Urmawi informed them: Ali ibn Ahmad al-Busri informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us: Abdullah, who is al-Baghawi, narrated: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated: from Humayd: from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to raise his hands in bowing and prostration. Ibn Majah brought it in his Sunan from Bundar similarly."
"1885","2027 - Abu Abdullah Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Isfahani there informed us: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Sa'id ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Buhayri informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil informed us: Abu Bakr Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Allawayh the judge narrated: Isma'il ibn Ahmad ibn Asad, governor of Khurasan, narrated: my father narrated: from Yazid ibn Harun: from Humayd al-Tawil: from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raising his hands when saying takbir, when bowing, and when raising his head from bowing. Abu al-Hasan al-Daraqutni said: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrates it from Humayd from Anas. Others narrate it from Humayd as mawquf, and that is the preserved version. I say: Yazid ibn Harun's narration strengthens Abd al-Wahhab's narration, and Allah knows best. I say: al-Daraqutni means only al-Thaqafi's exclusive mention of raising in prostration."
"1886","Another (no. 2028) - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim Sibtu Bahrawayh informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us: Abd al-Qahir ibn al-Sarri al-Sulami narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Seventy thousand of my ummah will enter Paradise. They said: Increase for us, O Messenger of Allah. He said: For every man, seventy thousand. They said: Increase for us - and he was on a sand dune - so he scooped with his hand. They said: Increase for us, O Messenger of Allah. He said: This, and he scooped with his hand. They said: O Prophet of Allah, may Allah keep away whoever enters the Fire after this."
"1887","No. 2029 - Aishah bint Mamar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us in Isfahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ayyub Sulayman ibn Isa ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us in al-Ahwaz: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib narrated to us: Abd al-Qahir ibn al-Sarri al-Sulami narrated to us, saying: I heard Humayd narrating from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my ummah will enter Paradise. They said: O Messenger of Allah, increase for us. He said: For every one, seventy thousand. They said: O Messenger of Allah, increase for us. He filled his two hands with sand and said: And the like of this. They said: O Messenger of Allah, increase for us. He filled his two hands and said: The like of this. They said: O Messenger of Allah, increase for us. Then Abu Bakr or Umar said: May Allah keep away whoever enters the Fire after this. Yahya ibn Main was asked about Abd al-Qahir and said: Salih (sound)."
"1888","Another (no. 2030) - al-Hafiz Abu Bakr Abd al-Razzaq ibn Abd al-Qadir al-Jili informed us in Baghdad, may Allah have mercy on him: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Saigh informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Naqqur informed us: Abu al-Qasim Isa ibn Ali ibn Isa ibn Dawud ibn al-Jarrah informed us: Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi narrated to us by dictation: Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, Yunus ibn Ubayd, and Humayd, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer [matn breaks off here in the source]."
"1889","No. 2031 - (Ha) Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi also informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, Yunus ibn Ubayd, and Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is one whom people trust; the Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe; the emigrant is one who abandons evil; and by the One in whose Hand is my soul, no servant enters Paradise whose neighbour is not safe from his harms. The words and his hand are not in al-Baghawis narration, and the rest of his narration is similar. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it in his book from Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Jabbar from Abu Nasr al-Tammar. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Musa ibn Ismail and a group of Hammads companions narrated it from Hammad, from Ali and Humayd, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and this is more likely. Abu al-Hasan al-Daraqutni said: It was narrated from al-Hasan as mursal, and that is more appropriate. It was said: Musa ibn Dawud corroborated Abu Nasr in raising it (as marfu), and Allah knows best."
"1890","Another (no. 2032) - Imam Abu Muhammad Abd al-Ghani ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Ali al-Maqdisi al-Hafiz informed us from his wording, saying: Imam al-Hafiz Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Silafah informed us, with my reading to him at the frontier of Alexandria: Abu al-Baqa al-Muammar ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Habbal informed us: Qadi Abu Muhammad Janah ibn Nudhayr ibn Salih al-Muharibi informed us: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Duhaym al-Shaybani informed us: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Musa al-Hunayni narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Maymun narrated to us: Aidh - he is Ibn Habib - narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw sputum in the qiblah and became angry until his face reddened; then a woman from the Ansar came, scraped it off, and put khaluq (perfume) in its place. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How good this is."
"1891","No. 2033 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us in Herat: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Sad Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri informed us: Abu Tahir ibn Khuzaymah - he is Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah - informed us: my grandfather - meaning Muhammad ibn Ishaq - informed us: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us: Aidh ibn Habib narrated to us: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw sputum in the qiblah of the mosque and his face reddened; then a woman from the Ansar came, scraped it off, and put khaluq in its place. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How good this is. Thus Ibn Khuzaymah brought it out in his Sahih. Al-Athram said: I heard Abu Abd Allah mention Aidh ibn Habib and praise him highly. Ibn Majah narrated it in his Sunan from Muhammad ibn Tarif from Aidh ibn Habib."
"1892","Another (no. 2034) - al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Ubayd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a Hibarah cloak; he said: I think he tied its two ends together."
"1893","Another (no. 2035) - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Ibn Abi Saminah al-Basri Abu Abd Allah narrated to us: Mutamir narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas: that the delegation of Thaqif said: O Messenger of Allah, our land is a cold land; what suffices us for ghusl from janabah? He said: As for me, I pour over my head three times. It has a corroboration in the Sahih from the hadith of Jubayr ibn Mutim."
"1894","Another (no. 2036) - Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Asbahani informed us by letter: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nuaym informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hadrami narrated to us: Jandal ibn Waliq ibn Hijris al-Taghlibi narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held a wedding feast for Umm Salamah with dates and clarified butter. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Humayd except Sharik."
"1895","Another (no. 2037) - Abu Muhammad Barghash ibn Abd Allah, freedman of Ibn Hamdi, informed us in Baghdad: Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Umar al-Urmawi informed them: Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn al-Mamun informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar al-Daraqutni informed us: Abu Amr Yusuf ibn Yaqub narrated to us: Abu Hani Ahmad ibn Bakkar narrated to us: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Stand and pray over your brother al-Najashi. One of them said: Do you command us to pray over an ilj (foreign unbeliever) from Abyssinia? So Allah revealed: And indeed among the People of the Book are those who believe in Allah and what was sent down to you, up to His saying: Indeed Allah is swift in account - that this verse was revealed concerning him. Al-Daraqutni said: Mutamir is alone in it, and we know no one who narrated it from him except Abu Hani Ahmad ibn Bakkar. Hammad narrated it from Thabit from Anas, and Abu Bakr narrated it from Humayd."
"1896","No. 2038 - Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Abi al-Raja informed us in Isfahan: Masud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb narrated to us: Yazid ibn Mihran al-Khabbaz narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When news of al-Najashis death came, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray over him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we pray over an Abyssinian servant? So Allah the Exalted revealed: And indeed among the People of the Book are those who believe in Allah and what was sent down to you - the verse."
"1897","No. 2039 - Muawiyah ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us of it by permission: Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nuaym informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Shuayb narrated to us with the same isnad, likewise, except he did not say the verse, stopping at: and what was sent down to you."
"1898","Another (no. 2040) - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath, grandson of Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Mandah, informed us in Isfahan: Mahmud ibn Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi informed them, he being present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Bayan narrated to us: Khalid narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, have mercy on me; O Allah, provide for me; O Allah, guide me."
"1899","Another (no. 2041) - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us, recited to him while we listened in Baghdad; it was said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey in Ramadan; a vessel was brought and he placed it on his hand, and when the people saw him they broke their fast."
"1900","No. 2042 - Abu al-Majd al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: Abu Abd Allah al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim Sibtu Bahrawayh informed us: Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abd al-Ala narrated to us: Mutamir narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey in Ramadan while fasting; a vessel of water was brought, he placed it on his hand and drank while the people looked on, so they drank. Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated it from Ahmad ibn Abd Allah from Abu Shihab from Humayd from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"1901","Another (no. 2043) - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim al-Khabbaz informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Harun al-Hammal narrated to us: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you has fever, let him sprinkle cold water over himself for three nights before dawn."
"1902","No. 2044 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, he being present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Qadi Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Abu Ghalib Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aishah narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us (Ha). No. 2045 - Abu al-Faraj Muhammad ibn Hibat Allah ibn Kamil al-Wakil also informed us in Baghdad: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Salman informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Shadhan informed us, saying: It was read to Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shafii: Abu Ghalib Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Nadr narrated to me: Ibn Aishah narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you has fever, let him sprinkle cold water over himself before dawn three times. Their wording is one, except that in al-Shafiis narration it is let him drip, perhaps a scribal error, and Allah knows best. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Musa ibn Ismail and others narrated it from Hammad ibn Salamah from Humayd from al-Hasan from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and that is more likely. Likewise it was narrated from Abu Zurah to this effect, and Allah knows best."
"1903","Another (no. 2046) - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali ibn al-Mattush al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas who said: There were words between Khalid ibn al-Walid and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and Khalid said to Abd al-Rahman: Do you exalt yourselves over us by days you preceded us with? It reached us that this was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Leave my companions for me; by the One in whose Hand is my soul, if you spent the like of Uhud, or the like of the mountains, in gold, you would not reach their deeds. Abu Hatim al-Razi was asked about it and said: It is only Humayd from al-Hasan from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), mursal. It has a corroboration in Muslim from the hadith of Abu Said al-Khudri: Do not revile my companions; by the One in whose Hand is my soul, if one of you spent the like of Uhud in gold, he would not reach the mudd of one of them nor half of it."
"1904","Another (no. 2047) - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan: Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, he being present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Qadi Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us: al-Fudayl ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intercession is only for the people of major sins of my ummah."
"1905","Another (no. 2048) - Shuhdah bint Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Ibari informed us by ijazah, and Imam Abu al-Faraj Abd al-Rahman ibn Najm ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Ansari informed us from her: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Baqillani informed them: al-Hasan - he is Ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shadhan - informed us: Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Khurasani al-Muaddal informed us: Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Salih al-Wazzan narrated to us: Arim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard yourselves from the Fire even with half a date."
"1906","No. 2049 - Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us in Baghdad: Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Tarrah informed them: Qadi Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Simnani informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Mahdi al-Anbari informed us: Abu Amr Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Harun al-Samarqandi narrated to us: Abu Umayyah - he is Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Muslim al-Tarsusi - narrated to us: Arim narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Guard yourselves from the Fire even with half a date. It has a corroboration in the Sahih from the hadith of Adi ibn Hatim."
"1907","Another (no. 2050) - Abu Amir Adnan ibn Nasr ibn Muhammad ibn Adnan and Abu Mansur Said ibn Umar ibn Nasr ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Said al-Bushanjiyan informed us in Bushanj: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Mansur ibn al-Husayn informed them: Abu al-Fath Nasr ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Hanafi informed us: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Dabbas informed us: Abu Ali Hamid ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Raffa informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz informed us: Amr ibn Awn narrated to us: Hushaym ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shook hands with a man, he did not withdraw his hand from his hand until the man was the one who withdrew his hand from his."
"1908","No. 2051 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, may Allah have mercy on him: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us: Abu Said Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi al-Basri informed us: Abu Labid Muhammad ibn Idris al-Sarakhsi informed us: Suwayd - he is Ibn Said - narrated to us: Mutamir narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) let down part of one of his wives garments, lengthening its train by a span or two spans, and said: Do not add beyond this."
"1909","Another (no. 2052) - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: Zahir ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them, read to him: Abu Sad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us: Abu Ahmad al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Tamimi narrated to us by dictation: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Thaqafi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Rafi ibn Abi Zayd Abu Abd Allah narrated to me: Abu Amir narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Himyar - correctly Humayd - from Anas who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, he liked to hear: O Najih, O Rashid."
"1910","No. 2053 - Abu Tahir Muawiyah ibn Ali ibn Muawiyah al-Sufi informed us by ijazah: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Sahl al-Balkhi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Rafi al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Amr al-Aqadi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked, when he went out for a need, to hear: O Najih, O Rashid. Al-Tirmidhi brought it out from Muhammad ibn Rafi with its isnad and said: A hasan sahih gharib hadith. Al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated it from Hammad ibn Salamah from Humayd from Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Muzani from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"1911","Another (no. 2054) - Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Ali ibn Saud ibn Thabit al-Ansari informed us in Egypt: Abu Jafar Yahya ibn al-Mushrif ibn Ali ibn al-Khidr al-Tammar informed them, saying: Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Said ibn Ahmad ibn Nafis al-Muqri informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Bundar ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Bundar, judge of Adana, informed us in Egypt: Abu Tahir al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Fil al-Asadi al-Balisi narrated to us verbally: Harun ibn Musa al-Farwi narrated to us: Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah has barred repentance from every innovator."
"1912","No. 2055 - al-Hafiz Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn Mahmud ibn al-Akhdar informed us in Baghdad: Said ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shadhan informed us: Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Adami informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Muslim narrated to us: Harun ibn Musa al-Farwi al-Madani narrated to us, saying: Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad narrated to me, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah has barred repentance from every innovator. Abu Bakr al-Shafii narrated it from Abu Mansur Sulayman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Nahrawani from Harun ibn Musa with its isnad."
"1913","Another (no. 2056) - Abu Muslim al-Muayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi informed us: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us: Marwan - he is Ibn Muawiyah - narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: Sad ibn Ubadah said: O Messenger of Allah, Umm Sad loved charity; will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf after her? He said: Yes, and water is incumbent upon you."
"1914","Another (no. 2057) - Abu al-Muzaffar Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Marwazi informed us in Marw: Abu Hafs Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Saffar informed us: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Suri al-Bayhaqi informed us, having come to us: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Qadi informed us: Muhammad ibn Yaqub ibn Yusuf al-Umawi narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Bakr al-Marwazi narrated to us: al-Sahmi - meaning Abd Allah - narrated to us: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three supplications are not rejected: the supplication of the father, the supplication of the fasting person, and the supplication of the traveller."
"1915","Another (no. 2058) - Abu al-Fath al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Jami ibn Hubayrah al-Qushayri informed us in Naysabur: Abu Sad Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Hasan al-Kirmani informed them: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Khalaf al-Shirazi narrated to us: al-Hakim Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Ali al-Hafiz narrated to me: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Dinawari informed us: Isa ibn Yunus al-Ramli narrated to us: Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us in al-Ramlah: Sufyan narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man supplicating, saying: O Allah, I ask You, as all praise is Yours, there is no god but You alone with no partner, the Bestower, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Possessor of majesty and honour. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has supplicated Allah by His greatest name, by which when He is called He answers. Al-Hakim said: We did not write it from the hadith of al-Thawri from Humayd except with this isnad. Hafs ibn Umar ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Talhah narrated it from Anas."
"1916","Another (no. 2059) - It was read to the eminent Shaykh Abu al-Fath Umar ibn Ali ibn Mahmud ibn Hammuyah, while we listened in Damascus: Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Saffar informed you: al-Janjarudhi - meaning Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman - informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl informed us: my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: Ali ibn Hujr informed us, from Ismail ibn Jafar, from Humayd, from Anas: that when the wind blew, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) it would be known in his face. Anas ibn Iyad narrated it from Humayd from Anas."
"1917","No. 2060 - Abu Tahir Rawh ibn Badr ibn Thabit al-Darani informed us by ijazah: Ghanim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Burji informed them: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Asbahani informed us: Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Sawwaf informed us: Abu Ali Ismail ibn Bakr al-Sukkari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Musayyibi narrated to us: Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, saying: When the wind blew, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) it would be known in his face. Al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated it from Humayd. It has a corroboration in the Sahih from the hadith of Aishah."
"1918","Another (no. 2061) - Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad informed us by ijazah: Abu Tahir Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran informed us: al-Hafiz Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mahdi al-Daraqutni narrated to us: Abu Muhammad ibn Said narrated to us by dictation: Bundar narrated to us: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas, that he would perform wudu and wipe the outer and inner parts of his ears, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do that. Ibn Said said: Al-Thaqafi says it thus, while others narrate it from Anas from Ibn Masud as his own action. I said: Al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated it from Hushaym from Humayd from Anas from Ibn Masud; likewise Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated it from Humayd."
"1919","No. 2062 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad: his maternal grandfather Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Naysaburi informed them: Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad ibn Ghalib al-Attar informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us: Yahya - he is Ibn Said - narrated to us: Bundar narrated to us: Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas: that he performed wudu and wiped the outer and inner parts of his ears, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do that."
"1920","Another (no. 2063) - al-Hafiz Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Silafi al-Asbahani informed us by ijazah: Abu al-Fawaris Umar ibn al-Mubarak al-Kharaqi informed them: Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran narrated to us by dictation: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shafii informed us: Isa ibn Abd Allah al-Tayalisi Zughath narrated to us: Yazid ibn Mihran narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah supports the religion with one who has no share in it. Abu Qilabah narrated it from Anas, and it has been written in his biography."
"1921","Another (no. 2064) - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, may Allah have mercy on him: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us: Ali ibn Harb narrated to us: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Persist with: O Possessor of majesty and honour. Al-Daraqutni said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated it from Hammad from Thabit and Humayd from Anas, but Abu Salamah al-Tabudhaki and Hajjaj ibn Minhal opposed him, narrating it from Hammad from Thabit and Humayd - among others - from al-Hasan al-Basri mursal from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and that is correct from Hammad. I said: It was narrated from Muammal from Hammad like Rawhs narration."
"1922","No. 2065 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us: Zahir ibn Tahir informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Jizi narrated to us: Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Persist with: O Possessor of majesty and honour. Ahmad ibn [...] narrated it from Muammal ibn Ismail."
"1923","Another (no. 2066) - al-Hafiz Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Silafi al-Asbahani informed us by ijazah: Abu Yasir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah al-Khayyat informed them: Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran informed us by dictation: Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Sawwaf informed us: Bishr ibn Musa informed us: Abu Hafs, meaning Amr ibn Ali al-Fallas, narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn al-Ala al-Kufi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever restrains his anger, Allah restrains His punishment from him; whoever guards his tongue, Allah veils his faults; and whoever excuses himself to Allah, Allah accepts his excuse. Al-Fadl: Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned him without recording any criticism. Abu Umayr ibn Anas narrated this from his father."
"1924","No. 2067 - Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sad al-Thaqafi informed us in Damascus: his maternal grandfather Abu al-Qasim Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl al-Hafiz informed them, read to him: Rizq Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Tamimi informed us in Baghdad: Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Hanbali informed us: Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad narrated to us: Bishr ibn Musa narrated to us: Amr ibn Ali al-Fallas narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn al-Ala al-Kufi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever restrains his anger, Allah restrains His punishment from him; whoever guards his tongue, Allah veils his faults; and whoever excuses himself to Allah, Allah accepts his excuse."
"1925","Another (no. 2068) - Hisham ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah and Aishah bint Mamar ibn al-Fakhir informed us, the wording being hers: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ishaq ibn Ahmad ibn Nafi informed us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Umar al-Adani informed us: Marwan narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that Jibril, peace be upon him, ordered him to recite the Quran in seven modes, each healing and sufficient. Yahya ibn Said narrated it from Humayd from Anas from Ubayy ibn Kab. Al-Daraqutni said: Marwan al-Fazari narrated it from Humayd from Anas; but the correct is Humayd from Anas from Ubayy ibn Kab."
"1926","Remainder of Humayd from Anas. No. 2069 - Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sad al-Thaqafi informed us in Damascus, read to him; it was said to him: Abu Tahir Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad al-Sabbagh informed you, you being present: Abu al-Hasan Ubayd Allah ibn al-Mutazz ibn Mansur narrated to us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah informed us: my grandfather - he is Muhammad ibn Ishaq - informed us: Ali ibn Hujr narrated to us: Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us. No. 2070 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib also informed us: Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Tarrad ibn Muhammad al-Radi informed them: Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Busri informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us: Abd Allah - he is Ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi - narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Muti narrated to me: Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us (Ha). No. 2071 - al-Mukhallis said: Abd Allah narrated to me, saying: Salih ibn Malik narrated to me: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah narrated to us (Ha). No. 2072 - He also said: Abd Allah narrated to us, saying: my grandfather narrated to me: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us - all of them - from Humayd, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and there I was with a palace of gold. I said: Whose palace is this? They said: For a young man of Quraysh. I thought I was he, so I said: And who is he? They said: Umar ibn al-Khattab. The wording is Ibn Mutis. Al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful narrated it, and Qatadah narrated it also."
"1927","No. 2073 - Abu al-Barakat Dawud ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baghdadi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Salamah informed them: Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Busri informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Abbas informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us: Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Zaidah: Humayd al-Tawil and al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and saw in it a palace of gold. I said: Whose palace is this? It was said: For a young man of Quraysh. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I thought I was he. He said: Umar. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for what I recall of your jealousy, O Abu Hafs, I would have entered it."
"1928","No. 2074 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan: Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, he being present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Abu Bakr narrated to us: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I entered Paradise and there I was with a palace of gold. I said: Whose is this? They said: For a young man of Quraysh. I thought I was he, so I said: Whose is it? They said: Umars. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Yahya ibn Said and Ibn Abi Adi from Humayd. Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated it from Anas also."
"1929","No. 2075 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad informed them, he being present: Abu Nuaym informed us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us: Ismail ibn Abd Allah informed us: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Abu Imran al-Jawni and Humayd informed us, from Anas."
"1930","No. 2076 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Bahz narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Abu Imran al-Jawni and Humayd informed us, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and saw a palace of gold. I said: Whose is this? They said: For a youth of Quraysh. I thought it was mine, and it was Umars. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing prevented me, O Abu Hafs, from entering it except what I know of your jealousy. He said: O Messenger of Allah, whomsoever I was jealous regarding, I would never be jealous regarding you. Bahzs wording. Musa said: I entered Paradise and there I was with a palace of gold. I said: Whose is this? It was said: For a youth of Quraysh. I thought I was he, so I said: Who is he? It was said: Umar ibn al-Khattab. Nothing prevented me, O Abu Hafs, from entering it except what I knew of your jealousy. He said: O Messenger of Allah, whomsoever I was jealous regarding, I would never be jealous regarding you. Abu Yala al-Mawsili narrated it from Abu Nasr al-Tammar from Hammad ibn Salamah similarly. Imam Ahmad also narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Bakr from Humayd."
"1931","No. 2077 - Abu al-Faraj Muhammad ibn Hibat Allah ibn Kamil ibn Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Wakil informed us in Baghdad: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Salman informed them: Abu al-Fadl Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shadhan informed us, saying: It was read to Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim al-Shafii: al-Qasim ibn Zakariyya narrated to us: Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and a palace was raised for me in it. I said: Whose is this? They said: For a man of Quraysh. I thought I was he. I said: Who is he? They said: Umar ibn al-Khattab. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing prevented me from entering it except your jealousy, O Abu Hafs. He said: Would I be jealous regarding you, O Messenger of Allah? Has Allah raised me except through you and guided me, and has Allah bestowed upon me except through you? He said: And he wept. Abu Bakr - meaning Ibn Ayyash - said: I said to Humayd: In sleep or waking? He said: No, rather waking. It was narrated in the Sahih from the hadith of Jabir ibn Abd Allah and Abu Hurayrah."
"1932","Another (no. 2078) - Shuhdah bint Ahmad ibn al-Faraj ibn Umar al-Ibari informed us by ijazah, and my cousin the jurist Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us from her: al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Busri informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shadhan informed us, saying: Abu Amr Uthman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Daqqaq informed us: Musa ibn Sahl al-Thaghri al-Washsha narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ulayyah informed us: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah admits the servant to Paradise for a morsel or a drink for which he praises Allah. It was narrated in the Sahih: Indeed Allah is pleased with the servant who eats a morsel or drinks a drink and praises Him for it."
"1933","Another (no. 2079) - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us in Baghdad: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Muammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas (Ha)."
"1934","No. 2080 - Imam Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Taymiyyah al-Khatib informed us in Harran: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Salman informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shadhan informed us, saying: It was read to Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shafii: Ibrahim ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Wakii narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muammal narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas: that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O our master and son of our master, O our best and son of our best. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O people, say your saying; let not Satan draw you on. I am Muhammad ibn Abd Allah. By Allah, I do not like you to raise me above what Allah has raised me. Their wording is one, and it preceded in Hammads narration from Thabit. Al-Nasai narrated it in Amal al-Yawm wa al-Laylah from Ibrahim ibn Yaqub from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Jabbar from Hammad ibn Salamah from Thabit and Humayd."
"1935","Another (no. 2081) - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan: Ismail ibn al-Fadl ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Akhshidh informed them: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Furak al-Qabbab informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us: Abd al-Samad ibn al-Numan narrated to us: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The wife of Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, I fear entering the Fire; I cannot endure. He said: Will you return the garden you took from him? She said: Yes. He sent to Thabit saying: Take the garden from her and release her. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated them. Abu Jafar is Isa ibn Mahan; Ali ibn al-Madini and Yahya ibn Main declared him trustworthy."
"1936","Another (no. 2082) - Abu al-Ala Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Asbahani informed us by ijazah: Abu Ali ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ubayd ibn Aqil al-Muqri narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three garments, one of them a shirt. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Humayd except Hammad, nor from Hammad except Muslim; Ibn Aqil is alone in it."
"1937","Another (no. 2083) - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us in Herat: Tamim ibn Abi Said al-Jurjani informed them, read to him: Ali ibn Muhammad al-Bahhathi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun informed us: Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti informed us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq, freedman of Thaqif, narrated to us: Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us: Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us: Marwan ibn Muawiyah al-Fazari narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will take this letter of mine to Caesar, and Paradise is his? A man of the people said: Even if I am not killed? He said: Even if you are not killed. The man set out with it and found Caesar coming to Bayt al-Maqdis; a carpet had been laid for him on which none but he walked. He threw the letter onto the carpet and stepped aside. When Caesar reached the letter he took it, then summoned the head of the Jathaliq (Catholicus) who read it to him. He said: My knowledge of this letter is but like yours. Caesar called out: Whoever owns the letter is safe. The man came forward and he said: When I arrive, come to me. When he arrived he came to him. Caesar ordered the doors of his palace locked, then ordered a crier who called: Caesar has followed Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and left Christianity. His troops came armed until they surrounded his palace. He said to the Messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): You see, I fear for my kingdom. Then he ordered his crier who called: Caesar is pleased with you; he only tested you to see your steadfastness upon your religion. Return. They left. Caesar wrote to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): I am a Muslim, and sent him dinars. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The enemy of Allah has lied; he is not a Muslim, he remains upon Christianity. And he distributed the dinars."
"1938","Another (no. 2084) - Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi informed us in Damascus: Ali ibn al-Muslim ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Tallab al-Khatib informed us: Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Jumay narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mansur - he is Abu Bakr al-Wasiti - narrated to us: Abu Umayyah Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Humayd al-Tawil informed us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The reciters (qurra) are the chiefs of the people of Paradise."
"1939","Another (no. 2085) - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us in Baghdad: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them: Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn al-Mamun informed us: Ali ibn Umar al-Harbi informed us: Ahmad ibn Kab narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ubadah narrated to us: Abu Sufyan al-Himyari narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us (Ha). No. 2086 - Aishah bint Mamar ibn al-Fakhir also informed us: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Ahmad ibn Kab ibn Amr ibn Uthman Abu Ubayd Allah al-Hannat al-Adl al-Wasiti narrated to us in Wasit: Muhammad ibn Ubadah narrated to us: Abu Sufyan al-Himyari narrated to us, from Hushaym, from Humayd, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Richness is not from abundance of goods; richness is only richness of the soul. The wording is one, except that in al-Harbis narration: but richness is richness of the soul. Abu Sufyan al-Himyari is Said ibn Yahya ibn Mahdi; Abu Zurah al-Razi said: He is saduq. It was narrated from Qatadah from Anas. The like is in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah."
"1940","No. 2087 - Abu Tahir Muawiyah ibn Ali ibn Muawiyah al-Sufi informed us by permission: Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nuaym al-Asbahani informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn - he is Ibn Ajlan - Abu Shaykh al-Asbahani al-Abhari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ubadah al-Wasiti narrated to us: Abu Sufyan al-Himyari narrated to us, from Hushaym, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Richness is not abundance of goods; richness is only richness of the soul. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Humayd except Hushaym, nor from Hushaym except Abu Sufyan; Muhammad ibn Ubadah is alone in it."
"1941","Another (no. 2088) - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Dharr al-Salihani informed them: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Askar narrated to us: Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Humayd al-Tawil, saying: I said to Anas: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Remorse is repentance? He said: Yes."
"1942","No. 2089 - My maternal uncle Imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi informed us, may Allah have mercy on him: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Shadhan informed us, saying: It was read to Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shafii: Abu Bakr Ismail ibn al-Fadl ibn Musa al-Balkhi narrated to us: Raja ibn Murajja al-Hafiz narrated to us: Amr ibn Tariq narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, saying: I said to Humayd al-Tawil: Did you hear from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Remorse is repentance? He said: Yes."
"1943","No. 2090 - Abu al-Maali Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Hibat Allah al-Bayyi informed us in Baghdad: Ahmad ibn al-Mubarak ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Qafarjal and Imam Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Harrani informed them: Hibat Allah ibn Abd al-Razzaq ibn Muhammad al-Ansari informed us: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran al-Muaddal informed us: Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Misri al-Waiz informed us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muawiyah al-Utbi narrated to us: Khalid ibn Abd al-Salam al-Sadafi narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remorse is repentance. Abd al-Rahman ibn Muawiyah said: Harmalah ibn Yahya dictated it to me from Khalid ibn Abd al-Salam, informing me he wrote it from him."
"1944","No. 2091 - Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah al-Saffar informed us in Naysabur: Wajih ibn Tahir informed them by ijazah: Abu Hamid al-Azhari informed us: Abu Muhammad al-Makhladi informed us: Musa - he is Ibn al-Abbas al-Juwayni - informed us: Abu Bakr al-Saghani narrated to us: Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Humayd, saying: I said to Anas: Did you hear the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Remorse is repentance? He said: Yes."
"1945","Another (no. 2092) - al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us in Baghdad: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Sulayman ibn Hayyan - he is Abu Khalid al-Ahmar - narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would turn to us with his face before takbir, saying: Stand close and straight, for I see you from behind my back."
"1946","No. 2093 - My maternal uncle Imam, scholar Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Maqdisi informed us, may Allah have mercy on him: Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad al-Daraqutni al-Hafiz informed us: al-Hasan ibn al-Khadir narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad Abu al-Ala narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sawwar narrated to us: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for prayer he said: Thus and thus, to his right and his left, then said: Straighten and align."
"1947","Another (no. 2094) - My maternal uncle Imam, devoted Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi informed us, may Allah have mercy on him: Abu al-Fath Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad informed us: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us: Muhammad ibn Umar ibn al-Qasim al-Narsi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shafii informed us: Muadh ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: al-Hajabi narrated to us: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would give one taslimah (salutation)."
"1948","No. 2095 - Muawiyah ibn Ali ibn Muawiyah al-Sufi informed us by ijazah: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad informed them: Abu Nuaym informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muadh - he is Ibn al-Muthanna - narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Hajabi narrated to us: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would give one taslimah. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Humayd except Abd al-Wahhab; al-Hajabi is alone in it. I said: Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated it from Humayd from Anas: that he would give one taslimah."
"1949","Another (no. 2096) - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed him, he being present: Abu Nuaym informed us: al-Tabarani narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Khulayd narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Abd Allah al-Tamimi narrated to us: Ismail ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ran his fingers through his beard. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Humayd except Ismail ibn Jafar; Ishaq ibn Abd Allah is alone in it."
"1950","Another (no. 2097) - Imam al-Hafiz Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Silafi informed us in his book: Abu Talib Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Basri informed them in Baghdad, saying: Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran narrated to us by dictation: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Nikhab al-Tibi informed us: Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn al-Kisai narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik concerning His saying: Whether We take you away, indeed We will take retribution from them, or We show you what We promised them, indeed We have power over them. He said: Allah honoured His Prophet by not showing him in his ummah what he dislikes; He raised him to Himself and retribution remained."
"1951","No. 2098 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, known as Qafak, informed us in Isfahan: Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Yunus informed them, read to him: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us: Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Busri al-Tamimi and Dalaj ibn Ahmad narrated to us, saying: Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Ishaq al-Tamimi narrated to us. No. 2099 - Ibn Mardawayh said: Ahmad ibn Ishaq ibn Nikhab al-Tibi narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn al-Hamadhani narrated to us, both saying: al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi al-Burani narrated to us: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, mentioning the like verbatim. Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated it from al-Fazari."
"1952","No. 2100 - Abu al-Qasim ibn Ahmad informed us: Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja informed them: Abu al-Husayn al-Dhakwani informed us: Ahmad ibn Musa al-Hafiz informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Musa ibn al-Walid narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us: Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas concerning Allahs saying: Whether We take you away, indeed We will take retribution from them. He said: Allah dislikes showing His Prophet, peace be upon him, in his ummah what he dislikes."
"1953","Another (no. 2101) - Abu Tahir Barakat ibn Ibrahim ibn Tahir al-Qurashi informed us: Abd al-Karim ibn Hamzah ibn al-Khadir al-Sulami informed them: Abd al-Aziz ibn Ahmad al-Kattani informed us: Tammam ibn Muhammad al-Razi informed us: Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Shuayb informed us: Abu Ali Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Udhri narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Masud ibn Amr al-Bakri narrated to us: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two rakahs of a married man are better than eighty-two rakahs of a bachelor. Al-Uqayli mentioned it from the narration of Mujashi ibn Amr from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam from his father from Anas similarly. This path is other than that, except that Masud ibn Amr al-Bakri: Ibn Abi Hatim did not mention him in his book."
"1954","Hamzah ibn Amr al-Dabbi Abu Amr al-Aidhi, from Anas ibn Malik; Muslim brought out a hadith from him. No. 2102 - Abu Ahmad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us in Baghdad: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Waki narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Hamzah - meaning al-Dabbi - saying: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (Ha). No. 2103 - Imam Ahmad said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Dabbi, from Anas who said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith by which Allah may benefit you? When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted at a stop, he would not depart until he prayed Zuhr. Muhammad ibn Amr said to Anas: O Abu Hamzah, even at midday? He said: Even at midday. The wording is one."
"1955","No. 2104 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, he being present: Abu Nuaym al-Asbahani informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Kathir, from Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj, from a man of Banu Dabbah, saying: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted at a stop, he would not move on until he prayed Zuhr."
"1956","No. 2105 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Waki narrated to us, from Shubah, from Hamzah al-Dabbi, saying: I heard Anas say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted at a stop, he would not depart until he prayed Zuhr. Muhammad ibn Amr said to him: Even at midday? He said: Even at midday."
"1957","No. 2106 - Uthman ibn Mahmud ibn Abi Bakr, known as Jubbuwayah, informed us in Isfahan: Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid informed us of his statement: Yahya - meaning Ibn Said - narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: Hamzah al-Aidhi narrated to me, saying: I heard Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted at a stop, he would not depart from it until he prayed Zuhr. A man said to him: Even at midday? He said: Even at midday."
"1958","Untuwanah al-Sadi narrated it from Hamzah. No. 2107 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us of it: Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, he being present: Abu Nuaym informed us: Sulayman al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Amr ibn Sukayn narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Sadusi narrated to us: Untuwanah al-Sadi narrated to us, from Hamzah Abu Amr, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted at a stop, he liked to pray Zuhr there before departing. He alighted at a stop, and when he wanted to depart he called the adhan then prayed, while the sun was almost at the middle of the sky. Abu Dawud brought it out in his Sunan from Musaddad. Al-Nasai also narrated it from Ubayd Allah ibn Said - both - from Yahya ibn Said from Shubah."
"1959","Another (no. 2108) - Imam Abu Musa Muhammad ibn Umar al-Hafiz al-Madini informed us by ijazah: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Abu Umar Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Mihrah narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani narrated to us: Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Mukharrimi narrated to us: Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Dabbi, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When we alighted at a stop, we would glorify (Allah) until we unloaded the mounts."
"1960","No. 2109 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, he being present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Kathir, from Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj, from a man of Banu Dabbah, saying: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) alighted at a stop, we would not cease glorifying until the mounts departed. Thus it occurs in this narration."
"1961","Hafsah bint Sirin, from Anas. No. 2110 - Uthman ibn Mahmud ibn Abi Bakr informed us in Isfahan: Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed them: Abu Amr Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abi Abd Allah ibn Mandah informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah informed us: al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us: Ali ibn Shuayb narrated to us: al-Waddah ibn Hassan narrated to us: Sallam Abu al-Ahwas narrated to us, from Asim ibn Sulayman, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would apply kohl an odd number of times. Ibn Sirin would apply kohl twice in each eye and divide one between them. Some stopped it (as mawquf)."
"1962","Khalaf Abu al-Rabi - imam of the mosque of Ibn Abi Arubah - from Anas. No. 2111 - Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them: Abu al-Hasan Ali - he is Ibn Ibrahim ibn Isa al-Muqri - informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Hamdan narrated to us by dictation: Abu Muslim Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Amr ibn Hamzah al-Qaysi Abu Usayd narrated to us: Khalaf Abu al-Rabi narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: that when Ramadan came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What are you facing and what faces you? - saying it three times - Umar ibn al-Khattab said: Has revelation descended or an enemy come? He said: No, but Allah forgives on the first night of Ramadan the people of this qiblah. He said: In the side of the people a man shook his head saying: Excellent, excellent. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As if your breast constricted at what you heard? He said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, but I remembered the hypocrites. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hypocrite is a disbeliever, and a disbeliever has nothing in this - or as the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said."
"1963","No. 2112 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us: al-Husayn al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim Sibtu Bahrawayh informed us: Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ararah narrated to us: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us with its isnad similarly. Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated it from Amr ibn Hamzah."
"1964","No. 2113 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Sufi informed us in Herat: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Fadl al-Ghazi al-Harras informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Khuzaymah informed us: my grandfather - meaning Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah - informed us: Muhammad ibn Rafi narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Amr ibn Hamzah al-Qaysi narrated to us: Khalaf Abu al-Rabi - imam of the mosque of Ibn Abi Arubah - narrated to us, saying: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What faces you and what do you face? - three times - Umar ibn al-Khattab said: O Messenger of Allah, has revelation descended? He said: No. He said: Has an enemy come? He said: No. He said: Then what? He said: Allah forgives on the first night of Ramadan every people of this qiblah, gesturing to it with his hand. A man before him shook his head saying: Excellent, excellent. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O so-and-so, did your breast constrict at it? He said: No, but I remembered the hypocrite. He said: The hypocrites are the disbelievers, and a disbeliever has nothing of that."
"1965","No. 2114 - Abu al-Mafakhir Uthman ibn Mahmud Jubbuwayah informed us in Isfahan: Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us: Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid informed us of his statement: al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Amr ibn Hamzah al-Qaysi narrated to me: Khalaf Abu al-Rabi - imam of the mosque of Said ibn Abi Arubah - narrated to us: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, mentioning the like up to his saying: Excellent, excellent. Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq said: If the report is sound, I know neither Khalaf Abu al-Rabi with uprightness nor disparagement, nor Amr ibn Hamzah al-Qaysi below him. This after mentioning it in his Sahih. I said: Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned them without recording any disparagement, saying: Khalaf ibn Mihran Abu al-Rabi - imam of the mosque of Ibn Abi Arubah - and Khalaf Abu al-Rabi from whom al-Qaysi narrated is another, other than him, though perhaps they are one, and Allah knows best. He said concerning Amr ibn Hamzah al-Qaysi: Muslim ibn Ibrahim and Muhammad ibn Said ibn al-Walid al-Khuzai narrated from him."
"1966","Another (no. 2115) - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us in Baghdad: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah said: I found in my fathers book in his handwriting: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Amr ibn Hamzah informed me: Khalaf Abu al-Rabi - imam of the mosque of Said ibn Abi Arubah - narrated to us: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This religion is strong, so enter deeply into it gently."
"1967","Rashid al-Himmani Abu Muhammad, from Anas; Abu Hatim said: He is salih al-hadith. No. 2116 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad, read to him he being present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn al-Qasim - he is Ibn Musawir - narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Umar al-Qawariri narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Habib ibn Nadabah narrated to us: Rashid Abu Muhammad al-Himmani narrated to us, saying: I saw Anas ibn Malik wearing a red fur, and he said: Our covers in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - we wore them and prayed in them. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Rashid except al-Hasan ibn Nadabah."
"1968","Another (no. 2117) - Abu Tahir Muawiyah ibn Ali ibn Muawiyah al-Sufi informed us by ijazah: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ibrahim ibn Hashim al-Baghawi narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us: Bakkar ibn Suqayr narrated to us: Rashid Abu Muhammad al-Himmani narrated to us, saying: I saw Anas ibn Malik at al-Zawiyah and said: Tell me how the wudu of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was, for it reached me you used to perform wudu for him. He said: Yes. He called for wudu water; a basin and a carved cup were brought, placed before him. He poured water over his hand, washing his palms thoroughly, then rinsed his mouth three times, inhaled three times, washed his face three times, then brought out his right hand and washed it three times, then washed the left three times, then wiped his head once, except he passed them over his ears wiping them, then inserted his palms into the water. Bakkar ibn Suqayr: Ali ibn al-Madini, Musa ibn Ismail, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak, al-Qawariri and others narrated from him."
"1969","Al-Rabi ibn Anas al-Khurasani al-Bakri al-Basri, from Anas. No. 2118 - Abu al-Daw Shihab ibn Mahmud ibn Abi al-Hasan al-Hatimi informed us, with my reading to him in Herat; I said to him: Abu al-Fath Abd al-Salam ibn Ahmad ibn Ismail ibn Muhammad Bakbarah informed you, read to him while you listened, and he acknowledged it: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Abi Masud al-Farisi informed us: Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Shurayh informed us: Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Said narrated to us: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us: Khalid ibn Yazid, dealer in pearls, narrated to us: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you come upon fertile land, give the animals their due; when you come upon barren land, move on. Keep to night travel, for the earth is folded at night. Do not camp on the road, for it is the shelter of every beast. Keep to gentleness, for Allah loves gentleness and aids through gentleness what He does not aid through harshness. Abu Dawud narrated it from Amr ibn Ali."
"1970","Another (no. 2119) - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, he being present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Ahmad ibn Bundar ibn Ishaq al-Shaar informed us: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us: Khalid ibn Yazid, dealer in pearls, narrated to us, from Abu Jafar al-Razi, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes out seeking knowledge is in the path of Allah until he returns."
"1971","No. 2120 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Nasr ibn Ali al-Jahdami narrated to us: Khalid ibn Yazid Abu Yazid narrated to us, from Abu Jafar al-Razi, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever goes out seeking knowledge is in the path of Allah until he returns. Al-Tirmidhi brought it out from Nasr ibn Ali, saying: A hasan gharib hadith. He said: Some narrated it without raising it."
"1972","No. 2121 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us, read to him in Isfahan; it was said to him: Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed you, read to him and he acknowledged it: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Hasan ibn Uthman al-Tustari narrated to us: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us: Khalid ibn Yazid al-Lului narrated to us, from Abu Jafar al-Razi, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever goes out seeking knowledge is in the path of Allah until he returns. Al-Tabarani said: It is not narrated from Anas except with this isnad; Abu Jafar and Khalid ibn Yazid are alone in it."
"1973","Another (no. 2122) - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid informed us, with my reading to him in Isfahan; I said to him: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed you, read to him while you listened, and he acknowledged it: Ibrahim ibn Mansur Sibtu Bahrawayh informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us: Abu Jafar narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves the world upon sincerity to Allah alone with no partner, leaves it while He is pleased with him. Anas said: It is the religion of Allah which the messengers brought before the clamour of narrations and divergence of desires; its confirmation is in the Book of Allah at the end of what was revealed: If they repent - their repentance being abandoning idols and their worship - and establish prayer and give zakah, then they are your brothers in religion. Ibn Majah narrated it from Nasr ibn Ali from Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri from Abu Jafar similarly."
"1974","No. 2123 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us in Herat: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Sad Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri informed us: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Sahl al-Masarjisi informed us: al-Muammal ibn al-Hasan ibn Isa Abu al-Wafa informed us: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Ramadi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us: Abu Jafar al-Razi informed us: al-Rabi ibn Anas narrated to us, saying: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves the world upon sincerity in Allah and His worship with no partner, establishing prayer and giving zakah, leaves it while Allah is pleased with him. Anas said: It is the religion of Allah which the messengers brought, conveying their Lords command. Allah says at the end of what was revealed: If they repent, establish prayer and give zakah, then they are your brothers in religion."
"1975","Another (no. 2124) - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, read to him in Baghdad: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us: Abu Jafar narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas and Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade plundering, and whoever plunders is not of us."
"1976","No. 2125 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us: Ali ibn al-Jad narrated to us, saying: Abu Jafar - meaning al-Razi - informed us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas and Humayd, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade plunder, saying: Whoever plunders is not of us."
"1977","No. 2126 - Abu al-Faraj Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari informed us in Baghdad: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Shafii informed us: Ishaq ibn al-Hasan ibn Maymun al-Harbi narrated to us: al-Ashyab - he is al-Hasan ibn Musa - narrated to us: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade plunder, saying: Whoever plunders is not of us."
"1978","Another (no. 2127) - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, read to him in Baghdad: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Abu Jafar, meaning al-Razi, narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued to supplicate qunut in Fajr until he left the world. Abu Yala narrated it from Zuhayr ibn Harb from Waki from Abu Jafar with its isnad: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut in Fajr only."
"1979","No. 2128 - al-Muayyad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Tusi informed us in Naysabur: Abu Muhammad Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Khuwari informed them, read to him: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Husayn al-Bayhaqi informed us: Abu Abd Allah al-Hafiz informed us: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Saffar informed us: Ahmad ibn Mihran al-Asbahani informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed qunut for a month supplicating against them, then left it; as for Subh, he continued to perform qunut until he left the world."
"1980","Another (no. 2129) - Abu al-Daw Shihab - also called Muhammad - ibn Mahmud al-Shadhbani informed us in Herat: Abu al-Fath Abd al-Salam ibn Ahmad ibn Ismail ibn Muhammad informed them, read to him: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Abi Masud al-Farisi informed us: Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Shurayh informed us; it was said to him: Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Said narrated to you: Muhammad ibn Awf narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Ala narrated to us: Abbad ibn Musa ibn Yusuf al-Kindi Abu Uthman narrated to us: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered a garden of the Ansar with Abu Bakr, Umar and men of the Ansar. In the garden were sheep which prostrated to him. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, we are more deserving of prostrating to you than these sheep. He said: It is not fitting for one to prostrate to another; had it been fitting for one to prostrate to another, I would have ordered the wife to prostrate to her husband."
"1981","No. 2130 - al-Sharif Abu al-Karam Abd al-Razzaq ibn Abd al-Sami ibn Muhammad al-Abbasi informed us in Baghdad: Hibat Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Hariri informed them: Ibrahim ibn Umar al-Barmaki informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim ibn Jafar ibn Bayan informed us: Jafar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Mustafad al-Firyabi narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Zubaydi al-Himsi narrated to us: Abbad ibn Yusuf al-Kindi Abu Uthman narrated to us, from Abu Jafar al-Razi, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered a garden of the Ansar with Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, among men of the Ansar. In the garden were sheep which prostrated to him. Abu Bakr, may Allah have mercy on him, said: O Messenger of Allah, we were more deserving of prostrating to you than these sheep. He said: It is not fitting in a nation for one to prostrate to another; had it been fitting for one to prostrate to another, I would have ordered the wife to prostrate to her husband."
"1982","Another (no. 2131) - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan: Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abd al-Kabir ibn Umar Abu Said al-Khattabi al-Tamimi al-Basri narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Abbad al-Kirmani narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us: al-Rabi ibn Anas narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out and saw in the mosque a man not completing his bowing or prostration. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of a man who does not complete bowing and prostration is not accepted. Al-Tabarani said: It is not narrated from Anas except with this isnad; Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr is alone in it."
"1983","Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Rayi, from Anas. No. 2132 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi al-Muaddib informed us in Isfahan: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad, known as Kulli, informed them: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Kharjani informed us: Qadi Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Assal informed us: Abu al-Fadl al-Abbas ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shahmah al-Hanbali narrated to us: Abu Hammam al-Walid ibn Shuja narrated to us: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Umar ibn Thabit al-Ansari narrated to me: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in his illness in which Allah took him, ascended the minbar and said: Bring the people to me. A gathering collected for him. He said: O people, Allah sent down His Book upon the tongue of His Prophet, permitting its lawful and forbidding its unlawful. What He permitted in His Book upon His Prophets tongue is lawful until the Day of Resurrection, and what He forbade in His Book upon His Prophets tongue is unlawful until the Day of Resurrection. O people, do not attach anything to me. Every Prophet has a legacy and dependants; my legacy and dependants are the Ansar, so preserve me concerning them."
"1984","No. 2133 - Abu al-Ala Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Asbahani informed us in his book: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khaythamah narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Shuja narrated to us: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Thabit al-Ansari narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Rijal, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us saying: Every Prophet has a legacy and dependants, and my legacy and dependants are the Ansar, so preserve me concerning them."
"1985","No. 2134 - Abu al-Fath Abd al-Wahhab ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Sabuni informed us by ijazah: Abu Nasr Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Sahl al-Sarraj al-Naysaburi informed them: Abu Sad al-Janjarudhi - he is Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman - informed us: al-Hakim Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Hafiz informed us: Abu al-Layth Nasr ibn al-Qasim al-Faraidi informed us in Baghdad: Abu Hammam - meaning al-Sakuni al-Walid ibn Shuja - informed us: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Thabit al-Ansari narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman, saying: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out in his illness in which Allah took him, sat upon the minbar and said: Bring the people to me. When they gathered he said: O people, Allah sent down His Book upon His Prophets tongue, permitting its lawful and forbidding its unlawful. What He permitted in His Book upon His Prophets tongue (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is lawful until the Day of Resurrection, and what He forbade in His Book upon His Prophets tongue is unlawful until the Day of Resurrection. O people, do not attach anything to me. Every Prophet has a legacy and dependants; my legacy is the Ansar, so preserve me concerning them. Abu Ahmad al-Hakim said: This is a gharib, elevated hadith from Rabiah from Anas; I know none who narrated it except Umar ibn Hafs from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd Allah ibn Harithah ibn al-Numan al-Ansari from him."
"1986","Zurarah ibn Rabiah ibn Zurarah al-Ataki Abu al-Hallal, from Anas. No. 2135 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur al-Khabbaz informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Wasiti narrated to us: Rawh narrated to us: Zurarah ibn Abi al-Hallal al-Ataki narrated to us, saying: I heard Anas say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever prays twelve rakahs in the day, Allah forbids his flesh to the Fire. He said: I have not left them since. Zurarah: Yahya ibn Main declared him trustworthy. Rawh - he is Ibn Ubadah - narrated more than one hadith from Zurarah. Muslim narrated from the hadith of Umm Habibah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever prays twelve rakahs in a day besides the obligatory, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise."
"1987","Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Anas. No. 2136 - It was read to Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed you, by ijazah if not hearing, while we listened in Isfahan, saying: Abu al-Fath Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah al-Asqalani informed us: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah - he is Ibn Salih - narrated to me: Isa ibn Asim narrated to me, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Anas who said: We prayed Subh with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). While he was in prayer he extended his hands then drew them back. When he finished prayer we said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you do in this prayer what you did not do before? He said: I saw Paradise, and in it a vine whose clusters hung low, its grapes like gourds. I wanted to take from it, but it was inspired to it: Withdraw, so it withdrew. Then the Fire was shown to me between me and you, until I saw my shadow and yours. I gestured to you to withdraw, but it was inspired to me: Affirm them, for you submitted and they submitted, you emigrated and they emigrated, you strove and they strove; I see no merit for me over you except prophethood. Something of this was narrated in the Sahih, with wording here not mentioned there. Abu Awanah al-Busti narrated it in his Sahih from Bahr ibn Nasr from Ibn Wahb. Abu Awanah said: It equals two thousand hadiths. It was reported from Amr ibn Abi Raja saying: This hadith drove me to Egypt."
"1988","Zayd ibn Wahb, from Anas. No. 2137 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Ali Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Fayruzan al-Jabban informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us: Ata ibn Jabalah narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of Madinahs roads when a dome was being built. He said: O Anas. I said: At your service. He said: Whose dome is this? I said: So-and-so the Ansaris. He said: O Anas, no building a servant builds but will be a burden upon him on the Day of Resurrection, except building a mosque or what is indispensable. Anas said: I went to the Ansari and told him the Prophets saying, so he ordered it demolished. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned along the road with me, saying: O Anas. I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Did I not see here a dome being built? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah; I went to its owner, told him the Prophets saying, and he ordered it demolished. He said: May Allah have mercy on him. Ata ibn Jabalah: al-Razi said he is layyin (weak). Abu Talhah al-Asadi narrated from Anas something like this."
"1989","Sad ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Anas. No. 2138 - It was read to Abu Talib al-Khadir ibn Hibat Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Tawus, while I listened more than once in Damascus: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn al-Sulami informed you, acknowledging it: Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn Abi Nasr informed us, saying: It was read to Qadi Abu Bakr Yusuf ibn al-Qasim ibn Yusuf ibn Faris al-Mayyanji, I being present listening; it was said to him: Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed you, read to him: al-Hasan ibn Ismail Abu Said narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from his father, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rulers are from Quraysh: when they judge they are just, and when mercy is sought from them they show mercy. Abu Dawud al-Sijistani said: I heard Abu Abd Allah - meaning Ahmad ibn Hanbal - asked about the hadith of Ibrahim ibn Sad from his father from Anas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The rulers are from Quraysh. He said: This is not in Ibrahims books; it should have no basis."
"1990","Sad al-Ansari, from Anas. No. 2139 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, he being present: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us: Ismail ibn Abd Allah Sammuyah narrated to us: Malik ibn Ismail al-Nahdi narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Wahb ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sad al-Ansari, from his father, that Anas ibn Malik went to al-Mihras, urinated standing, then performed wudu and wiped over his khuffs, then headed to the mosque or prayer. I said: You did something disliked: you urinated standing, then performed wudu, wiped over your khuffs, then headed to the mosque or prayer. He said: I served the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nine years, and he did that."
"1991","Said ibn Jubayr, from Anas. No. 2140 - Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Saffar informed us in Naysabur: Wajih ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Makhladi informed us: al-Muammal - he is Ibn al-Hasan ibn Isa - informed us: Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn Kaysan narrated to us: my father informed me, from Wahb ibn Manus, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Anas ibn Malik. Anas said: I never saw anyones prayer more like the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than this youth - meaning Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz. He said: We counted in his bowing ten tasbihs, and in his prostration ten tasbihs."
"1992","No. 2141 - Said ibn Rawh ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrawayh al-Salihani informed us in Isfahan: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan informed us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Mutawakkil al-Asqalani narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn Kaysan narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from Wahb ibn Manus, saying: I heard Said ibn Jubayr say: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: I never prayed behind an imam more like the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than this youth - meaning Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz."
"1993","No. 2142 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Sufi informed us in Herat: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn al-Fudayl al-Fudayli informed them: Faqih Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Malihi informed us: Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hafsawayh al-Tajir al-Sarakhsi informed us: Abu Yazid Hatim ibn Mahbub al-Shami informed us: Salamah ibn Shabib al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn Kaysan narrated to us, saying: my father narrated to me, from Wahb ibn Manus, from Said ibn Jubayr, saying: Anas ibn Malik said: I never saw anyones prayer more like the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than this youth - meaning Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz. Anas said: We counted in his bowing ten tasbihs, and in his prostration ten tasbihs. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad from Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn Kaysan similarly. Abu Dawud brought it out in Prayer from Ahmad ibn Salih. He and al-Nasai narrated it from Muhammad ibn Rafi - both - from Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim."
"1994","Said ibn Tahman al-Basri, from Anas. No. 2143 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, he being present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us: Ismail ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us: Ikrimah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Said ibn Tahman, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: There will be rulers over you who delay prayer from its times. They said: What shall we do? He said: Pray it at its time; if you catch it with them, make your prayer with them supererogatory. It has a corroboration in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Abu Dharr."
"1995","Said ibn Abi Said - his fathers name Kaysan al-Maqburi - from Anas ibn Malik. No. 2144 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan, may Allah have mercy on him: Zahir ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them: Said ibn Muhammad al-Buhayri informed us: Abu Amr ibn Hamdan informed us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan al-Nasawi informed us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Said, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I was beneath the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), its saliva dripping upon me. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah has given every rightful one his right. No bequest to an heir. The child is for the bed, and for the adulterer the stone. No man shall ally himself to other than his masters, nor be attributed to other than his father; whoever does so, upon him is Allahs curse continuously until the Day of Resurrection. No woman shall spend from her husbands house except with her husbands permission. A man said: Even food, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Is anything of our wealth better than food? A loaned item is to be returned, a granted milch-animal returned, a debt settled, and the guarantor liable."
"1996","No. 2145 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us, may Allah have mercy on him: Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, he being present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Said ibn Abi Said, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A loaned item is to be returned, and a granted milch-animal returned."
"1997","No. 2146 - With the same isnad he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No bequest to an heir. Umar ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid."
"1998","No. 2147 - Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Yusuf informed us by ijazah, and my maternal uncle Imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi, may Allah have mercy on him, informed us from him: Abu Tahir Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Yusuf informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar al-Daraqutni al-Hafiz informed us: Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us: Umar ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, saying: Said ibn Abi Said narrated to me, from Anas who said: I was beneath the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), its foam dripping upon me. I heard him say: Allah has given every rightful one his right, so no bequest to an heir. The child is for the bed, and for the adulterer the stone. No man shall claim another than his father, nor attach himself to other than his masters; whoever does so, upon him is Allahs curse continuously. No woman shall spend anything of her husbands wealth except with his permission. A man said: Not even food, O Messenger of Allah? He said: That is the best of our wealth. Then he said: A loaned item is to be returned, a debt settled, and the guarantor liable. Thus al-Daraqutni brought it out. Ibn Majah brought out part of it in his Sunan from Hisham ibn Ammar."
"1999","Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman, freedman of Ibn Abbas, from Anas. No. 2148 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us in Baghdad: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, from Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When Allah created the earth it swayed, so He created the mountains and cast them upon it and it settled. The angels marvelled at the creation of the mountains, saying: O Lord, is any of Your creation stronger than the mountains? He said: Yes, iron. They said: O Lord, is any of Your creation stronger than iron? He said: Yes, fire. They said: O Lord, is any of Your creation stronger than fire? He said: Yes, water. They said: O Lord, is any of Your creation stronger than water? He said: Yes, wind. They said: O Lord, is any of Your creation stronger than wind? He said: Yes, the son of Adam: he gives charity with his right hand hiding it from his left."
"2000","No. 2149 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, saying: Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman, freedman of Ibn Abbas, narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah created the earth it swayed, so He created the mountains and cast them upon it and it settled. The angels marvelled at the creation of the mountains, saying: O Lord, is any of Your creation stronger than the mountains? He said: Yes, iron. They said: O Lord, is any of Your creation stronger than iron? He said: Yes, fire. They said: O Lord, is any of Your creation stronger than fire? He said: Yes, water. They said: O Lord, is any of Your creation stronger than water? He said: Yes, wind. They said: O Lord, is any of Your creation stronger than wind? He said: Yes, man: he gives charity with his right hand hiding it from his left."
"2001","No. 2150 - Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sad al-Thaqafi informed us in Damascus: his grandfather al-Hafiz Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl informed them: Abu al-Husayn, grandson of Abu Bakr ibn Abi Ali, informed us: Abu Bakr ibn Mardawayh informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Awwam narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: al-Awwam ibn Hawshab informed us, from Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When Allah created the earth it swayed, so He created the mountains and cast upon it and it settled. The angels marvelled at the creation of the mountains, saying: O Lord, is any of Your creation stronger than the mountains? He said: Yes, iron - and he mentioned the rest similarly. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar from Yazid ibn Harun, saying: A gharib hadith, known as marfu only through this channel."
"2002","Sulayman ibn Tarkhan al-Taymi, from Anas. No. 2151 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan: Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, he being present: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us: Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us: Mutamir narrated to us, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Among the supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: O Living, O Sustainer."
"2003","No. 2152 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Sad Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi and Ustadh Abu Yala Ishaq ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sabuni informed us, saying: Abu Sad Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Musa al-Simsar informed us: Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Anas who said: Among the supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: O Living, O Sustainer. Al-Nasai narrated it in Amal al-Yawm wa al-Laylah from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala. Al-Daraqutni said: Mutamir is alone in it, and from him Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala."
"2004","Another (no. 2153) - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us in Isfahan: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, he being present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us: Ismail ibn Abd Allah informed us: Abu al-Numan Arim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us: al-Mutamir narrated to us, saying: I heard my father say: Anas narrated to us, mentioning a hadith. He said: I believe Anas narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from a belly that is not satisfied, I seek refuge in You from a prayer that does not benefit, I seek refuge in You from a supplication that is not heard, and I seek refuge in You from a heart that does not humble itself - or as he said."
"2005","No. 2154 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Hasan ibn Zafar ibn al-Shahd ibn Ali al-Hatimi informed us in Herat, known as Shihab: Abd al-Salam ibn Ahmad ibn Ismail al-Iskaf and Dhakwan ibn Sayyar informed them: Muhammad ibn Abi Masud al-Farisi informed us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Shurayh informed us: Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salih - he is Ibn al-Nattah - narrated to us: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: O Allah, I seek refuge from a soul that is not satisfied, I seek refuge in You from a prayer that does not benefit, I seek refuge in You from a supplication that is not heard, and I seek refuge in You from a heart that does not humble itself. It was narrated from Qatadah from Anas. Abu Dawud brought it out in his Sunan from Muhammad ibn al-Mutawakkil from al-Mutamir from his father: I believe Anas narrated to us similarly. Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban brought it out in his Sahih from Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Musa from Huraym ibn Abd al-Ala from Mutamir, saying: I heard my father say: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us."
"2006","Another (no. 2155) - Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Said ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Samad al-Muadhdhin informed us in Isfahan: Fatimah bint Muhammad ibn Abi Sad al-Baghdadi informed them: Said ibn Abi Said al-Sufi narrated to us: Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Makhlad ibn Shayban al-Makhladi al-Muaddal informed us: Makki ibn Abdan narrated to us: Ammar ibn Raja narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas who said: At his death, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enjoin: Prayer and what your right hands possess."
"2007","No. 2156 - Hibat Allah ibn Ali ibn Saud al-Busiri informed us in Cairo: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Umar al-Farra informed them: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Hasan informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ismail al-Darrab informed us: Ahmad ibn Marwan ibn Muhammad al-Maliki informed us: Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri narrated to us: Qabisah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined while his tongue could hardly pour forth, saying: Prayer and what your right hands possess."
"2008","No. 2157 - Imam Abu Bakr Abd al-Razzaq ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Abi Salih al-Jili informed us in Baghdad, may Allah have mercy on him: Abu al-Waqt Abd al-Awwal ibn Isa informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Dawudi informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Hammuyah informed us: Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym al-Shashi informed us: Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us: Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined while his tongue could hardly speak, saying: Prayer and what your right hands possess. It was narrated from Sulayman al-Taymi from Qatadah from Anas."
"2009","Another (no. 2158) - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn al-Fakhir informed us in Isfahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abd al-Wahid ibn Hamad ibn Muhammad informed us: Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq informed us: my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil informed us: Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he would recite in Fajr between sixty and a hundred verses. Al-Daraqutni said: Abu Yusuf Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Qadi is alone in it. It has a corroboration in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Barzah."
"2010","Another (no. 2159) - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, read to him: Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Abu Arubah - he is al-Husayn ibn Abi Mashar al-Harrani, and I wrote it only from him - informed us: Amr ibn Hisham narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Fazari, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas who said: The first to strike in the Trench was the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he took the pickaxe with both hands then said: In Allahs name, and with Him we began; had we worshipped other than Him we would be wretched. How excellent a Lord, how excellent a religion. Then he struck."
"2011","Another (no. 2160) - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Darir informed us: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim Sibtu Bahrawayh informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us: Mutamir narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he said: On the night I was taken, I saw people whose tongues were clipped with scissors of fire - or he said: of iron. I said: Who are these, O Jibril? He said: Preachers of your ummah. Al-Daraqutni said: Mutamir is alone in it from his father. Ali ibn Zayd narrated it from Anas. Isa ibn Yunus narrated it from al-Taymi."
"2012","No. 2161 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, he being present: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Ahmad ibn Khulayd - meaning al-Halabi - narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw on the night I was taken men whose tongues were cut with scissors of fire. I said: O Jibril, who are these? He said: These are preachers of your ummah, commanding what they do not do. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Sulayman al-Taymi except Isa ibn Yunus. I said: Mutamirs narration from his father shows he was not alone in it, and Isas narration shows Mutamir was not alone in it, and Allah knows best."
"2013","Another (no. 2162) - Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Baghdadi informed us in Egypt: Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Yusuf al-Urmawi informed them: Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Busri informed us, saying: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Abbas al-Mukhallis informed us: Yahya - he is Ibn Said - narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq al-Marwazi narrated to us, saying: I heard my father say: Abu Hamzah informed us, from Sulayman al-Amash, from Sulayman, from Anas who said: Zaynab, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), died; she was a sickly woman. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) followed her and her condition grieved us. When he entered the grave his face shone yellow, then his face brightened. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw from you something that grieved us; when you entered the grave your face shone yellow, then your face brightened - why? He said: I remembered my daughters weakness and the severity of the graves punishment; I was told it was lightened for her. She was squeezed a squeeze whose sound was heard between the horizons. Abu Hamzah is Muhammad ibn Maymun al-Sukkari."
"2014","Another (no. 2163) - Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us in Isfahan: Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Thaqafi informed us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridhah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abd Allah ibn Musa ibn Abi Uthman al-Anmati al-Baghdadi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Aruzzi narrated to us: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: May the fasting person kiss? He said: What harm in that? A sweet basil he smells. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Sulayman except his son Mutamir."
"2015","Another (no. 2164) - Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi informed us in Marw: Abu al-Fadl Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad al-Maghazili informed them, read to him: Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Rara al-Asbahani informed us, read to him: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us: Ismail ibn Ali ibn Ismail narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali ibn Khushrum narrated to us: Suwayd ibn Nasr narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He refused me that He make repentance for the killer of a believer."
"2016","Another (no. 2165) - Ibrahim ibn Uthman ibn Yusuf ibn Ayyub informed us, having come to us: Abu al-Muzaffar Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Salih al-Warraq informed them: al-Mubarak ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Ahmad al-Sayrafi informed us: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Shadhan informed us: Uthman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd Allah narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Haytham al-Baladi narrated to us: Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us: Ali ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I performed wudu for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a month before his death, and he wiped over his khuffs and turban."
"2017","No. 2166 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Said ibn Muhammad al-Buhayri informed us: Abu Amr ibn Hamdan informed us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan al-Nasawi informed us: Hisham ibn Khalid al-Azraq narrated to us: Baqiyyah narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Fudayl narrated to me, saying: I heard Sulayman al-Taymi say: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: I performed wudu for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a month before his death, and he wiped over the turban and the khuffs."
"2018","No. 2167 - Abu Tahir Muawiyah ibn Ali ibn Muawiyah al-Sufi informed us by ijazah: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nuaym al-Asbahani informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr Abu Zurah narrated to us: Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, saying: Ali ibn al-Fudayl ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Hanafi narrated to me, saying: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I performed wudu for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a month before his death, and he wiped over the khuffs and the turban. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Sulayman al-Taymi except Ali ibn al-Fudayl. It has a corroboration in the Sahih from the hadith of al-Mughirah ibn Shubah."
"2019","Another (no. 2168) - Shuhdah bint Ahmad al-Ibari informed us by ijazah, and my cousin Imam Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi informed us from her: Tarrad ibn Muhammad al-Zaynabi informed them: Abu al-Fath Hilal ibn Jafar ibn Sadan informed us: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Yahya ibn Ayyash al-Qattan informed us: Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated to us: Sahl ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us (Ha). No. 2169 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: Zahir ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them, read to him: Said ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Buhayri informed us: Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan informed us: al-Hasan ibn Sufyan informed us: Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us: Sahl ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the call to prayer is made, the doors of heaven are opened and supplication is answered. The wording is one."
"2020","No. 2170 - The learned Tammam bint al-Husayn ibn Qanan informed us in Baghdad: Hibat Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Hariri informed them: Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Fath informed us: Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ismail, known as Ibn Samun, informed us: Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Salm al-Katib informed us: Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated to us: Abu Ziyad Sahl ibn Ziyad narrated to us with its isnad likewise verbatim. Al-Daraqutni said: Usayd ibn Zayd narrated it from Ibn al-Mubarak from Sulayman al-Taymi from Qatadah from Anas, and a group mentioned they narrated it from al-Taymi from Qatadah from Anas as mawquf. He said: The correct is mawquf."
"2021","Sulayman ibn Kindir al-Ijli Abu Sadaqah, freedman of Anas, from Anas. No. 2171 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us: Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, he being present: Abu Nuaym informed us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us: Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, saying: Abu Sadaqah, freedman of Anas, informed me, saying: I asked Anas about the prayer times. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray Zuhr when the sun declined, Asr between these two prayers of yours, Maghrib when the sun set, Isha when the twilight disappeared, and Subh from dawn until sight spread."
"2022","No. 2172 - al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us: Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us: Ahmad informed us: Abd Allah narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Hajjaj narrated to us: Shubah narrated to me, from Abu Sadaqah, freedman of Anas - Shubah praising him highly - saying: I asked Anas about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray Zuhr when the sun declined, Asr between these two prayers of yours, Maghrib when the sun set, Isha when the twilight disappeared, and Subh when dawn rose until sight spread. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ismail ibn Masud and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala from Khalid. Al-Mahamili narrated it from Muhammad ibn Yazid from Yazid - both - from Shubah."
"2023","Sinan al-Ansari of Banu Amr ibn Awf, from Anas. No. 2173 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us in Isfahan: Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Mahmud and Abu al-Fath Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali informed us, saying: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah informed us in al-Ramlah: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Haywah narrated to us: that Sinan al-Ansari of Banu Amr ibn Awf informed him that he heard a man asking Anas ibn Malik: Did you hear anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about locusts? Anas said: I will not inform you anything from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but we went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Hunayn, and with Umar ibn al-Khattab was a sack of locusts he had packed; he would put his hand behind, take, eat and hand to us and we ate, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) watched. Then we returned to Madinah; we were brought it, bought from it abundantly, and dried it on rooftops."
"2024","No. 2174 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abi Hamid ibn Abi Masud Kuwwatah informed us in Isfahan: his grandfather Abu Masud Abd al-Jalil ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid and Masud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them: al-Rais al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl informed us: Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Ibrahim al-Naysaburi informed us: Muhammad ibn Yaqub al-Asamm narrated to us: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Hakam ibn Ayan al-Misri informed us in Egypt: Ibn Wahb informed us, saying: I heard Haywah ibn Shurayh say: I heard Sinan ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari say: I asked Anas ibn Malik about locusts. He said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Hunayn, and with Umar ibn al-Khattab was a basket of locusts he had packed behind him; he would take from it, hand to us and we ate, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) watched. Anas said: Then we returned to Madinah; we were brought it, bought and abundantly, dried it above the rooftops, and ate from it for a time."
"2025","Simak ibn Harb, from Anas ibn Malik. No. 2175 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Simak narrated to us, from Anas (Ha)."
"2026","No. 2176 - al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak ibn al-Mattush informed us in Baghdad: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us: Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us: Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Simak ibn Harb informed us, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Baraah with Abu Bakr to the people of Makkah. He said: Then he called him and sent Ali with it, saying: None conveys it except a man of my household. The wording is one. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abd al-Samad from Hammad. Al-Tirmidhi brought it out from Bundar from Affan and from Abd al-Samad from Hammad, saying: A hasan gharib hadith from Anas."
"2027","No. 2177 - Zaynab bint Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Shiri informed us in Naysabur: Ali ibn Jami ibn Ali ibn Abi Umar al-Katib al-Fami informed them, read to him: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Dashti informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmish al-Ziyadi informed us: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Bazzaz informed us: Abu Qilabah narrated to us: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Surah Baraah, entrusting it to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: None delivers on my behalf except me or a man of my household."
"2028","Sahl ibn Abi Umamah Asad ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf al-Ansari, from Anas. No. 2178 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Abi Tahir al-Thaqafi informed us: Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us: Ahmad ibn Isa narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Amya narrated to me: that Sahl ibn Abi Umamah narrated to him that he and his father entered upon Anas ibn Malik in Madinah in the time of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz when he was governor, while he prayed a light, swift prayer as the prayer of a traveller or near it. When he gave salam he said: May Allah have mercy on you, was this prayer obligatory or something voluntary? He said: It is obligatory; it is the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), erring in nothing except something I forgot. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Do not be hard upon yourselves, lest it be made hard upon you; a people were hard upon themselves and it was made hard upon them - those are their remnants in monasteries and cloisters: And monasticism they invented, We did not prescribe it for them. Then they came the next morning saying: We ride out to look and reflect. He said: Yes. They all rode; they came upon ruined dwellings whose people perished, extinct, fallen upon their roofs. They said: Do you know these dwellings? He said: How well I know them and their people. These are the people of the dwellings; transgression and envy destroyed them. Envy extinguishes the light of good deeds, transgression confirms or denies that. The eye commits adultery, the hand, foot, body and tongue, and the private part confirms or denies that. Abu Dawud brought it out in his Sunan from Ahmad ibn Salih from Ibn Wahb: his saying from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) up to: which We did not prescribe for them, only."
"2029","Sharik ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Namir, from Anas. No. 2179 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us: Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us: Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us: Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, saying: my father narrated to me, from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, from Anas who said: A man travelled with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon a camel, and cursed his camel. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O servant of Allah, do not travel with us upon a cursed camel."
"2030","No. 2180 - Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Asbahani informed us by permission: al-Hasan ibn Ahmad informed them: Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us: al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, saying: my father narrated to me, from Sharik ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Namir, from Anas ibn Malik who said: While a man was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon his camel, he cursed it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not travel with us upon a cursed camel. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Sharik ibn Abi Namir except Abu Uways; Ismail is alone in it."
"2031","2181 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad and Abu Dharr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim reported to us, both saying: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan reported to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Warah narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asbati narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir al-Kinani informed me, from Anas ibn Malik who said: While a man was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a camel, he cursed his camel, so he said: O servant of Allah, do not travel with us on a cursed camel. It has a corroborating witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Imran ibn Husayn and Abu Barzah."
"2032","Another: 2182 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us - there - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman reported to us, Abu Tahir - he is Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah - reported to us, my grandfather - he is the Imam Muhammad ibn Ishaq - reported to us, Ali ibn Hujr al-Sa'di narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar - meaning al-Ansari - narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abdullah - he is Ibn Abi Namir - from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out when the prayer had been established, and saw people hastily praying two rak'ahs, so he said: Two prayers together? And he forbade praying in the mosque when the prayer has been established. 2183 - And with the same chain my grandfather informed us, Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, Hafs ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to me, from Sharik, from Anas, with the like of it, up to his saying: Two prayers together? He did not add beyond this. And Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Khuzaymah said: Malik ibn Anas and Ismail ibn Ja'far reported this report, from Sharik ibn Abi Namir, from Abu Salamah, mursal. And Ibrahim ibn Tahman reported from Sharik both reports together, from Anas and from Abu Salamah - both. And Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated both to us, from Hafs ibn Abdullah, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, with both chains separately: the report of Anas separately, and the report of Abu Salamah separately. Thus Ibn Khuzaymah brought it in his Sahih. And Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim said - mentioning the hadith - he said: My father said: Malik, al-Thawri and al-Darawardi opposed them, from Sharik, from Abu Salamah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying, and this is more likely and more authentic. And al-Daraqutni mentioned similar to this statement, and Allah knows best what is correct."
"2033","Another: 2184 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim reported to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab reported to us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim reported to us, Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Duri narrated to us, Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mu'adhdhin narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abi Namir. 2185 - And Abu al-Ala Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed us - by ijazah - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated to us, Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Uthmani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Sa'd al-Mu'adhdhin narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is the mirror of the believer. Al-Tabarani said: None reported it from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir except Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Sa'd; Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Uthman was alone in it."
"2034","2186 - And Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us - there - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them - recited to him - Abu Ya'la Ishaq ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sabuni reported to us, Abu Muhammad al-Makhladi reported to us, Abu al-Fadl Ya'qub ibn Yusuf ibn Asim narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated to us - recited to him - Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Rabi'ah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Ra'y narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Mu'adhdhin narrated to us, from Sharik ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Namir, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is the mirror of the believer."
"2035","Shabib ibn Bishr al-Bajali, from Anas. 2187 - Abu al-Mafakhir Uthman ibn Mahmud ibn Abi Bakr, known as Habbawayh, informed us - in Isfahan - that Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Simsar reported to us, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khurshidh gave his statement, Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us, Ali ibn Ahmad al-Jawaribi narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Anas - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed ten regarding wine: its drinker, its server, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried - and what remained of it was cut off, from the book of Ibn Khurshidh. [FLAG: source text truncated in print]"
"2036","2188 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Ibn Ma'mar - he is Muhammad - narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed ten regarding wine: its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its seller, its buyer, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its drinker, its server, and the eater of its price. Al-Tirmidhi reported it from Abdullah ibn Munir. And Ibn Majah brought it from Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari - both - from Abu Asim al-Nabil. And al-Tirmidhi said: Strange from the hadith of Anas."
"2037","2189 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad al-Saydalani informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad informed them - while he was present - Abu Sa'id al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Hasnawayh reported to us - by ijazah - Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Isa al-Khashshab reported to us, the judge Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim reported to us, my father narrated to us, Shabib narrated to us, Anas narrated to us: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed ten regarding wine: its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its drinker, its server, the one served it, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, the buyer, the one for whom it is bought, and the eater of its price."
"2038","2190 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym reported to us, Ahmad ibn Bundar reported to us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim reported to us, my father narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed ten regarding wine: ... and the buyer, and the one for whom it is bought. [FLAG: source text truncated with ellipsis in print]"
"2039","Another: 2191 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - recited to him in Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Ibn Ma'mar - meaning Muhammad - narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the signs of the Hour: obscenity, foul speech, severing of kinship ties, distrusting the trustworthy, and trusting the treacherous."
"2040","Another: 2192 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Ibn Ma'mar - meaning Muhammad - narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes out for a time in the path of Allah will have for him the like of what touched him of dust as musk on the Day of Resurrection. Ibn Majah brought it from Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari, from Abu Asim."
"2041","Another: 2193 - Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Ali ibn Su'ud ibn Thabit al-Ansari informed us - in Fustat, Egypt - that Abu Ja'far Yahya ibn al-Musrif ibn Ali ibn al-Khidr al-Tammar informed them, Ahmad ibn Sa'id ibn Ahmad ibn Nafis al-Muqri reported to us, Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Bundar ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Bundar, judge of Adhana - in Egypt - reported to us, Abu Tahir al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Fil al-Balisi reported to us - in the city of Antioch - Nasr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Anas who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking a mount, but he did not find with him what to mount him on, so he directed him to another who mounted him, and he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, so he said: The one who guides to good is like its doer. Al-Tirmidhi brought it from Nasr ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kufi, and said: A strange hadith from this angle. It has a corroborating witness in Sahih Muslim from the hadith of Abu Mas'ud Uqbah ibn Amr."
"2042","Another: 2194 - Aishah bint Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us - in Isfahan - that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri reported to us, Abu Ali Hasan ibn Yunus narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar Rustah narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Shabib ibn Bishr al-Bajali narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not bestow a blessing upon a servant and he says: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, except that what he gave is better than what he took. Ibn Majah brought it from al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Khallal, from Abu Asim al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad al-Nabil. Abu Muslim al-Kashshi reported it from Abu Asim, but did not raise it."
"2043","2195 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym reported to us, Abu al-Qasim al-Tabarani reported to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Ibn Ma'mar - meaning Muhammad - narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not bestow a blessing upon a servant and he says: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, except that what he gave to Allah is better than what he took."
"2044","2196 - And Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi al-Fath ibn Makki al-Nahrawani informed us - in Baghdad - that Abu al-Hasan Sa'd al-Khayr ibn Muhammad ibn Sahl al-Ansari informed them, Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad al-Duni reported to us, Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sunni reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Rijal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not bestow a blessing upon a servant regarding family, wealth and children and he says: Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, except that he has given better than what he took."
"2045","Another: 2197 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - in Isfahan - that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them - while he was present - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan reported to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab reported to us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim reported to us, my father narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shabib narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant does not find the sweetness of faith until he knows that what befell him was never going to miss him, and what missed him was never going to befall him."
"2046","Another: 2198 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur al-Khabbaz reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna reported to us, Amr ibn al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shabib ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two eyes will never be touched by the Fire: an eye that spent the night guarding the Muslims in the path of Allah, and an eye that wept out of fear of Allah, mighty and majestic."
"2047","Another: 2199 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim reported to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab reported to us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim reported to us, my father Amr ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Shabib ibn Bishr reported to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of every matter that requires an apology."
"2048","Another: 2200 - Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sa'd al-Thaqafi informed us - in Damascus - that his grandfather the hafiz Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl informed them - recited to him - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Simsar reported to us, Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Milah narrated to us, Abu Amr ibn Hakim narrated to us, Abu Umayyah narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Anas ibn Malik - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two voices are cursed: the sound of a flute at a blessing, and the sound of wailing at a calamity."
"2049","2201 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Sa'id al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Hasnawayh reported to us - by ijazah - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Isa al-Khashshab reported to us, the judge Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shabib narrated to us, Anas narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two voices are cursed in this world and the Hereafter: the sound of a flute at a blessing, and the sound of cursing at a calamity - meaning by cursing: woe to her."
"2050","Another: 2202 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us that Abu al-Fath Ismail ibn al-Fadl ibn Ahmad ibn al-Akhshidh informed them - while he was present - Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim reported to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab reported to us, the judge Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim reported to us, my father Amr ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shabib ibn Bishr reported to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no divorce without marriage, and no freeing without ownership."
"2051","Another: 2203 - Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Sa'id ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Samad al-Kharaqi informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abi Nasr ibn Abi al-Qasim - known as Muhajir - informed them - recited to him - Abu al-Fadl al-Mutahhar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Buzani reported to us, Abu Umar Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab al-Sulami reported to us, Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Yazid al-Zuhri reported to us, my uncle Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar Rustah narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, Shabib ibn Bishr al-Bajali narrated to us, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cursed, cursed is he who claims lineage to other than his father; cursed, cursed is he who attaches himself to other than his patrons."
"2052","Another: 2204 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Ibn Ma'mar - he is Muhammad - narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Shabib ibn Bishr, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah - whether it falls short or reaches - will have the like of the reward of four persons from the children of Ismail whom he freed."
"2053","2205 - And Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad informed us - in Isfahan - that Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Dharr al-Salihani informed them, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim reported to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abd al-Rahim reported to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Hayyan reported to us, Ibn Abi Asim - he is Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Dahhak - reported to us, my father narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Shabib narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik - may Allah be pleased with him - say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah - whether it falls short or reaches - will have the reward of four persons from the children of Ismail, were he to free them."
"2054","Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas. 2206 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Tamimi informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Husayn ibn Yunus informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Dhakwani reported to us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz reported to us, Abu Amr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us (h). 2207 - And Aishah bint Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us - in Isfahan - that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja informed them, Abu al-Fath Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri reported to us, Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Askari al-Faqih narrated to us - in Tarsus - Humayd ibn al-Asbagh narrated to us, both saying: Adam narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse: A good word like a good tree. He said: It is the palm tree. And he recited: And an evil word like an evil tree. He said: It is the colocynth. The wording is one. Al-Tirmidhi reported it from Abd ibn Humayd, from Abu al-Walid, from Hammad, with its chain, similar. And from Ahmad ibn Abdah, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Shu'ayb, and he did not raise it."
"2055","2208 - Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi al-Mu'addib informed us that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani reported to us, Ahmad ibn Musa al-Hafiz reported to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ghalib ibn Harb narrated to us, Ali ibn Uthman al-Lahiqi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, and Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a basket of unripe dates, and he said: The example of a good word. And Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili reported it from Ghassan, from Hammad, raised."
"2056","Another: 2209 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi reported to us, Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan reported to us, Abdan al-Jawaliqi narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Qahtabah narrated to us, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good comportment is one part of seventy-five parts of prophethood."
"2057","Another: 2210 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim al-Khabbaz reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili reported to us, Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna reported to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Ta'i Abu Malik narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most complete of people in faith are the best of them in character, and good character reaches the rank of fasting and prayer."
"2058","Another: 2211 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us - there - that Tamim ibn Abi Sa'id ibn Abi al-Abbas informed them, Abu Amir al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Nasawi reported to us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri reported to us, Abu Arubah al-Husayn ibn Abi Ma'shar al-Harrani reported to us, Abd al-Quddus narrated to us, my uncle Salih ibn Abd al-Kabir narrated to us, my uncle Abd al-Salam ibn Shu'ayb narrated to me, from his father. 2212 - And Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi informed us - in Damascus - that Abu al-Husayn Ali ibn al-Muslim ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Tallab al-Khatib reported to us, Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Jumay' reported to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad narrated to us - in Sidon - meaning his father - Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Ubulli narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to me, my uncle Salih ibn Abd al-Kabir narrated to me, my uncle Abd al-Salam narrated to me, from his father, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Azd are the Azd of Allah; people want to lower them, but Allah refuses except to raise them, and there will come upon people a time when a man will say: Would that my father were Azdi, and would that my mother were Azdiyyah. Their wording is one, except that Abu Arubah said in a narration: Would that my mother were Azdiyyah. Their wording is one, except that Abu Arubah said in a narration: Would that my mother - without waw - and added at its beginning: Regarding the Azd. Al-Tirmidhi brought it from Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Kabir ibn Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from his uncle Salih ibn Abd al-Kabir, from his uncle Abd al-Salam ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Azd are the Azd of Allah on earth. And he said: A strange hadith, we know it only from this angle, and it has been reported from Anas halted, and it is with us more authentic."
"2059","Another: 2213 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Batirqani reported to us - by ijazah - Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Sindi ibn Ali narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Kabir ibn Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, my uncle Salih ibn Abd al-Kabir ibn Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Shu'ayb narrated to me, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a bowl or cup containing milk and honey, and he said: Two condiments in one vessel? I will not eat it, nor will I forbid it. Al-Bukhari was asked about it and rejected it."
"2060","Another: 2214 - Abu Tahir Mu'awiyah ibn Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us - by ijazah - that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, Abu Nu'aym reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ahmad ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Allaf narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab narrated to us, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Congregational prayer exceeds the prayer of the individual by twenty-five. Al-Tabarani said: None reported this hadith from Shu'ayb except his son Abd al-Salam. Al-Daraqutni said: There is disagreement from him: Salih ibn Abd al-Kabir ibn Shu'ayb reported it from his uncle Abd al-Salam, from his father Shu'ayb, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Attab al-Dallal reported it from Abd al-Salam ibn Shu'ayb, halted, and this is more likely correct. I say: This narration of ours is other than the narration of Salih, and it is raised. It has a corroborating witness in the Sahih."
"2061","Shubayl ibn Azrah al-Duba'i al-Basri, from Anas. 2215 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Asbahani informed us - there - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur al-Khabbaz reported to us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim reported to us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili reported to us, Ishaq ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Shubayl ibn Azrah narrated to us, he said: I and Qatadah entered upon Anas, and Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the righteous companion is like the perfume seller: if you do not get something from him, you will get his scent; and the example of the evil companion is like the blacksmith: if you do not get something from him, you will get his smoke. Abu Dawud brought it from Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar, from Sa'id ibn Amir, from Shubayl."
"2062","2216 - Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed us - by ijazah - that Abu Ghalib Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal informed them, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ghalib al-Barqani reported to us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn al-Haytham al-Anbari reported to us, Ibn Abi al-Awwam - meaning Muhammad - narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Amir narrated to us, Shubayl ibn Azrah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the righteous companion is like the perfume seller: if you do not get his perfume - or he said: he does not give you his perfume - you get his scent; and the example of the evil companion is like the blacksmith: if he does not burn your garment, his scent reaches you."
"2063","2217 - And Abu al-Qasim Mahmud ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud al-Haddad informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baghban informed them, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Tayyan reported to us, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khurshidh gave his statement, Abu al-Qasim Abdullah ibn Muhammad - known as Hamid Ra's, in Baghdad - narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ahmad al-Bukhari narrated to us - in Bukhara - from Sa'id ibn Amir who said: My maternal uncle carried me on his shoulder, and I heard Shubayl narrating from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The example of the righteous companion is like the perfume seller: if his perfume does not reach you, his scent reaches you; and the example of the evil companion is like the blacksmith: if he does not burn your garment, his scent reaches you. And it has been reported in the two Sahihs from the narration of Abu Musa al-Ash'ari."
"2064","Shaybah ibn Musawir - Makki - from Anas. 2218 - The free woman Zaynab bint Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad informed us - in Nishapur - that Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Jami' ibn Ali al-Qadi informed them - recited to him - Abu Sahl Abd al-Malik ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Dashti reported to us, the teacher Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmish al-Ziyadi narrated to us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan reported to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Umar ibn Abdullah ibn Razin narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from Shaybah ibn Musawir, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a grave, and his grey mule shied, and the people were seized, so he said: Leave her, for the occupant of the grave is being punished, for he does not guard himself from urine."
"2065","Sadaqah ibn Isa, from Anas ibn Malik. 2219 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf informed us - in Baghdad - that Abu Muhammad al-Mubarak ibn Ahmad ibn Barakah al-Kindi informed them, Abu al-Husayn Asim ibn al-Hasan ibn Asim reported to us, Abu Umar Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Mahdi reported to us, Abu Amr Uthman ibn Ahmad ibn Abdullah, known as Ibn al-Sammak, narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Sallam al-Sawwaq narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: A man was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pray over him, and he said: Is there a debt upon him? They said: Yes. He said: If you guarantee his debt, I will pray over him. Sadaqah: I did not see him in the book of Ibn Abi Hatim. And al-Bukhari mentioned him in his Great History, saying: He heard Anas; Ubayd Allah ibn Musa reported from him, and he did not add beyond this."
"2066","Dahhak ibn Abdullah al-Qurashi, from Anas ibn Malik. 2220 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far reported to us, Ismail ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Sa'id ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, Amr narrated to us, from Bukayr, from al-Dahhak ibn Abdullah al-Qurashi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey pray the forenoon supererogatory prayer eight rak'ahs, and when he finished he said: I prayed a prayer of desire; I asked my Lord, mighty and majestic, three things, and He gave me two and withheld one from me: I asked my Lord not to destroy my nation by years of famine, and He did; I asked Him not to make an enemy prevail over them, and He did; and I asked Him not to divide them into sects - meaning: He did not do it."
"2067","2221 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim and Ahmad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi reported to us, both saying: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri reported to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah reported to us, Harmalah ibn Yahya al-Tujibi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb reported to us, Amr informed me, from Bukayr, from al-Dahhak ibn Abdullah al-Qurashi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey praying the forenoon supererogatory prayer eight rak'ahs, and when he finished he said: I prayed a prayer of desire and fear; I asked three, and He gave me two and withheld one from me: I asked Him not to afflict my nation with years of famine, and He did; I asked Him not to make their enemy prevail over them, and He did; and I asked Him not to divide them into sects, and He refused me. Imam Ahmad reported it in his Musnad from Harun ibn Ma'ruf, from Ibn Wahb, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, that al-Dahhak narrated to him from Anas ibn Malik that he said: I saw - similar, and in it: And I asked my Lord three. And Imam Abu Bakr ibn Khuzaymah brought it in his Sahih from Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb, from his uncle Abdullah; and from Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Barqi, from Ibn Abi Maryam, from Bakr ibn Mudar - both - from Amr ibn al-Harith, similar."
"2068","Talhah ibn Nafi' Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik. 2222 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna reported to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to often say: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. So they said: O Messenger of Allah, we believe in you and what you brought; do you fear for us? He said: Yes, hearts are between two fingers of the fingers of Allah; He turns them."
"2069","2223 - And al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us - in Baghdad - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to often say: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. He said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, we believe in you and what you brought; do you fear for us? He said: Yes, hearts are between two fingers of the fingers of Allah; He turns them, blessed and exalted."
"2070","2224 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them - while he was present - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan reported to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab reported to us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim reported to us, Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to often say: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. They said: O Messenger of Allah, we believe in you and what you brought, so what do you fear for us? He said: Yes, hearts are between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful; He turns them. And Fudayl ibn Iyad reported it from al-A'mash."
"2071","2225 - Abu Ali Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Khattab ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us - in al-Harbiyyah - that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them, Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muslimah reported to us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis reported to us, Yahya - he is Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Imran al-Abidi narrated to us - in Makkah - Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Sulayman - meaning al-A'mash - from Abu Sufyan, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. And it is correct: It was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, do you fear, though we believe in you and are certain of what you brought? He said: What do I know? The hearts of creatures are between two fingers of the fingers of Allah, mighty and majestic. And Ahmad ibn Yunus reported it from Abu Bakr, from al-A'mash. Al-Tirmidhi brought it from Hannad, from Abu Mu'awiyah, and said: A good hadith. He said: And thus more than one reported it from al-A'mash, and some of them reported it from him, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the hadith of Abu Sufyan from Anas is more authentic. And al-Daraqutni said: Abu Mu'awiyah al-Darir and Fudayl ibn Iyad reported it from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas, and Sulayman al-Taymi and Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash opposed them, reporting it from al-A'mash, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas. And this hadith was reported from Abu al-Ahwas, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan and Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas, indicating both statements are correct."
"2072","Another: 2226 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Gabriel came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day while he was sitting, grieved, stained with blood; some of the people of Makkah had struck him. He said: So he said to him: What is wrong with you? He said: So he said: These did to me and did. He said: So Gabriel, peace be upon him, said to him: Would you like me to show you a sign? He said: Yes. He said: So he looked at a tree from beyond the valley and said: Call that tree. So he called it, and it came walking until it stood before him. So he said: Command it to return to its place. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It suffices me."
"2073","2227 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili reported to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas who said: Gabriel came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day while he was sitting, grieved; the people of Makkah had struck him. So he said: What is wrong with you? So he said: These did to me and did. He said: Would you like me to show you a sign? He said: Yes. He said: So he looked at a tree from beyond the valley and said: Call that tree. So he called it, and it came walking until it stood before him. So he said to it: Return. So it returned until it went back to its place. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It suffices me, it suffices me. Ibn Majah reported it from Muhammad ibn Tarif, from Abu Mu'awiyah. And a group reported it from Abu Mu'awiyah, among them: Abu Khaythamah, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr and al-Hasan ibn Arafah."
"2074","Another: 2228 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad informed them - while he was present - Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ubayd ibn Ghannam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, is Hajj every year? He said: If I said yes, it would become obligatory, and if it became obligatory you would not uphold it, and if you did not uphold it you would be punished."
"2075","2229 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur Sibt Bahrawayh reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna reported to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us one day angry, and we thought Gabriel was with him, until he ascended the pulpit; I never saw a day with more weeping veiled ones. So he said: Ask me; by Allah, you will not ask me about anything except I will inform you of it. So a man stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is my father? He said: Your father is Hudhafah - for the one claimed for him. So a man stood to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, is Hajj upon us every year? So he said - meaning -: If I said yes, it would become obligatory, and if it became obligatory you would not uphold it, and if you did not uphold it you would be punished. Umar ibn al-Khattab said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet; do not disgrace us with our secrets, and pardon us, may Allah pardon you. He said: So it was lifted from him. Then he turned toward the wall and said: I never saw like today regarding good and evil; Paradise and Hell were shown to me behind this wall. As for the mention of Ibn Hudhafah and the saying of Umar, they have been mentioned in the Sahih; here only the mention of Hajj. Ibn Majah brought it from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr, mentioning Hajj only."
"2076","Another: 2230 - Abu Muhammad Sufyan ibn Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Wahhab ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Mandah informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Umar al-Baghban informed them, Abu Amr Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abi Abdullah ibn Mandah reported to us, my father reported to us, Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Umar - he is Ibn Hafs al-Tajir - narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim - he is Ibn Abdullah ibn Bukayr ibn Zayd al-Nahshali Abu Bakr, known as Shadhan al-Farisi - narrated to us, Sa'd ibn al-Salt narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had twenty young men of the Ansar who stayed with him for his needs; when he wanted something, he sent them in it."
"2077","Another: 2231 - Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf informed us in his book, and the Imam, my maternal uncle Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - reported it from him to us, that Abu Tahir Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Yusuf informed them, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abdullah ibn Bishran reported to us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mahdi al-Daraqutni al-Hafiz reported to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, Utbah ibn Abi Hakim informed me, from Talhah ibn Nafi' that he narrated to him, he said: Abu Ayyub, Jabir ibn Abdullah and Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari narrated to me from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding this verse: In it are men who love to purify themselves, and Allah loves those who purify themselves. So he said: O assembly of Ansar, Allah has praised you well regarding purification; what is this purification of yours? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we perform ablution for prayer and bathe from major impurity. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is there anything else with that? They said: No, except that when one of us comes out from relieving himself, he likes to cleanse with water. He said: It is that, so keep to it. Thus al-Daraqutni reported it in his book."
"2078","Another: 2232 - Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Abi Bakr ibn Ali al-Khurasani al-Dallal informed us - in Isfahan, may Allah have mercy on him, by my recitation to him - I said to him: Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Baghban informed you - and he acknowledged it - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abi Abdullah ibn Mandah reported to us, my father reported to us, Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Umar reported to us - he is Ibn Hafs al-Tajir - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us - he is al-Nahshali al-Farisi - Sa'd ibn al-Salt narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: A man of the Muslims was struck on the day of Uhud, and his mother came to him and said: O my son, may martyrdom be pleasant for you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what makes you know? Perhaps he used to speak of what did not concern him, and be miserly with what would not enrich him. Al-Daraqutni said: Sa'd ibn al-Salt reported it from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas, and Hafs ibn Ghiyath opposed him, reporting it from al-A'mash, from Anas, and the statement of Sa'd ibn al-Salt is more likely."
"2079","Another: 2233 - Abu al-Muzaffar Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Sam'ani informed us - in Marw - that Abu al-As'ad Hibat al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Hawazin informed them, my grandfather Abu al-Qasim al-Qushayri reported to us, Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Khaffaf reported to us, he said: Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Thaqafi reported to us, Dawud ibn Rushayd Abu al-Fadl narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Abi Hakim who said: Talhah ibn Nafi' narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik and Jabir ibn Abdullah say: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - I think he said: on a campaign - he said: Either the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered a cluster to be cut, or it was cut, its leaves dried, and in the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was a stick with which he struck, and its leaves scattered. He said: Do you know what is the example of the believer when he stands for his prayer? His sins are gathered and placed above his head; when he falls prostrating, they scatter from him right and left."
"2080","Another: 2234 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili reported to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Anas who said: They struck the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once until he fainted, so Abu Bakr - may Allah be pleased with him - stood and began calling: Woe to you, would you kill a man for saying: My Lord is Allah? So they said: Who is this? They said: Ibn Abi Quhafah the madman."
"2081","Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Mu'awiyah al-Jarmi Abu Qilabah, from Anas. 2235 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan, may Allah have mercy on him - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri reported to us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili reported to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until people boast over mosques."
"2082","2236 - And the Imam Abu al-Futuh As'ad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Ijli informed us - in Isfahan - that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah informed him, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Mu'adh ibn al-Muthanna ibn Mu'adh al-Anbari Abu al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, and Qatadah from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. [FLAG: matn text missing in source, breaks off after qala]"
"2083","2237 - And Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Sufi informed us - in Herat - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sa'd Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Muqri reported to us, Abu Tahir ibn Khuzaymah reported to us, my grandfather reported to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Khuza'i narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, and Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until people boast over mosques."
"2084","2238 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Sa'id ibn Muhammad al-Bujayri reported to us, Abu Amr ibn Hamdan reported to us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili reported to us, Abdullah ibn Mu'awiyah al-Jumahi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until people boast over mosques."
"2085","2239 - Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sa'd al-Thaqafi informed us - in Damascus - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far reported to us, Ahmad ibn Isam narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Amir narrated to us, Salih ibn Rustum narrated to us, he said: Abu Qilabah said: We went out early with Anas ibn Malik to al-Zawiyah, and we passed a mosque when the dawn prayer came, so he said: Would that we pray in this mosque. They said: Until we reach the other mosque. So he said: Which mosque, the other mosque? They said: A mosque newly built. So he mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come upon my nation a time in which they boast over mosques, but only few maintain them - or he said: they maintain them only little. Ibn Majah brought it from Abdullah al-Jumahi - and some scholars spoke about him. And Imam Ahmad reported it in his Musnad from Yunus, Abd al-Samad, Affan ibn Muslim and Hasan ibn Musa - all - from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah. And it was reported through Qatadah, from Anas. And Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah brought it in his Sahih by both paths - as we mentioned. And he also reported it from Muhammad ibn Rafi', from Mu'ammal ibn Ismail, from Hammad, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah. And Abu Dawud and al-Nasai brought it from the hadith of Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, similar."
"2086","Another: 2240 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Faris reported to us, Yunus ibn Habib reported to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most merciful of my nation to my nation is Abu Bakr, the strongest of them in the religion of Allah is Umar, the strongest - or most truthful - of them in modesty is Uthman - Abu Bishr doubted, meaning Yunus - the most knowledgeable of them of the lawful and unlawful is Mu'adh ibn Jabal, the most knowledgeable of them of what Allah revealed to me is Ubayy ibn Ka'b, the most knowledgeable of them of inheritance is Zayd ibn Thabit, and the trustee of this nation is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. Asim followed him, from Abu Qilabah."
"2087","2241 - And Abu Abdullah Ismail ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Qattan informed us - in Baghdad - that Abu Ghalib Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Banna informed them - recited to him - Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Muhtadi Billah reported to us, Abu Hafs Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Kattani narrated to us, Abu Bakr Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Abbas ibn Muhammad and Abu Umayyah narrated to us, they said: Qabisah ibn Uqbah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Khalid and Asim, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most merciful of my nation is Abu Bakr, the strongest in the religion of Allah, mighty and majestic, is Umar, the most truthful in modesty is Uthman, the most knowledgeable of inheritance is Zayd, the best reciter of them is Ubayy ibn Ka'b al-Ansari, the most knowledgeable of them of the lawful and unlawful is Mu'adh ibn Jabal, and every nation has a trustee, and the trustee of this nation is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah - may Allah have mercy on them all."
"2088","2242 - And Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us - there - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Nasr - he is Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali ibn Musa - reported to us, the noble Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Husayni narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Sharqi reported to us, Abdullah ibn Hashim al-Tusi narrated to us, Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most merciful of my nation to my nation is Abu Bakr, the strongest in the religion of Allah is Umar, the most truthful in modesty is Uthman, the most knowledgeable of them of the lawful and unlawful is Mu'adh ibn Jabal, the best reciter of them of the Book of Allah is Ubayy ibn Ka'b, the most knowledgeable of them of inheritance is Zayd ibn Thabit, and every nation has a trustee, and the trustee of this nation is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. Imam Ahmad reported it in his Musnad from Affan, from Wuhayb, from Khalid; and from Waki', from Sufyan, from Khalid. And al-Nasai reported it from Ahmad ibn Sulayman, from Affan, from Wuhayb, from Khalid; and from Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi, from Khalid. And Ibn Majah reported it from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Abd al-Wahhab, from Khalid; and from Ali ibn Muhammad, from Waki', from Sufyan. And Abu Hatim ibn Hibban brought it in his Sahih from Ahmad ibn Mukram al-Birti, from Ali ibn al-Madini, from Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi, from Khalid; and from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from a group, from al-Thaqafi. Reported in the Sahih from it only the merit of Abu Ubaydah."
"2089","Another: 2243 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Mus'ab reported to us, the judge Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Assal narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Khatib reported to us, Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Simak ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr were eating, this verse was revealed: So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it. So Abu Bakr raised his hand and said: O Messenger of Allah, will I indeed see what I did of an atom's weight of evil? So he said: O Abu Bakr, do you see what you dislike in this world as measures, and Allah stores measures of atoms of good until He fulfills them to you on the Day of Resurrection. Al-Bukhari reported something through Simak ibn Atiyyah, from Ayyub. Al-Tabarani said: None reported it from Ayyub except Simak, nor from Simak except al-Haytham; Ziyad ibn Yahya was alone in it. I say: It is not as al-Tabarani said."
"2090","2244 - Abu Hashim al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Jarbadhqani informed us - in Isfahan - that Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Umar informed them - while he was present - Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani reported to us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz reported to us, Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Muhammad ibn Rustum narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yusuf ibn al-Dahhak narrated to us. 2245 - Ibn Mardawayh said: And Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Hasan narrated to me, Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Musa narrated to us, both saying: Ziyad ibn Yahya Abu al-Khattab narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, Simak ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: While Abu Bakr was eating with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) food, this verse was revealed to him: So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it. He said: So Abu Bakr raised his hand. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is wrong with you? He said: O Messenger of Allah, will I indeed see what I did of an atom's weight of evil? He said: O Abu Bakr, do you see what you dislike in this world as measures of atoms of evil; stored for you are measures of atoms of good until He fulfills them to you on the Day of Resurrection. 2246 - And Ibn Mardawayh said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Junayd al-Naysaburi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Naysaburi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, like it exactly. 2247 - Al-Haytham said: And Sarrar ibn Mujashshir narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas, with the like of the hadith of Simak."
"2091","Another: 2248 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri reported to us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili reported to us, Makhlad ibn Abi Zumayl narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with his companions, and when he finished his prayer he turned to them with his face and said: Do you recite in your prayer behind the imam while the imam recites? So they were silent. So he said it three times. So a speaker said - or speakers said: We do. He said: Then do not do so; let one of you recite the Opening of the Book to himself."
"2092","2249 - And Zahir informed us - also - al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Malik reported to us, Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Abdullah reported to us, my father Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mahbub al-Marwazi reported to us, Muhammad ibn Isa al-Tarsusi narrated to us, Abu Tawbah al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' and Abu Ja'far al-Nufayli narrated to us, both saying: Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in one of the two evening prayers, and said: Do you recite behind me? They said: Yes. He said: Then do not do so except with the Mother of the Quran, for there is no prayer for one who does not recite it. Abu Hatim ibn Hibban reported it in his Sahih from Abu Ya'la, from Makhlad; and from Umar ibn Sa'id ibn Sinan, from Faraj ibn Rawahah, from Ubayd Allah al-Raqqi. And he said: Abu Qilabah heard this report from Muhammad ibn Abi Aishah, from one of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he heard it from Anas; both paths are preserved. And Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Ubayd Allah ibn Amr erred in it; the hadith is what Khalid al-Hadhdha reported from Abu Qilabah, from Muhammad ibn Abi Aishah, from a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah knows best what is correct. And al-Daraqutni said: The mursal is more authentic."
"2093","Another: 2250 - Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Marwazi informed us - there - that Abd al-Khaliq ibn Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami, Abd al-Rahman and Ahmad, sons of Yahya ibn Abdullah ibn al-Husayn al-Nasihi, informed them, Uthman ibn Muhammad al-Mahmi reported to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya reported to us, Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdus al-Taraifi narrated to us, Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Jahm al-Sadusi, muezzin of Arim, narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three - whoever has them in him is a hypocrite, even if he fasts, prays and claims to be Muslim: when he promises he breaks it, when he is entrusted he betrays, and when he speaks he lies. And Wuhayb halted it from Ayyub. And it has a corroborating witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah."
"2094","Another: 2251 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us - there - that Tamim ibn Abi Sa'id al-Jurjani informed them, Ali ibn Muhammad al-Bahhathi reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani reported to us, Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti reported to us, Ahmad ibn Isa al-Sukayni reported to us - in Wasit - Ishaq ibn Zurayq al-Ras'ani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Khalid al-San'ani narrated to us, Rabah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will indeed support this religion with people who have no share. Thus Ibn Hibban brought it in his book. And al-Nasai brought it from Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Askar, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Rabah. And it was reported from Humayd, from Anas, and it already came in his biography."
"2095","Another: 2252 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf informed us - in Baghdad - that the Imam Abu Sa'd Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Sa'd al-Baghdadi informed them - recited to him in Baghdad - Abu al-Muzaffar Mahmud ibn Ja'far al-Kawsaj reported to us, Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Sulayman al-Baghdadi reported to us, Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Ishaq al-Ansari narrated to us, Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Amir al-Bazzaz al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Affan ibn Muslim narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) slaughtered seven sacrificial camels with his hand, standing."
"2096","Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik. 2253 - It was recited to Shaykh Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamzah ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Shafi'i - while we listened - al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed you - by ijazah - and Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad al-Ghazzal informed you (h). 2254 - And the Imam, the Hafiz Abu Muhammad Abd al-Ghani ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Ali ibn Surur al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us that Abu al-Fath Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Salman informed them, he said: Hamad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Haddad reported to us, both saying: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq - he is al-Thaqafi - narrated to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Makhzumi al-Fitri narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Abu Talhah married Umm Sulaym, and the dowry between them was Islam; Umm Sulaym accepted Islam before Abu Talhah, so he proposed to her, and she said: I have accepted Islam; if you accept Islam, I will marry you. So he accepted Islam, and the dowry between them was Islam. Al-Nasai brought it from Qutaybah. And similar already came in the biography of Ja'far, from Thabit."
"2097","Another: 2255 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far reported to us, Ismail ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Umarah, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Three contain healing from every disease except death: senna and sannut. They said: This senna we know; what is sannut? He said: If Allah willed, He would have made it known to you. Muhammad said: And I forgot the third. Muhammad ibn Umarah ibn Amr ibn Hazm; Malik and others reported from him. Yahya ibn Ma'in declared him trustworthy."
"2098","Abdullah ibn Ma'qil, from Anas. 2256 - Abu Hamid Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Thabit ibn Zayd informed us - in Baghdad - that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Muhammad al-Ansari informed them, Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Muhtadi Billah reported to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Saydalani reported to us, it was said to him: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Naysaburi narrated to you, he said: Isa ibn Ibrahim and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, both saying: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to me, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim, from Ibn Ma'qil, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution while wearing a Qitri turban; he inserted his hand under the turban and wiped the front of his head, and did not undo the turban. Abu Dawud brought it from Ahmad ibn Salih, from Ibn Wahb, similar or the like. [FLAG: compiler heading names Abdullah ibn Ma'qil but takhrij notes say correct is Abu Ma'qil; long editorial note stripped per rules]"
"2099","Abdullah ibn Abi Utbah, freedman of Anas, from him. 2257 - Abu Tahir Mu'awiyah ibn Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us - by ijazah - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - recited to him - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ibrahim ibn Hashim - he is al-Baghawi - narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn Abi Utbah, freedman of Anas, from Anas who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked something, it was seen in his face. Al-Tabarani said: None reported it from Qatadah except Hisham; Mu'adh was alone in it."
"2100","Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Shihab al-Zuhri, from Anas. 2258 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd reported to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Muslim, nephew of Ibn Shihab, narrated to me, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about al-Kawthar, so he said: It is a river Allah gave me in Paradise; its soil is musk, its water whiter than milk and sweeter than honey; birds visit it whose necks are like the necks of camels. He said: And Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, they are soft. He said: Their eaters are softer than them. Thus Imam Ahmad brought it in the Musnad. And al-Tirmidhi reported it from Abd ibn Humayd, from al-Qa'nabi, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah, and said: A good hadith. And al-Zuhri reported it from his brother Abdullah."
"2101","2259 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu al-Wafa Mahmud ibn al-Hasan ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Abdullah ibn Mandah informed them - while he was present - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Abdullah ibn Mandah reported to us, Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Umar ibn Ishaq al-Hamadhani reported to us, he said: It was recited to Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Hafiz Ibn al-Sunni - in Dinawar - Abu Bakr ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, that his brother Abdullah ibn Muslim informed him, from Anas ibn Malik: that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: What is al-Kawthar? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A river Allah gave me in Paradise, whiter than milk and sweeter than honey; in it are birds whose necks are like the necks of camels. So Umar said: They are soft, O Messenger of Allah. So he said: Their eaters are softer than them."
"2102","Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Abdi, from Anas. 2260 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili reported to us, Sahl ibn Zanjalah al-Razi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abu Bakr and Umar are the masters of the elderly of Paradise among the early and the late."
"2103","Abdullah Abu Bakr al-Hanafi al-Basri, from Anas. 2261 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush informed us - in Baghdad - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Shumayt narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah al-Hanafi narrate that he heard Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Begging is not lawful except for three: one of crushing poverty, one of overwhelming debt, or one of painful blood-liability."
"2104","2262 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Hafiz reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far reported to us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Shumayt narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrate to my father and my uncle, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Begging is not lawful except for one of three: overwhelming debt, crushing poverty, or painful blood."
"2105","2263 - And Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us - recited to him in al-Harbiyyah - it was said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed you, al-Hasan ibn Ali reported to us, Abu Bakr al-Qati'i reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Akhdar ibn Ajlan who said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik - meaning - that a man of the Ansar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining of need. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you have nothing? So he brought him a coarse cloth and a cup. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will buy this? So a man said: I will take them for a dirham. He said: Who will add over a dirham? So the people were silent. So he said: Who will add over a dirham? So a man said: I will take them for two dirhams. So he said: They are yours. Then he said: Begging is not lawful except for one of three: one of painful blood, overwhelming debt, or crushing poverty."
"2106","2264 - And Abdullah said: My father narrated to us, Mu'tamir narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Akhdar ibn Ajlan, from Abu Bakr al-Hanafi, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sold a cup and a coarse cloth to whoever adds. In some copies: From Anas, from a man of the Ansar, and thus I saw it in the narration of Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Akhdar, from Abu Bakr al-Hanafi, from Anas, from a man of the Ansar, that he suffered hardship. Al-Nasai brought it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from al-Mu'tamir and Isa ibn Yunus, from al-Akhdar, like the hadith of Mu'tamir. And Abu Dawud brought it - at length - from al-Qa'nabi. And Ibn Majah reported it from Hisham ibn Ammar - both - from Isa ibn Yunus, from al-Akhdar ibn Ajlan, similar. And al-Tirmidhi reported - part of it like the narration of Mu'tamir - from Humayd ibn Mas'adah, from Ubayd Allah ibn Shumayt ibn Ajlan, and said: A good hadith."
"2107","2265 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal reported to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq reported to us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Ahmad ibn Mani' reported to us, Rawh narrated to us, Akhdar ibn Ajlan al-Tamimi narrated to us: that he heard an elder of Banu Hanifah called Abu Bakr narrate from Anas ibn Malik: that a man of the Ansar was struck with poverty, he and his household; he entered upon them and found them collapsed from exhaustion and hunger. So he said: What is wrong with you? They said: Hunger; rescue us with something. So the Ansari went until he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, I come to you from a household; I do not think I will return to them until they perish or some of them perish. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What destroys you? He said: Hunger. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you have nothing? He said: I have nothing. He said: Go and bring whatever you have. So the Ansari returned and found nothing but a coarse cloth and a cup, and brought them to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: This cloth and cup are all I had; as for the cloth, they spread part of it and wore part; as for the cup, they drank from it. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will buy from him this cloth and cup? So a man said: I will take them for a dirham. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will add over a dirham? Anas said: So the people were silent. So he said: Who will add over a dirham? So a man said: I will take them for two. So he said: They are yours, and gave them to him. So he said: Go, buy with one of them food and cast it to them, and buy with one of them an axe, then bring it to me. So he did that. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it in his hand and said: Do you have a handle to fix it? So he said: No, by Allah, I do not have it. So one of the people said: By my father and mother, I have a handle, perhaps it fits. So he said: Bring it if you wish. So he brought it. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the axe and fixed it in the handle, then handed it to the Ansari. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go with this axe, cut whatever thorns or firewood you find, then bundle your bundle, bring it to the market, and sell it for what Allah decrees for you; then do not come to me nor let me see you for fifteen nights. So the man each day went out early, gathered firewood, then brought his firewood to the market and sold it for two-thirds of a dirham, until fifteen nights passed over him, and he earned in them ten dirhams. Then he came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, Allah has placed blessing for me in what you commanded me; I earned in fifteen nights ten dirhams; I bought with five dirhams food for the dependents, and bought clothing for them with five dirhams. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is better for you than coming on the Day of Resurrection with spots of begging on your face. Begging is not proper except for three: one of painful blood, overwhelming debt, or crushing poverty."
"2108","2266 - And Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us - in al-Harim - that Abu al-Ghanaim Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muhtadi informed them - recited to him - Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn Umar al-Barmaki reported to us, Abu Muslim - he is Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Basri - reported to us, al-Ansari - meaning Muhammad ibn Abdullah - narrated to us, al-Akhdar ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out for a cloth and a cup to whoever adds; so a man gave a dirham, and another gave two dirhams, and he sold it."
"2109","Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas, from his grandfather. 2267 - Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us - in Isfahan - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Ismaili reported to us, among others, they said: Abu al-Husayn al-Khaffaf reported to us, Abu al-Abbas al-Sarraj reported to us, Abu Yahya informed me, Abu Zayd al-Harawi Sa'id ibn al-Rabi' reported to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas who said: I heard Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The donkey, the woman and the dog cut off prayer. Al-Daraqutni said: Abu Zayd was alone in raising it from Shu'bah; Ghundar, Abu al-Walid and Muhammad ibn Kathir halted it, and the halted is more authentic."
"2110","2268 - Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Dahbal ibn Ali ibn Karih al-Harimi informed us - there - that Abu Ghalib Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Banna informed them, Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Jawhari reported to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muzaffar ibn Musa Abu al-Husayn al-Hafiz al-Bazzaz reported to us, Abu al-Qasim al-Nu'man ibn Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Harun al-Baladi narrated to us, Abu Yusuf al-Qulusi narrated to us, Abu Zayd narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The dog, the woman and the donkey cut off prayer. And in Muslim from the hadith of Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayrah, the like."
"2111","Another: 2269 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us - there - that Tamim ibn Abi Sa'id al-Jurjani informed them, Ali ibn Muhammad al-Bahhathi reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani reported to us, Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban al-Busti reported to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Zuhayr reported to us in Tustar, Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us, Malik ibn Ismail narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Humayd who said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to me that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no omen, and the omen is upon whoever takes omens; and if there is in anything, it is in the house, the horse and the woman. Thus Ibn Hibban brought it; and in the two Sahihs from the hadith of Ibn Umar, similar."
"2112","Another: 2270 - Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us - in Baghdad - that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them, Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn al-Ma'mun reported to us, Ali ibn Umar al-Harbi reported to us, Abu al-Fadl Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Jarjarai narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sudran Abu Ja'far narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Salim narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that he (h). 2271 - And Mu'awiyah ibn Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us in his book that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Salim, companion of the tablets, narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: that he saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing a black turban. Al-Tabarani said: None reported it from Ubayd Allah except Anbasah; Ibn Sudran was alone in it. Muslim reported from the hadith of Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah wearing a black turban."
"2113","Ubayd Allah ibn Dihqan, from Anas. 2272 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Mada al-Missisi narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Tamim narrated to us, Asad ibn Ubaydah - meaning al-Bajali - narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dihqan, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man eating with his left and drinking with his left."
"2114","2273 - And al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us - in Baghdad - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Yazid ibn Harun and Rawh narrated to us, both saying: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us - Rawh said: From Abdullah ibn Dihqan, and Yazid said: From Ubayd Allah ibn Dihqan - from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man eating with his left or drinking with his left. Rawh said in his hadith: And drinking with his left. And Ahmad also reported it from Affan, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Dihqan, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man eating with his left. It has a corroborating witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abdullah ibn Umar. [FLAG: name varies Abdullah vs Ubayd Allah ibn Dihqan in source]"
"2115","Ubayd Allah ibn Rawahah, from Anas. 2274 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Aban ibn Khalid who said: Ubayd Allah ibn Rawahah narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik that he never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray al-Duha except when going out on a journey or returning from a journey. And Imam Ahmad also brought it from Ibrahim ibn Ishaq, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from Aban ibn Khalid."
"2116","2275 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, al-Adib al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik reported to us, Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Aban ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Rawahah, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not pray al-Duha except when returning from a journey or going out."
"2117","2276 - Abu Rashid Habib ibn Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Sufi informed us - by ijazah - that Ghanim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Burji informed them, Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hasan ibn al-Sawwaf reported to us, al-Hasan - he is Ibn Ali ibn al-Walid - narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Jamil narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, Aban ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: I heard Ibn Rawahah say: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me: that he never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray al-Duha at all except when going out on a journey or returning from a journey. And Abdan reported it from Aban ibn Khalid. And Muslim reported from the hadith of Abdullah ibn Shaqiq who said: I said to Aishah: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray al-Duha? She said: No, except when returning from his absence."
"2118","Abd al-Rahman ibn Hashim ibn Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas, from Anas. 2277 - The Imam Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Lanjani informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Abdullah al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas al-Rustumi informed them, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Tayyan reported to us, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khurshidh gave his statement, Abu Bakr Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Naysaburi reported to us, Yunus narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb reported to us, Ya'qub ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri narrated to me, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hashim ibn Utbah ibn Abi Waqqas, from Anas who said: When Gabriel brought al-Buraq to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It was as if it pricked its ears, so Gabriel said to it: Hush, O Buraq; by Allah, none like him ever rode you. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) traveled, and there was an old woman groaning beside the road. So he said: What is this, O Gabriel? He said: Travel, O Muhammad. He said: So he traveled as far as Allah willed him to travel. And dropped from our hearing: There was something calling him, set aside from the road: Come, O Muhammad. Gabriel said to him: Travel, O Muhammad. So he traveled as far as Allah willed him to travel. Up to here dropped. He said: Then a creature of the creatures met him and said: Peace upon you, O First; peace upon you, O Last; and peace upon you, O Gatherer. So Gabriel said to him: Return the greeting, O Muhammad. He said: So he returned the greeting. Then the second met him and said to him like the saying of the first. Then the third met him and said to him like the saying of the first two, until he reached Bayt al-Maqdis. Then water, wine and milk were presented to him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the milk. So Gabriel said to him: You hit the fitrah; had you drunk the water, you would have drowned and your nation would have drowned; had you drunk the wine, you would have strayed and your nation would have strayed. Then Adam and those below him of the prophets were raised for him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led them that night. Then Gabriel said to him: As for the old woman you saw groaning beside the road, nothing remains of this world except what remains of that old woman; as for the one you wanted to incline to, that is the enemy of Allah, Iblis, who wanted you to incline to him; as for those who greeted you, they are Ibrahim, Musa and Isa, peace be upon them."
"2119","Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm - also said Ibn al-Asamm - Abu Bakr, from Anas; Muslim reported for him one hadith on clothing from Anas from the narration of Abu Awanah from him. 2278 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili reported to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asamm who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar did not omit the takbir."
"2120","2279 - And Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm who said: I heard Anas say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman completed the takbir when they rose and when they lowered. And Yahya al-Qattan, Waki', Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abd al-Razzaq reported it from Sufyan, from Abd al-Rahman."
"2121","2280 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym reported to us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ishaq al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq reported to us, al-Thawri reported to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar and Uthman completed the takbir when they rose and when they lowered. And Abu Awanah reported it from Abd al-Rahman."
"2122","2281 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym al-Asbahani reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far reported to us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asamm who said: I heard Anas, and he was asked about the takbir in prayer when bowing and prostrating. So he said: He says takbir when he bows, when he rises, when he prostrates, and when he stands from the two rak'ahs. He said: From whom? He said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar. So Hakim said to him: And from Uthman? So he said: And Uthman - may Allah be pleased with them."
"2123","2282 - And Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us - there - that Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Fudayli informed them, Muhallim ibn Ismail ibn Mudar al-Dabbi reported to us, al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Sijzi reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj reported to us, Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Asamm who said: Anas ibn Malik was asked about the takbir in prayer. He said: He says takbir when he bows, when he prostrates, when he raises his head from prostration, and when he stands from the two rak'ahs. So Hakim said to him: From whom do you preserve this? He said: From the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar. Then he was silent. So Hakim said: And Uthman? He said: And Uthman. And Imam Ahmad reported it in his Musnad from Affan, from Abu Awanah, like the narration of Qutaybah, and in it: Anas was asked about the takbir in prayer while I listened. And Khalaf ibn Hisham reported it from Abu Awanah, similar. Al-Nasai brought it in his Sunan from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, similar."
"2124","Abd al-Rahman ibn Wardan al-Madini, from Anas. 2283 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us - in Baghdad - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Wardan - a Medinan - narrated to us, he said: We entered upon Anas ibn Malik with a group of the people of Madinah, and he said: Have you prayed? - meaning al-Asr - They said: Yes. We said: May Allah keep you right, when did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray this prayer? He said: He used to pray it while the sun was white and clear. Reported in the Sahih: Elevated, alive, from the hadith of Anas."
"2125","2284 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad reported to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq reported to us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Ahmad ibn Mani' reported to us, Marwan - he is Ibn Mu'awiyah - narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Wardan, Abu Bakr al-Ghifari, who said: They asked Anas ibn Malik - while we were here - at what hour did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray al-Asr? He said: He used to pray it while the sun was white and clear."
"2126","Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Anas. 2285 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informed them, al-Hasan ibn al-Mudhhib reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Safwan narrated to us, Rashid ibn Sa'd and Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr narrated to me, from Anas (h). [FLAG: matn missing in source, breaks off after chain]"
"2127","2286 - And Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sa'd al-Thaqafi informed us - in Damascus - that his grandfather Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Hafiz informed them, Ahmad ibn Mardawayh reported to us, Abu Sa'd ibn Hasnawayh narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far ibn Ma'bad narrated to us, Abu al-Husayn ibn al-Sunni narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Shu'ayb al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Safwan narrated to us, Rashid ibn Sa'd and Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When I was taken up, I passed by people with nails of copper scratching their faces and chests. So I said: Who are these, O Gabriel? He said: These are those who eat the flesh of people and attack their honors. Their wording is one. And Abu Dawud reported it from Muhammad ibn al-Musaffa, from Baqiyyah and Abu al-Mughirah, from Safwan, from Rashid and Abd al-Rahman. And he also reported it by this path, making it from Rashid, from Abd al-Rahman."
"2128","Abd al-Hamid ibn Muhammad al-Mi'wali al-Basri, from Anas. 2287 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad informed us - there - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far reported to us, Abdullah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Yahya ibn Hani, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Mahmud who said: I prayed with Anas ibn Malik on Friday, and we were pushed to the pillars, so we moved forward or back. So Anas said: We used to avoid this in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [FLAG: compiler heading names Abd al-Hamid ibn Muhammad but chain says Ibn Mahmud]"
"2129","2288 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq reported to us, from al-Thawri, from Yahya ibn Hani, Abd al-Hamid ibn Mahmud narrated to me, he said: I was with Anas ibn Malik, and we fell between the pillars, so we moved back. When we prayed, Anas said: We used to avoid this in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2130","2289 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Baqqal reported to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq reported to us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil reported to us, Ahmad ibn Mani' reported to us, Qabisah narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Hani, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Mahmud who said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Hani, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Mahmud who said: We prayed with Anas ibn Malik on Friday, and the people crowded him until he fell between the pillars; when he gave salam, he said: We used to avoid this in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu Dawud reported it from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Ibn Mahdi. And al-Tirmidhi reported it from Hannad, from Waki'. And al-Nasai reported it from Amr ibn Mansur, from Abu Nu'aym - all - from Sufyan. And al-Tirmidhi said: A good hadith."
"2131","Abd al-Hamid ibn Wasil Abu al-Wasil, from Anas. 2290 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ali al-Abbar narrated to us, Mu'allil ibn Nufayl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani and Khattab ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Abu al-Wasil Abd al-Hamid ibn Wasil, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Guardian of Islam and its people, make me firm in it until I meet You. Al-Tabarani said: It is not reported from Anas except by this chain. Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili reported it from Ismail ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid al-Qurashi, from Ashshab ibn Bashir, from Abd al-Hamid, from Anas. And Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Warah reported it from Yahya ibn Salih, from Sulayman ibn Ata, from Abu al-Wasil, from Anas."
"2132","Abu Imran Abd al-Malik ibn Habib al-Jawni, from Anas. 2291 - Abu Tahir Mu'awiyah ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us - in writing - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Ahmad - he is Ibn Zuhayr al-Tustari - narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad al-Qatawani narrated to us, Abd al-Salam ibn Hafs narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Friday was presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Gabriel came with something in his palm like a white mirror, in its middle like a black dot. So he said: What is this, O Gabriel? He said: This is Friday; your Lord presents it to you so it is a festival for you and your people after you; for you in it is good; you are first, and the Jews and Christians after you. In it is an hour in which no one supplicates his Lord for good allotted to him except He gives it, or seeks refuge from evil except He averts from him what is greater than it. And we call it in the Hereafter the Day of Increase. That is because your Lord made in Paradise a wide valley of white musk; when Friday comes, He descends from Illiyyun and sits upon His throne, the throne surrounded by pulpits of gold crowned with jewels; the truthful and the martyrs come and sit upon them; the people of the chambers come from their chambers until they sit upon the dune - a white dune of fragrant musk - then He manifests to them and says: I am He who fulfilled My promise to you, completed My favor upon you; this is the place of My honor, so ask Me. So they ask Him contentment. So He says: My contentment settled you in My abode and granted you My honor, so ask Me. So they ask Him contentment. So He makes them witness contentment. Then He opens for them what no eye saw nor ever crossed the heart of man, until their departure from Friday - a green peridot or a red ruby, its rivers flowing, its fruits hanging low, in it its spouses and servants. They are not in Paradise more eager for anything than Friday, to increase in looking at their Lord, blessed and exalted, and His honor; therefore it is called the Day of Increase. Al-Tabarani said: None reported it from Abu Imran except Abd al-Salam ibn Hafs; Khalid was alone in it. And Ali ibn Ishkab reported it from Abu Badr, from Ziyad ibn Khaythamah, from Uthman ibn Muslim, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cast to us one day; when he finished, we said: You did well. So he said: Gabriel came to me in the form of a white mirror with a black dot in it - and he mentioned similar to this hadith. And Shayban ibn Farrukh reported it from al-Sa'q ibn Hazn, from Ali ibn al-Hakam al-Bunani, from Anas."
"2133","Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb al-Bunani, from Anas. 2292 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ja'far reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us - and once he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb reported to us - from Anas ibn Malik who said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal used to lead his people; Haram entered while wanting to water his palms; he entered the mosque to pray with the people; when he saw Mu'adh lengthen, he shortened his prayer and joined his palms to water them. When Mu'adh finished the prayer, it was said to him: Haram entered the mosque; when he saw you lengthen, he shortened his prayer and joined his palms to water them. He said: He is a hypocrite; does he hurry from prayer for watering his palms? He said: So Haram came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while Mu'adh was with him, and said: O Prophet of Allah, I wanted to water palms of mine; I entered to pray with the people; when he lengthened, I shortened my prayer and joined my palms to water them, so he claimed I am a hypocrite?! So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to Mu'adh and said: Are you a trial, are you a trial? Do not lengthen with them; recite Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and By the sun and its brightness, and the like."
"2134","2293 - And the Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Saffar informed us - in Nishapur - that Wajih ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Ya'qub ibn Ahmad al-Sayrafi, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Ismaili and Abd al-Karim ibn Hawazin al-Qushayri reported to us, they said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Khaffaf reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ismail Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas who said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal used to lead his people; Haram entered - wanting to water his palms - and entered the mosque to pray among the people; when he saw Mu'adh lengthen, he shortened his prayer and joined his palms to water them. When Mu'adh prayed, it was said to him: Haram entered the mosque; when he saw you lengthen, he shortened his prayer and joined his palms to water them. So he said: He is a hypocrite! Does he hurry prayer for watering his palms? So Haram came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while Mu'adh was with him, and said: O Prophet of Allah, I wanted to water palms of mine; I entered the mosque to pray with the people; when he lengthened, I shortened my prayer and joined my palms to water them, so he claimed I am a hypocrite? So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to Mu'adh and said: Are you a tempter? Do not lengthen with them; recite Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, By the sun and its brightness, and the like."
"2135","Another: 2294 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us - in Baghdad - that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Anas who said: While the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among palms of ours - palms of Abu Talhah - he went to relieve himself. He said: And Bilal walked behind him, honoring the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by not walking beside him. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed a grave and stood until Bilal reached him. So he said: Woe to you, O Bilal, do you hear what I hear? He said: I hear nothing. He said: The occupant of this grave is being punished; so he was asked about, and found to be a Jew. Abu Ma'mar reported it from Abd al-Warith."
"2136","2295 - Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Sam'ani informed us - in Marw - that Abd al-Khaliq ibn Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Haskawayh reported to us, Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Hiri reported to us, Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Duhaym al-Shaybani reported to us - in Kufa - Muhammad - he is Ibn al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Hunayn - narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Amr Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: While the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among palms of ours - palms of Abu Talhah - relieving himself, he said: And Bilal walked behind him. So he said: Woe to you, O Bilal, do you hear what I hear? He said: I hear nothing. He said: The occupant of this grave is being punished. He said: So he was asked about, and found to be a Jew."
"2137","Another: 2296 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ghazi informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqqur reported to us, Ali ibn Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Shadhan al-Harbi reported to us, Abu Abdullah Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Jabbar al-Sufi narrated to us, Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Umarah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three will remain in my nation: boasting over lineages, wailing, and rain-stars."
"2138","2297 - And this Zahir informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili reported to us, Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Dhari' al-Basri narrated to us, he said: I heard Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb narrate from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three will not cease in my nation until the Hour comes: wailing, boasting over lineages, and rain-stars."
"2139","2298 - And Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us that Yahya ibn Ali ibn al-Tarrah informed them - recited to him - Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqqur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis reported to us, it was said to him: Abu Hamid Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to you, Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya ibn Umarah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three people will not abandon until the Hour comes: wailing, boasting over lineages, and rain-stars. And Nasr ibn Ali reported it from Zakariyya ibn Yahya, similar. Abu Zur'ah al-Razi was asked about Zakariyya ibn al-Dhari', and spoke well of him. It has a corroborating witness in Muslim from the hadith of Abu Malik al-Ash'ari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: Four in my nation, adding: And defamation of lineages."
"2140","Another: 2299 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Mu'addib informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad - known as Kulli - informed them, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh reported to us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Kharjani reported to us, the judge Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Assal reported to us, Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Sa'id ibn Shahriyar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Sulayman al-Qarqasani narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr. Al-Bukhari reported from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As the like."
"2141","Abd al-Warith, freedman of Anas, from Anas. 2300 - Abu Rashid Ismail ibn Ghanim ibn Khalid al-Bayyi' al-Asbahani informed us that Abu Sa'id Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Mutarriz informed them - recited to him - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Qatari al-Khashshab narrated to us, from Abd al-Warith, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man has his food placed before him, and it is not lifted until he is forgiven. So it was said: O Messenger of Allah, for what is that? He said: He says: In the name of Allah when it is placed, and praise be to Allah when it is lifted. Qatari: Ibn Abi Hatim mentioned him, saying: Waki', Ubayd Allah ibn Musa and Ubayd ibn Ishaq reported from him, and he mentioned no criticism of him."
"2142","Asim ibn Sulayman, from Anas. 2301 - Abu al-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak ibn al-Ma'tush al-Harimi informed us - by my recitation to him on the western side of Baghdad - I said to him: Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn informed you - and he acknowledged it - he said: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib reported to us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Usamah narrated to us, Sharik informed me, from Asim al-Ahwal (h). 2302 - And Ahmad said: Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas, with it. [FLAG: matn missing in source, breaks off after chain]"
"2143","2303 - And Mahmud ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud al-Haddad informed us - in Isfahan - that Mas'ud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Simsar reported to us, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khurshidh gave his statement, al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Sharik, from Asim, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O possessor of two ears. Their wording is one."
"2144","2304 - Abu al-Faraj Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Umari informed us - in Baghdad - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Muhammad reported to us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shafi'i reported to us, Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us (h). 2305 - Al-Shafi'i said: And al-Fadl ibn al-Hasan ibn al-A'yan al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Luwayn narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O possessor of two ears."
"2145","2306 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Baqqal reported to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq reported to us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Jamil reported to us, Ahmad ibn Mani' reported to us, Abu Nasr narrated to me, Sharik narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O possessor of two ears. Abu Dawud brought it from Ibrahim ibn Mahdi. And al-Tirmidhi reported it from Mahmud ibn Ghaylan - both - from Sharik. Al-Daraqutni said: Muhammad ibn Abi Ahmad al-Zubayri reported it from al-Thawri, from Asim, from Anas. And he erred in it against Abu Ahmad; the correct from Abu Ahmad is what Nasr ibn Ali and Ahmad ibn Sinan reported from him, from Sharik, from Asim."
"2146","Another: 2307 - Ismail ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Qattan informed us - in Baghdad - that Abu Ghalib Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Banna informed them, Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Muhtadi Billah reported to us, Abu Hafs Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Kattani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harun al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abu Hashim Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiyah al-Darir narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about fasting while traveling. He said: So he said: Whoever breaks fast, it is a concession; whoever fasts, fasting is better. And it was reported from Musa ibn A'yan, from Ma'mar, from Asim, from Anas, halted."
"2147","Another: 2308 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - in Isfahan - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, the teacher Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muqri al-Khabbazi al-Tabari reported to us, Abu al-Tayyib al-Rabi' ibn Muhammad al-Hatimi reported to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sharqi reported to us, that Hatim ibn Yunus al-Jurjani narrated to them - from memory - Ali ibn Uthman narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's prayer in congregation exceeds a man's prayer alone by twenty-some degrees. Al-Daraqutni said: Hajjaj ibn Minhal was alone in it from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Asim - meaning from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi reported it from Hammad, halted, and it is correct. I say: This narration of ours is other than the narration of al-Hajjaj, so he was not alone in it then. And it has a corroborating witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah."
"2148","Another: 2309 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri reported to us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili reported to us, Abu Bakr reported to us, Abdullah ibn al-Ajlah narrated to us, from Asim, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in a single garment, crossing its ends. Abdullah ibn al-Ajlah: al-Razi said: No harm in him. And this already came in other than the narration of Asim."
"2149","Another: 2310 - Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Yusuf informed us - by ijazah - and my maternal uncle, the Imam, the devout Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi, reported it from him to us, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Bishran reported to us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad al-Daraqutni narrated to us, Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated to us, al-Ala ibn Ismail al-Attar narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say takbir until his thumbs aligned with his ears, then bow until every joint of him settled in its place, then descend with takbir; his knees preceded his hands. Al-Ala ibn Ismail was alone in it from Hafs, with this chain, and Allah knows best."
"2150","Another: 2311 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Anmati narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ismail ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The perfume of men is what its scent is apparent and its color hidden; the perfume of women is what its color is apparent and its scent hidden."
"2151","Another: 2312 - Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abi al-Raja informed us - in Isfahan - that Mas'ud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abi Abdullah ibn Mandah reported to us, my father reported to us, Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Jami' and Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Hamzah reported to us, both saying: Khayr ibn Arafah narrated to us, Urwah ibn Marwan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik - may Allah be pleased with him - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intercession is for the people of major sins of my nation. Al-Tabarani reported it from Khayr ibn Arafah al-Tujibi al-Misri. Abu Hatim and Abu Zur'ah said: This hadith is rejected with this chain. And Yunus ibn Abd al-A'la reported it from Ibn al-Mubarak. And Abu Hatim said: It is an error; it is Asim, from Anas: Whoever denies intercession or the Basin ... [FLAG: source ends with ellipsis]"
"2152","2313 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Thaqafi informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah reported to us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Khayr ibn Arafah al-Tujibi Abu Tahir al-Misri narrated to us, Urwah ibn Marwan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intercession is for the people of major sins of my nation on the Day of Resurrection. Al-Tabarani said: None reported it from Asim except Ibn al-Mubarak; Urwah was alone in it."
"2153","Attab - freedman of Ibn Hurmuz - from Anas. 2314 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi informed us - in Baghdad - that his father informed them, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Sarifini reported to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Hababah reported to us, Abdullah - he is Ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi - narrated to us, Ali - meaning Ibn al-Ja'd - narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Attab who said: I heard Anas say: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this hand of mine upon hearing and obeying as much as I could."
"2154","2315 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far reported to us, Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Attab, freedman of Hurmuz, informed me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this hand of mine upon hearing and obeying as much as I could."
"2155","2316 - And Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah informed them, al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard Attab, freedman of Ibn Hurmuz, who said: I heard Anas say: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this right hand of mine upon hearing and obeying as much as I could. Thus Imam Ahmad reported it in his Musnad. And he also reported it from Waki' and Yazid ibn Harun, from Shu'bah."
"2156","2317 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri reported to us, Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili reported to us, Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Attab, freedman of Hurmuz, who said: I accompanied Anas ibn Malik on a ship and heard him say: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this hand of mine - pointing with his right palm - upon hearing and obeying as much as I could. Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Abu al-Nadr reported it from Shu'bah. And similar already came in the narration of Ja'far ibn Ma'bad. Ibn Majah brought it from Ali ibn Muhammad, from Waki', from Shu'bah. And it has a corroborating witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Jarir al-Bajali."
"2157","Uthman ibn Jabir, from Anas. 2318 - The Imam Abu al-Jud Ghiyath ibn Faris ibn Makki al-Muqri informed us - in Cairo - that Abdullah ibn Rifa'ah ibn Ghadir informed them, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad reported to us, Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajj reported to us, he said: Abu al-Qasim Ali ibn Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim reported to us, Abu Zur'ah - meaning Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr al-Nasri - narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Jabir, from Anas ibn Malik that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: War is deceit. Thus Abu al-Yaman reported it. And Abu al-Mughirah reported it from Safwan, saying: Amr ibn Uthman ibn Jabir, and Allah knows best. Imam Ahmad reported it from Abu al-Yaman and Abu al-Mughirah."
"2158","Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab al-Hashimi, from Anas. 2319 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us - there - that Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Fudayli informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad al-Malihi reported to us, Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hafsawayh al-Sarakhsi narrated to us, Abu Yazid Hatim ibn Mahbub al-Shami reported to us, Salamah - he is Ibn Shabib - narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Uthman ibn Mawhab, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatimah: What prevents you from hearing what I counsel you with: to say morning and evening: O Living, O Sustainer, by Your mercy I seek help; rectify all my affairs for me, and do not leave me to myself for the blink of an eye."
"2159","2320 - And Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi informed us - in Damascus - that Ma'ali ibn Hibat Allah informed them, Sahl ibn Bishr ibn Ahmad al-Isfarayini reported to us, Ali ibn Munir ibn Ahmad al-Khallal reported to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Naysaburi reported to us, Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasai reported to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Sallam reported to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Mawhab al-Hashimi informed me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatimah - may Allah be pleased with her -: What prevents you from hearing what I counsel you with: to say when you wake and when you evening: O Living, O Sustainer, by Your mercy I seek help; rectify all my affairs for me, and do not leave me to myself for the blink of an eye."
"2160","2321 - And Muhammad ibn Hamzah informed us - in Damascus - that Ali ibn al-Muslim ibn al-Fath al-Sulami informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Hadid reported to us, my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ahmad reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Samiri reported to us, Abu al-Abbas Ismail ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani wrote to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Uthman ibn Mawhab narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatimah: What prevents you from hearing what I counsel you with: to say when you wake - and he mentioned it. [FLAG: matn truncated in source after fa-dhakarahu]"
"2161","2322 - And the Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur informed us - in Nishapur - that his grandfather Umar ibn Ahmad informed them, Ahmad ibn Khalaf reported to us, the judge Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hafiz reported to us, Abu Abdullah al-Saffar narrated to us, Ibn Abi al-Dunya narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah and others narrated to us, they said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik, and he mentioned it similar. Al-Hakim brought it in al-Mustadrak."
"2162","Urwah ibn Ruwaym al-Lakhmi, from Anas. 2323 - Sa'id ibn Rawh ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrawayh al-Salihani informed us - in Isfahan - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan reported to us, al-Hasan ibn Sufyan ibn Amir reported to us, Muhammad ibn al-Mutawakkil narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn al-Muntasir narrated to us, Urwah ibn Ruwaym narrated to us, he said: We were with Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan when Anas ibn Malik came to him. So Abd al-Malik said to him: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with no one between you and him, with no addition or omission. Anas said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Faith is Yemeni, toward Lakhm and Judham; indeed disbelief and hardness of hearts are in these two tribes of Rabi'ah and Mudar."
"2163","2324 - And Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan reported to us, Ahmad reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Urwah ibn Ruwaym who said: Anas ibn Malik came to Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan while he was - in Damascus - he said: So he entered upon him, and Mu'awiyah said to him: Narrate to me a hadith you heard from the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with no one between you and him. He said: Anas said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Faith is Yemeni, thus, toward Lakhm and Judham. It has a corroborating witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah, except he did not mention Lakhm and Judham."
"2164","Amir ibn Sharahil al-Sha'bi, from Anas. 2325 - Shihab ibn Mahmud al-Hatimi informed us - in Herat - that Abd al-Salam ibn Ahmad ibn Ismail informed them, Muhammad ibn Abi Mas'ud al-Farisi reported to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Shurayh reported to us, it was said to him: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated to you, Yusuf ibn Sa'id ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Kabir ibn al-Mu'afa narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Dharih, from al-Sha'bi, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the nearness of the Hour: the crescent seen for one night and said to be of two nights, sudden death appearing, and mosques taken as roads."
"2165","2326 - And As'ad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf Abu al-Futuh al-Ijli informed us - in Isfahan - that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Juzdaniyyah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah reported to us. 2327 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Ahmad ibn Abdullah reported to us, both saying: Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Missisi reported to us, Abd al-Kabir ibn al-Mu'afa ibn Imran narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from al-Abbas ibn Dharih, from al-Sha'bi, from Anas ibn Malik - raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - who said: Among the nearness of the Hour: the crescent seen beforehand and said to be of two nights, mosques taken as roads, and sudden death appearing. Al-Tabarani said: None reported it from al-Sha'bi except al-Abbas, nor from him except Sharik; Abd al-Kabir was alone in it. Al-Daraqutni mentioned this narration then said: Others report it from al-Sha'bi, mursal, and Allah knows best. In the narration of Ahmad ibn Abdullah from al-Tabarani: He raises it, the rest like it."
"2166","Uqbah ibn Wassaj, from Anas; al-Bukhari reported for him a hadith from Anas. 2328 - The Hafiz Abu Muhammad Abd al-Aziz ibn Mahmud al-Bazzaz informed us - in Baghdad - that Muhammad ibn Umar al-Urmawi informed them, Jabir ibn Yasin al-Attar reported to us, Umar ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Kattani reported to us, Abdullah - he is al-Baghawi - narrated to us, Abu Talib al-Nasai - he is Abd al-Jabbar ibn Asim - narrated to us, Hani ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ablah al-Uqayli narrated to me (h). 2329 - And Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi informed us - in Baghdad - that al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khayyat informed them, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqqur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis reported to us, Abdullah - he is al-Baghawi - narrated to us, Abu Talib narrated to us, Hani ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Ablah al-Uqayli narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah who said: Uqbah ibn Wassaj narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah brighten whoever hears my saying - and al-Kattani said: May Allah brighten the heart of whoever hears my saying - then he did not add in it: Three over which the heart of a Muslim man never harbors treachery: sincerity of deed for Allah, exalted; sincere advice to rulers; and sticking to the congregation of Muslims, for their supplication encompasses those behind them. Al-Daraqutni mentioned this narration and others, saying: All disturbed."
"2167","Ata ibn Abi Rabah. 2330 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn As'ad al-Harawi informed us - there - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi reported to us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi reported to us, Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah reported to us, my grandfather the Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq reported to us, Ali ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Farrukh reported to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Honor your houses with some of your prayer."
"2168","2331 - And Abu Tahir Barakat ibn Ibrahim al-Khushu'i informed us that Abd al-Karim ibn Hamzah ibn al-Khidr al-Sulami informed them, Abd al-Aziz ibn Ahmad al-Kinani reported to us, Tammam ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Razi al-Hafiz reported to us, Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Habib ibn Abd al-Malik reported to us, Allan ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Farrukh narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give your houses a share of your prayer."
"2169","2332 - And it was recited to Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sa'd al-Thaqafi - in Damascus, while we listened - your grandfather the Hafiz Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl informed you - while you listened, and he acknowledged it - Umar ibn Ahmad al-Faqih reported to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Ali reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih al-Misri narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Farrukh narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Anas ibn Malik - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Honor your houses with some of your prayer. Abdullah ibn Farrukh: Muslim brought for him in his Sahih. It has a corroborating witness in Muslim from the hadith of Jabir ibn Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When one of you finishes prayer in his mosque, let him give his house a share of his prayer, for Allah places good in his house from his prayer."
"2170","Another: 2333 - Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Sufi informed us - in Herat - that Zahir ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad informed them, Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman reported to us, Abu Tahir - he is Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah - reported to us, my grandfather - meaning Muhammad ibn Ishaq - reported to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Ibn Farrukh reported to us. 2334 - Muhammad ibn Ishaq said: And Ali ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mughirah al-Misri narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Rabi' ibn Tariq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Farrukh reported to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to me, from Ata, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the lightest of people in prayer while complete. He said: And I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and as soon as we gave salam we stood; then I sat with Abu Bakr, and when he gave salam he sprang from his place as if rising from hot stones. Its beginning is recorded in the Sahih: lightest of people in prayer."
"2171","2335 - And As'ad ibn Sa'id ibn Rawh informed us - recited to him in Isfahan - it was said to him: Fatimah bint Abdullah informed you - recited to her while you listened, and he acknowledged it - Muhammad ibn Abdullah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Yahya ibn Uthman ibn Salih narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Farrukh narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and as soon as he gave salam he stood; then I sat with Abu Bakr - may Allah be pleased with him - and when he gave salam he sprang as if rising from a hot stone."
"2172","Ata ibn Abi Maymunah Abu Mu'adh, freedman of Anas, from him. 2336 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim al-Saydalani informed us - in Isfahan - that Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Thaqafi informed them, Muhammad ibn Ridhah reported to us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani reported to us, Sahl ibn Muhammad ibn Sahl al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Jumahi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Muzani narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah. 2337 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath informed us - in Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - while he was present - Abu Nu'aym al-Asbahani reported to us, Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bakr ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, from Anas who said: Nothing involving retaliation was ever raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except he commanded pardon in it. Their wording is one, except that [...]. [FLAG: source ends with lacuna brackets]"
"2173","2338 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi al-Darir informed us - in Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur reported to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali reported to us, Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili reported to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Bakr - meaning al-Muzani - narrated to me, I heard Ata ibn Abi Maymunah narrate - I know it only from Anas - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was never raised retaliation except he commanded pardon in it."
"2174","2339 - And Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali ibn al-Muslim al-Lakhmi informed us - in Damascus - that Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Muslim ibn al-Fath al-Sulami informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Abi al-Hadid reported to us, my grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Uthman reported to us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ja'far al-Samiri reported to us, Abu Yusuf Ya'qub al-Qulusi narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail al-Minqari narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Bakr ibn Abdullah al-Muzani narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, freedman of Anas, from Anas who said: Nothing involving retaliation was ever raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except he commanded pardon in it. Imam Ahmad reported it from Abd al-Samad, from Abdullah ibn Bakr. And Abu Dawud brought it in al-Diyat from Musa ibn Ismail. And al-Nasai brought it from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, and from Ibn Bashshar, from Ibn Mahdi, Bahz ibn Asad and Affan ibn Muslim - all - from Abdullah ibn Bakr, similar. And Ibn Majah reported it from Ishaq ibn Mansur, from Hibban ibn Hilal - all - from Abdullah ibn Bakr, similar."
"2175","Umar ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from his uncle Anas. 2340 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us that Mahmud al-Sayrafi informed them - while he was present - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan reported to us, Abdullah al-Qabbab reported to us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim reported to us, Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari narrated to us, Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Tarif ibn al-Daffa' narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to me, from Umar ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas who said: I said: O uncle, a horse of mine died tonight. He said: Why did you not slaughter it and feed your neighbors? So I said: Has it reached you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade horse meat? He said: I, by Allah, am witness: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the meat of dogs and domestic donkeys, and the people spoke much about that. As for donkey meat, it was mentioned from Anas in the Sahih."
"2176","Amr ibn Zaynab al-Ghubari, from Anas. 2341 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il narrated to us; Abd al-Samad narrated to us; Harb narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Zaynab narrated to me, that Anas ibn Malik narrated to him, that Mu'adh said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think, if there are rulers over us who do not follow your Sunnah and do not abide by your command, what do you command us regarding them? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no obedience to one who does not obey Allah, mighty and majestic."
"2177","2342 - And Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informed them: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us; Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Abd al-Samad narrated to us; Harb ibn Shaddad - a Basran - narrated to us; Yahya - meaning Ibn Abi Kathir - narrated to us: Amr ibn Zaynab al-Ghubari said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to him, that Mu'adh said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think, if there are rulers over us - then he mentioned the like of it, except that Yahya did not say (narrated to us), and Allah knows best."
"2178","Amr ibn Amir al-Ansari, from Anas. 2343 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Harith, from Amr ibn Amir al-Ansari, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade three things: the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, visiting graves, and this nabidh in these vessels. Then he said: Lo, I forbade you three things, then it occurred to me that people store their condiments, offer gifts to their guests, and keep provisions for those absent among them, so eat and keep whatever you wish. And I had forbidden you from visiting graves - I think Abu Bakr doubted - so visit them and do not speak obscene speech, for it is said that it softens the heart, brings tears to the eye, and reminds of the Hereafter. And I had forbidden you nabidh, so make nabidh in whatever you wish; whoever wishes may tie the mouth of his waterskin, bearing his own sin."
"2179","2344 - And the judge Abu al-Faraj Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Umari informed us - at Baghdad - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Husayn informed them: Abu Talib Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ghaylan informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Shafi'i informed us; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ubaydah narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Ibrahim - he is Ibn Tahman - narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Kufi, from Amr ibn Amir and Abd al-Wahhab, from Anas ibn Malik, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, and nabidh in al-hantam, al-dubba, al-naqir and al-muzaffat vessels, and visiting graves. He said: Then he said: Lo, I had forbidden you three things, then later it occurred to me: I had forbidden you eating the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days - and he mentioned the hadith. Such is in the narration of our Shaykh; he did not add to this. And Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad, from Affan, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Amr ibn Amir, from Anas, with the like of it. And the like of it has been narrated in Muslim from the hadith of Buraydah ibn al-Husayb al-Aslami."
"2180","Amr ibn Abi Amr, the freedman of al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Anas. 2345 - Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali informed us - by my reading to him, in the western quarter of Baghdad - I said to him: Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed you - by reading to him while you listened, and he acknowledged it: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i informed us; Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Yunus narrated to us; Layth narrated to us, from Yazid - meaning Ibn al-Had - from Amr, from Anas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I am the first of people for whom the earth will split open from around my skull on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast; and I shall be given the Banner of Praise, and no boast; and I am the master of people on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast; and I am the first who shall enter Paradise on the Day of Resurrection, and no boast. And I shall come to the gate of Paradise and take hold of its ring, and they will say: Who is this? And I shall say: I am Muhammad, so they will open for me and I shall enter, and lo, al-Jabbar will be facing me, so I shall prostrate to Him, and He will say: Raise your head, O Muhammad, speak and you shall be heard, say and it shall be accepted from you, intercede and your intercession shall be granted. So I shall raise my head and say: My nation, my nation, O Lord. And He will say: Go to your nation; whomever you find in his heart the weight of a grain of barley of faith, admit him into Paradise. So I shall go forth, and whomever I find in his heart that, I shall admit them into Paradise. Then lo, al-Jabbar, mighty and majestic, will be facing me, and I shall prostrate to Him, and He will say: Raise your head, O Muhammad, speak and you shall be heard, say and it shall be accepted from you, intercede and your intercession shall be granted. So I shall raise my head and say: My nation, my nation, my Lord. And He will say: Go to your nation; whomever you find in his heart half a grain of barley of faith, admit them into Paradise. So I shall go, and whomever I find in his heart the weight of that, I shall admit them into Paradise. Then I shall find al-Jabbar facing me, and I shall prostrate to Him, and He will say: Raise your head, O Muhammad, speak and you shall be heard, say and it shall be accepted from you, intercede and your intercession shall be granted. So I shall raise my head and say: My nation, my nation. And He will say: Go to your nation; whomever you find in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of faith, admit him into Paradise. So I shall go, and whomever I find in his heart the weight of that, I shall admit them into Paradise. And the reckoning of people will be finished, and those remaining of my nation will be admitted into the Fire with the people of the Fire, and the people of the Fire will say: What did it avail you that you used to worship Allah and associate nothing with Him? Then al-Jabbar will say: By My might, I shall surely free them from the Fire. So He will send to them, and they will come out having been scorched, and they will enter the River of Life, and they will sprout in it as the seed sprouts in the froth of the flood, and it will be written between their eyes: These are the freed ones of Allah, blessed and exalted. Then they will be taken and admitted into Paradise, and the people of Paradise will say to them: These are the dwellers of Hell. Then al-Jabbar will say: Rather, these are the freed ones of al-Jabbar. The hadith of intercession has been narrated in the Sahih from the hadith of Anas, except that in this narration there are wordings not found in it, and Allah knows best. Al-Bukhari narrated a hadith with the chain of al-Layth, from Ibn al-Had, from Amr, from Anas. Al-Nasa'i brought it, from Ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam, from Shu'ayb, from al-Layth. And al-Darimi narrated it in his book, from Abdullah ibn Salih, from al-Layth."
"2181","Another narration. 2346 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Darir informed us - may Allah have mercy on him - at Isfahan - that Zahir ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Mustamli informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us; Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan informed us; Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Madini narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hanzali narrated to us, saying: I read to Abu Qurrah: Did Musa ibn Uqbah mention - ha. 2347 - And Abu al-Ala Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid - known as Lafhali al-Isbahani - informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nu'aym informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasa'i narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, saying: I said to Abu Qurrah: Did Musa ibn Uqbah mention, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Anas ibn Malik: that a man entered the mosque, announcing a lost animal, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May you not find it? And he acknowledged it, saying: Yes. It has a corroborating witness in Muslim from the hadith of Buraydah."
"2182","Isa ibn Tahman, from Anas. 2348 - The Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar al-Mufti informed us - at Naysabur - that Wajih ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Shahhami informed them - ha. 2349 - And the Imam Abu al-Muzaffar Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Sam'ani al-Mufti informed us - at Marw - that Abu al-As'ad Hibat al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Hawazin informed them; both said: Abd al-Karim ibn Hawazin informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Abdan al-Ahwazi informed us; Ahmad ibn Ubayd informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali al-Khazzaz narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Hisham ibn Bahram narrated to us; Yahya ibn Ibrahim al-Kufi narrated to us, from Isa ibn Tahman, who said: I heard Anas say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: O Possessor of Majesty and Honor, so he said: Ask, for He has turned toward you."
"2183","Isa al-Iskandarani, from Anas. 2350 - Ahmad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Lanjani informed us - may Allah have mercy on him - at Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn al-Abbas ibn Ali al-Rustami informed them: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Tayyan informed us; Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khurshid informed us by his word; Abu Bakr Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ziyad al-Naysaburi informed us; Yunus - he is Ibn Abd al-A'la - narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to me, that Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to him, from Isa - who used to reside in the mosque of Alexandria - that he heard Anas ibn Malik informing from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: When Allah, mighty and majestic, loves a people, He afflicts them with trials."
"2184","2351 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu al-Fath Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah al-Asqalani informed us; Harmalah ibn Yahya al-Tujibi narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Amr informed us, that Ishaq ibn al-Azraq narrated to him, from Isa - who used to reside in the mosque of Alexandria - that he heard Anas informing from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: When Allah, mighty and majestic, loves a people, He afflicts them with trials."
"2185","Imran ibn Qudamah al-Ammi al-Basri, from Anas. Abu Hatim al-Razi said: There is no harm in his hadith; he narrated from Anas, and Harb ibn Maymun narrated from him. 2352 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us: al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed us; Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us; Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Harb ibn Maymun narrated to us, saying: I heard Imran al-Ammi say: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where Allah created the disease, He created the cure, so seek treatment."
"2186","Ghaylan ibn Jarir al-Mi'wali, from Anas. 2353 - Abu al-Mafakhir Uthman ibn Mahmud ibn Abi Bakr - known as Habbawayh - informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Baghban informed them: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Mandah informed us; Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khurshid informed us by his word; Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Isma'il al-Mahamili narrated to us - by dictation - Abu Yahya Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us; al-Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us; Bashshar ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ghaylan ibn Jarir narrated to us, from Anas - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most complete of the believers in faith are the best of them in character."
"2187","2354 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu Tahir - he is Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Ma'dani al-Adib - informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Hurmuz al-Ardistani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us; Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us; Mu'alla ibn Asad narrated to us; Abu Awn al-Uqayli narrated to us; Ghaylan ibn Jarir narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most complete of the believers in faith are the best of them in character. Bashshar ibn Ibrahim ibn Awn: Abu Hatim al-Razi deemed him trustworthy. Al-Daraqutni said: Bashshar ibn Ibrahim Abu Awn alone narrated it, from Ghaylan."
"2188","Qatadah ibn Di'amah al-Sadusi, from Anas. 2355 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abdullah al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us; Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Aruzzi narrated to us; Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us; Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that a man used to buy and sell in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there was weakness in his judgment, so his family came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, place an interdiction upon so-and-so, for he buys and sells and there is weakness in his judgment. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and forbade him from selling, and he said: O Prophet of Allah, I cannot refrain from selling. So he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you will not give up selling, then say: Take and give, and no deceit."
"2189","2356 - And Abu al-Futuh Mas'ud ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Karim al-Daqqaq informed us - in the western quarter of Baghdad - that the Hafiz Abu al-Qasim Isma'il ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Samarqandi informed them: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqqur informed us; Muhammad ibn Abdullah, the nephew of Yahya, informed us; Isma'il - he is Ibn al-Abbas al-Warraq - narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us; Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that a man in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to trade, and there was weakness in his judgment, so his family came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, place an interdiction upon so-and-so, for he trades and there is weakness in his judgment. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and forbade him from selling, and he said: O Prophet of Allah, I cannot refrain from selling. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you will not give up selling, then take with give-and-take, and no deceit."
"2190","2357 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them - while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us; Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Azhar ibn Marwan narrated to us; Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik: that a man in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had weakness in his judgment, and he used to trade, and his family came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, place an interdiction upon him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and forbade him from that, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, I cannot refrain. So he said: When you trade, say: Take, and no deceit. Imam Ahmad narrated it, from Abd al-Wahhab. And Abu Dawud narrated it in his Sunan, from al-Aruzzi. And Ibn Majah brought it, from Azhar ibn Marwan. And al-Tirmidhi and al-Nasa'i - both - brought it, from Yusuf ibn Hammad - both of them - from Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la, from Sa'id; and al-Tirmidhi said: A sahih gharib hadith. And Abu Hatim ibn Hibban brought it in his book, from Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili with his chain. And al-Daraqutni brought it in his book, from al-Baghawi, from Ahmad ibn Hanbal, from Abd al-Wahhab. And Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated it, from Sa'id, like the narration of Abd al-Wahhab and Abd al-A'la. And it has been narrated from Sa'id, from Qatadah, as mursal, and Allah knows best. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Ibn Umar."
"2191","Another narration. 2358 - Al-Mubarak ibn al-Mubarak al-Harimi informed us - at Baghdad - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Surayj and Yunus ibn Muhammad said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah and Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Prices rose in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would fix prices. So he said: Allah is the Creator, the Withholder, the Extender, the Provider, the Fixer of prices, and I hope to meet Allah, mighty and majestic, with no one seeking from me redress for an injustice I did to him in blood or wealth. And Imam Ahmad narrated it - also - from Affan, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Qatadah, and Thabit, and Humayd, from Anas."
"2192","2359 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us; Abd al-Wahid - he is Ibn Ghiyath - narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: Prices rose in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so they said: O Messenger of Allah, fix prices for us. So he said: Allah is the Withholder, the Extender, the Fixer of prices, the Provider; I hope to meet Allah with none of you seeking from me redress for an injustice in life or wealth. Abu Dawud narrated it, from Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah, from Affan ibn Muslim, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Thabit. And al-Tirmidhi brought it, from Bundar, from Hajjaj ibn Minhal, from Hammad, from Thabit, and from Qatadah, and Humayd, from Anas. And Ibn Majah narrated it, from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Hajjaj, from Hammad, from them. And al-Tirmidhi said: A sahih hadith."
"2193","Another narration. 2360 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Darir informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us; Nasr - he is Ibn Ali - narrated to us, saying: My father informed me, from al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on a military expedition, he would say: O Allah, You are my support and You are my helper, and by You I fight."
"2194","2361 - And Zahir informed us: al-Husayn informed us; Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad informed us; Ubayd Allah - he is Ibn Umar al-Jushami - narrated to us; Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us; al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met the enemy, he would say: O Allah, You are my support and my helper, and by You I fight. Abu Dawud and al-Tirmidhi - both - brought it, from Nasr ibn Ali, and al-Tirmidhi said: Hasan gharib."
"2195","2362 - And Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Muhammad al-Qurashi informed us - at Damascus - that Ma'ali ibn Hibat Allah ibn al-Hasan al-Tha'labi informed them: Sahl ibn Bishr al-Isfarayini informed us; Ali ibn Munir ibn Ahmad al-Khallal informed us; Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zakariyya ibn Hayyawayh informed us; Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasa'i informed us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us; Azhar ibn al-Qasim narrated to us; al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went on an expedition, he would say: O Allah, You are my support and my helper, and by You I fight. Thus al-Nasa'i brought it in Amal al-Yawm wa al-Laylah. And Abu Hatim ibn Hibban narrated it in his book, from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Nasr ibn Ali."
"2196","Another narration. 2363 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us; Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us; Abu Bishr Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from vitiligo, madness, leprosy, and evil diseases."
"2197","2364 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from vitiligo, leprosy, madness, and evil diseases. Imam Ahmad narrated it, from Bahz, and Hasan ibn Musa, from Hammad."
"2198","2365 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - at Isfahan - that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them - while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us; Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Abu Musa narrated to us; Abu Dawud narrated to us; Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from madness, leprosy, vitiligo, and from evil diseases. Al-Nasa'i brought it, from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa. And Abu Dawud brought it, from Musa ibn Isma'il, from Hammad."
"2199","2366 - And Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi informed us - at Baghdad - that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them: al-Sharif Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Muhtadi Billah informed us; Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Allaf narrated to us - by dictation - Abdullah al-Baghawi narrated to us; Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - ha."
"2200","2367 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan informed us; Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Jabbar informed us; Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - the like of it, except that he said: and the worst of diseases. And likewise Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated it, from Bishr ibn al-Sari, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Qatadah, saying: and the worst of diseases. And Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated it, from Qatadah, with additional wordings."
"2201","2368 - Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Qalanisi al-Dhuhli narrated to us; Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us; Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Nahwi narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from helplessness and laziness, and I seek refuge in You from hardness of heart, heedlessness, destitution, humiliation and wretchedness, and I seek refuge in You from transgression, discord and hypocrisy, and seeking repute and showing off, and I seek refuge in You from deafness, dumbness, madness, vitiligo, leprosy, and evil diseases. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it in this complete form except Shayban; Adam alone narrated it. I say: and his statement: he alone narrated it."
"2202","2369 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us; Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim narrated to us; Ibn Warah narrated to us; my father and Ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us; Shayban narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from anxiety, helplessness and laziness, and I seek refuge in You from hardness of heart, heedlessness, destitution, humiliation and wretchedness, and I seek refuge in You from deafness, dumbness, madness, leprosy, and the worst of diseases."
"2203","2370 - And the Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar informed us - at Naysabur - that his grandfather Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur informed them: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Khalaf al-Shirazi informed us, saying: al-Hakim Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hafiz informed us: Abdan ibn Yazid al-Daqqaq narrated to us - at Hamadhan - Ibrahim ibn al-Husayn ibn Dizil narrated to us; Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us; Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in his supplication: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from helplessness, laziness, miserliness, old age, hardness of heart, heedlessness, destitution, humiliation and wretchedness, and I seek refuge in You from poverty, disbelief, transgression, discord, hypocrisy, showing off and seeking repute, and I seek refuge in You from deafness, dumbness, madness, vitiligo, and evil diseases. Thus al-Hakim brought it in al-Mustadrak."
"2204","2371 - And Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed us - at Isfahan - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Janzarudhi informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Dahtham al-Tarsusi informed us; Ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us - at Baghdad - al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kindi narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Masruq narrated to us, from Shayban, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to say in his supplication - then he mentioned it, with the like of it."
"2205","Another narration. 2372 - The ascetic Abu al-Ma'ali Muhammad ibn Safi ibn Abdullah al-Naqqash informed us - at Baghdad - that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Muqri - known as al-Mazrafi - informed them: al-Sharif Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Muhtadi Billah narrated to us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Dust informed us; Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi narrated to us; Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah - ha."
"2206","2373 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Nasr al-Tammar narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate, saying: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, and a deed that is not raised, and a heart that does not humble itself, and a saying that is not heard. The wording is one."
"2207","2374 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Isbahani informed us; Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us; Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, and a deed that is not raised, and a heart that does not humble itself, and a supplication that is not heard. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad, from Bahz and Abu Kamil, from Hammad."
"2208","Another narration. 2375 - Abu Isma'il Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Mashadhah informed us - at Isfahan - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Mustamli informed them: Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Adib informed us; Abu Sa'id Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Razi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ayyub al-Razi informed us; Muslim ibn Ibrahim informed us; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The pommel of the sword of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was of silver. Abu Dawud narrated it, from Muslim ibn Ibrahim, from Jarir. And he narrated it from Ibn Muthanna, from Mu'adh ibn Hisham, from his father, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, who said: it was. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it, from Ibn Bashshar, from Wahb ibn Jarir, from his father, and said: A hasan gharib hadith; and thus Hammam narrated, from Qatadah, from Anas. And al-Nasa'i narrated it, from Abu Dawud, from Amr ibn Asim, from Hammam, and Jarir, from Qatadah, from Anas. Al-Nasa'i said: This is a munkar hadith; the correct version is Qatadah, from Sa'id. He said: None narrated it from Hammam except Amr ibn Asim. And al-Darimi brought it, from Abu al-Nu'man, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Qatadah, from Anas, and said: Hisham al-Dastuwai differed from him, narrating from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and people claimed that it is the preserved one."
"2209","Another narration. 2376 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Musa narrated to us; Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Complete the front row; if there is any shortfall, let it be in the last one."
"2210","2377 - And Abu Ali ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Ali al-Nasri informed us - at Baghdad - that the judge Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them: Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Isa al-Baqillani informed us; Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i informed us; Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Basri narrated to us; Abu Asim narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Straighten the rows; if there is any shortfall, it should be in the last one."
"2211","2378 - And Abu al-Mafakhir Uthman ibn Mahmud ibn Abi Bakr - known as Habbawayh - informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Baghban informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us; Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khurshid informed us by his word; Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Isma'il al-Mahamili narrated to us; Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us; al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Complete the first row; if there is any shortfall, then the last one."
"2212","2379 - And Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali - known as Ibn al-Ma'tush - informed us - at Baghdad - that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad informed us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad informed us; my father narrated to me; Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us; Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Complete the first row, then the one that follows it; if there is any deficiency, let it be in the last row. And Imam Ahmad narrated it - also - from Abd al-Wahhab, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas. And he narrated it from Hasan ibn Musa, from Shayban, from Qatadah, as it was said. Abu Dawud narrated it, from Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Anbari, from Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata. And al-Nasa'i narrated it, from Isma'il ibn Mas'ud, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Sa'id."
"2213","2380 - And Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sa'd al-Thaqafi informed us - by reading to him, while we listened - at Damascus - it was said to him: Your grandfather, the Hafiz Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl, informed you - by reading to him while you listened, and he acknowledged it: Asim ibn al-Hasan informed us - at Baghdad - Abu Umar ibn Mahdi informed us; Abdullah ibn Ishaq al-Misri narrated to us; Bakkar ibn Qutaybah narrated to us; Abu Asim al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Straighten the first and second rows; if there is any shortfall, let it be in the last one."
"2214","In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; praise be to Allah alone, and may Allah send blessings upon Muhammad and his family and grant him abundant peace. And from the chapter of Qatadah, from Anas. 2381 - Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Sa'd al-Thaqafi al-Isbahani informed us - at Damascus - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us; Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us; Abu Mas'ud Ahmad ibn al-Furat al-Razi informed us; Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped on the top of his foot because of a pain he had."
"2215","2382 - And Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Majd al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram on the top of the foot because of a pain he had."
"2216","2383 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur al-Khabbaz informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us; Muhammad - he is Ibn Mahdi - narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram on the top of the foot because of a pain he had."
"2217","2384 - And Abu Muslim Hisham ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us - at Isfahan - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us; Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Makhladi informed us; Abu al-Abbas al-Sarraj informed us; Muhammad ibn Nafi' and Muhammad ibn Sahl ibn Askar narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped while in ihram on the top of the foot because of a sprain he had. Abu Dawud al-Sijistani brought it, from Ahmad ibn Hanbal. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it in al-Shama'il, from Ishaq ibn Mansur. And al-Nasa'i brought it, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim. And Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, from Ishaq ibn Ibrahim - all of them - from Abd al-Razzaq."
"2218","Another narration. 2385 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us; Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be cupped on the two jugular veins and the upper back."
"2219","2386 - And Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us; Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us; Abu Mas'ud Ahmad ibn al-Furat al-Razi narrated to us; Wahb ibn Jarir informed us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Anas - ha."
"2220","2387 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped on the two jugular veins and the upper back. The wording is one, except that Zuhayr said: upon the two jugular veins."
"2221","2388 - And Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us - at Baghdad - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Bahz narrated to me; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, saying: I heard Qatadah narrating from Anas, who said: he was - ha."
"2222","2389 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us; Abu Ali Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Sawwaf informed us; Abu Ali Bishr ibn Musa ibn Salih al-Anbari narrated to us; Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Musa al-Ashyab narrated to us, and I heard Jarir ibn Hazim, saying: I heard Qatadah; Anas ibn Malik narrated to us: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be cupped three times, twice - ha."
"2223","2390 - And Umar ibn Sa'd Allah ibn Ibrahim ibn Dabbus al-Bayyi' informed us - at Baghdad, and our Shaykh Abu Bakr Abd al-Razzaq ibn Abd al-Qadir al-Jili - may Allah have mercy on him - pointed me to him - that Abu al-Qasim Yahya ibn Thabit ibn Bundar informed them: my father informed us; Abu Mansur Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Imran - known as Ibn al-Sawwaq - informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ja'far ibn Hamdan ibn Malik al-Qati'i informed us; Abu Muslim Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Muslim al-Basri informed us; Abu al-Nu'man Arim narrated to us, and Sulayman ibn Harb - both said: Jarir narrated to us, from Qatadah, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to be cupped twice on the two jugular veins and once on the upper back. The wording of al-Ashyab, Arim and Sulayman. And Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hanbal said: he is cupped three times, once on his upper back and twice on the two jugular veins."
"2224","Another narration. 2391 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us; Ahmad al-Dawraqi narrated to us; Mubashshir ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, who said: Qatadah narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be dissension and division in my nation; a people who speak well and act badly, reciting the Qur'an without it passing beyond their collarbones, passing out of the religion as the arrow passes out of the game, then not returning to it until it returns to its notch. They are the worst of creation; blessed is he who kills them, and blessed is he whom they kill. They call to the Book of Allah while having nothing to do with it; whoever fights them is closer to Allah than they are. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is their mark? He said: Shaving the head."
"2225","2392 - And Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us; al-Awza'i narrated to us; Qatadah narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be dissension and division in my nation; a people who speak well and act badly, reciting the Qur'an without it passing beyond their collarbones; one of you would regard his prayer as insignificant compared to their prayer and his fasting compared to their fasting; they pass out of the religion as the arrow passes out of the game, then do not return until it returns to its notches; the worst of creation; blessed is he who kills them and whom they kill. They call to the Book of Allah while having nothing to do with it; whoever fights them is closer to Allah than they are. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is their mark? He said: Shaving the head. Imam Ahmad said: And Abu al-Mughirah narrated it to us, from Anas, from Abu Sa'id, then he retracted."
"2226","2393 - And Abdullah said: My father narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us; Rabah narrated to us; Ma'mar narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be dissension and division in my nation; there will emerge from them a people reciting the Qur'an without it passing beyond their collarbones; their mark is shaving and close-cropping the hair. When you see them, put them to death."
"2227","2394 - And Abu Sadiq al-Hasan ibn Yahya ibn al-Husayn ibn Sabbah al-Misri informed us - at Damascus - that Abdullah ibn Rifa'ah al-Sa'di informed them: Ali ibn al-Hasan al-Khila'i informed us; Abu al-Faraj Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Nahwi informed us - by reading to him: Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Qaysarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Sahl al-Khara'iti narrated to us; Ali ibn Harb narrated to us; Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among you there are a people who worship so devoutly that people are amazed and they are amazed with themselves, passing out of the religion as the arrow passes out of the game. Imam Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it in his Musnad, from Isa ibn Yunus, from al-Awza'i, from Qatadah, from Anas, and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri. And Abu Dawud narrated it, from Nasr ibn Asim al-Antaki, from al-Walid ibn Muslim, and Mubashshir ibn Isma'il, from al-Awza'i; and from al-Hasan ibn Ali, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah. And the like of it was narrated in the Sahih, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri."
"2228","Another narration. 2395 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Adib al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Minhal Abu Abdullah al-Darir narrated to us; Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were invited to a trotter I would accept, and if it were gifted to me I would accept it."
"2229","2396 - And A'ishah bint Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us - at Isfahan - that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Bakr Thawwab ibn Yazid ibn Thawwab al-Mawsili narrated to us in the Sacred Mosque; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Muthanna - the maternal uncle of Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili - narrated to us; Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I were invited to a trotter I would accept, and if a foreleg were gifted to me I would accept it."
"2230","2397 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us, that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us; Abdullah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Rawh and Abd al-Wahhab said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2231","2398 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il ibn Muhammad al-Sayrafi informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah informed us; Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad and al-Abbas ibn al-Walid said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us; Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a trotter were gifted to me I would accept it. Al-Tirmidhi brought it in al-Ahkam with the like of it, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi', from Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal, from Sa'id, and said: A hasan sahih hadith. It has a witness in al-Bukhari from the hadith of Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah."
"2232","Another narration. 2399 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Abdullah ibn Mandah informed us; my father Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Mandah narrated to us - by dictation from his wording - Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us; Uthman ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us; al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Marzuq Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The one who strives in the path of Allah - mighty and majestic - is under My guarantee: if I take his soul, I shall admit him into Paradise, and if I return him, I shall return him with reward and spoils. Al-Tirmidhi brought it, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah Bazi', from Mu'tamir, with his chain, with the like of it - and said: A hasan sahih hadith. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah."
"2233","Another narration. 2400 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them - by reading to him: the teacher Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muqri al-Khabbazi narrated to us; Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn Ali al-Khuza'i narrated to us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Qattan informed us; Abu al-Azhar Ahmad ibn al-Azhar narrated to us - ha. 2401 - And Abu Ali Diya ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi Ali ibn al-Khurayf informed us - at Baghdad - that the judge Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them: Ali ibn Ibrahim ibn Isa al-Baqillani informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Isma'il ibn al-Abbas al-Warraq narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Zanjawayh narrated to us - both said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are four: Maryam the daughter of Imran, Asiyah the daughter of Muzahim, Khadijah the daughter of Khuwaylid, and Fatimah the daughter of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The wording of Ibn Zanjawayh. And Abu al-Azhar said: with four: Maryam the daughter of Imran, and Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh - and the rest of it is the like thereof."
"2234","2402 - And al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us - at Baghdad - that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me - ha. 2403 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us - both said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds: Maryam the daughter of Imran, Khadijah the daughter of Khuwaylid, Fatimah the daughter of Muhammad, and Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh. Al-Tirmidhi brought it, from Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Zanjawayh, from Abd al-Razzaq, and said: A sahih hadith. And it has already come in the narration of Thabit, from Anas."
"2235","Another narration. 2404 - The Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Saffar informed us - at Naysabur - that Abu Bakr Wajih ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us; Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Makhladi informed us; Abu al-Abbas al-Sarraj informed us; Muhammad ibn Rafi' narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought al-Buraq on the night he was taken by night, saddled and bridled, for him to ride, but it became difficult for him, so Jibril said to it: What makes you do this? By Allah, none has ever ridden you more honored to Allah than him. He said: So it broke into sweat."
"2236","2405 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Abu al-Qasim Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Muhammad ibn Mahdi Abu Abdullah al-Ubulli narrated to us - at Basra: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought al-Buraq on the night he was taken by night, saddled and bridled, but it became difficult for him, so Jibril (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to it: Is it with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that you do this? None has ridden you more honored to Allah than him. He said: So al-Buraq broke into sweat. Imam Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hanbal, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Naysaburi, Ishaq ibn Abi Isra'il, Abd ibn Humayd, and Hashim ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Mukharrimi - all of them - narrated it from Abd al-Razzaq. And al-Tirmidhi brought it, from Ishaq ibn Mansur, from Abd al-Razzaq, and said: A gharib hadith; we know it only from the hadith of Abd al-Razzaq. I say: Perhaps he meant from Ma'mar, for it has been narrated from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah."
"2237","2406 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim informed us - by my reading to him at Isfahan - I said to him: Abu al-Khayr Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed you - by reading to him while you listened: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Dhakwani informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Hashim narrated to us; Mu'alla ibn Mahdi narrated to us; al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought al-Buraq but it became difficult for him, so Jibril said: No human has ridden you more honored to Allah than him, so it broke into sweat."
"2238","Another narration. 2407 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Isbahani informed us; Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us; Isma'il ibn Abdullah Sammuyah narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Bishr narrated to us; al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded with the Pledge of Ridwan, Uthman - may Allah be pleased with him - had been sent by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the people of Makkah, so the people pledged allegiance, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Uthman is engaged in the need of Allah and His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he struck one of his hands upon the other, and the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on behalf of Uthman was better than their own hands for themselves. Al-Tirmidhi brought it, from Abu Zur'ah al-Razi, from al-Hasan ibn Bishr, and said: A hasan gharib sahih hadith. I say: And al-Hakam has been criticized by some of them."
"2239","Another narration. 2408 - Abu Tammam Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Hasan - known as Sirhank at Isfahan - informed us, that his maternal grandfather Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Musa informed them: the judge Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us; al-Hasan ibn Ali - he is Ibn Ahmad ibn Sulaym - narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hamadhani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Hamadhani narrated to us; Ali ibn Abi Bakr al-Asfadni al-Razi narrated to us; Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said."
"2240","2409 - And Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi al-Mu'addib informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad - known as Kulli - informed them: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Jurjani informed us; the judge Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Assal informed us; Abu Quraysh Muhammad ibn Jum'ah ibn Khalaf al-Quhistani narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Abd al-Malik al-Asadi narrated to us; Ali ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from Hammam, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is called to account will be punished. The wording of both is one."
"2241","2410 - And the Imam Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Silafi al-Hafiz informed us - by ijazah - that the judge Abu al-Fath Isma'il ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad al-Maliki informed them - at Qazwin - saying: I heard Abu Ya'la al-Khalil ibn Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Khalili al-Hafiz - by dictation: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Khayran al-Shaybani narrated to me - at Hamadhan: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi al-Hinna informed us; Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Asadi narrated to us; Ali ibn Abi Bakr al-Asfadni al-Razi narrated to us; Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has his reckoning scrutinized will perish. Abu Ya'la al-Khalili said: None narrated it except Muhammad ibn Ubayd, from Ali ibn Abi Bakr. Al-Tirmidhi brought it, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Abd al-Malik al-Asadi al-Hamadhani - and said: A gharib hadith; we know it from the hadith of Qatadah only through this route. I say: And Ali al-Asfadni al-Kindi al-Razi was deemed trustworthy by Abu Hatim al-Razi. It has a witness in the Sahihayn from the hadith of Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from A'ishah."
"2242","Another narration. 2411 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them - by reading to her while they listened: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us; Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Dabari narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: When the bier of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh was carried, the hypocrites said: How light his bier is, because of the judgment he passed concerning Banu Qurayzah. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: No; rather, the angels are carrying him."
"2243","2412 - And Abu Rawh Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us - there - that Abu al-Mahasin As'ad ibn Ziyad informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Dawudi informed us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hammuyah informed us; Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym informed us; Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ma'mar - ha. 2413 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, saying: Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: When the bier of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh was carried, the hypocrites said: How light his bier is, and that was because of his judgment concerning Banu Qurayzah. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: The angels were carrying him. The wording of both is one."
"2244","2414 - And Abd al-Mu'izz ibn Muhammad al-Sufi informed us - at Herat - that Abu al-Qasim Tamim ibn Abi Sa'id ibn Abi al-Abbas al-Jurjani informed them: Abu Sa'd Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Janzarudhi informed us; Abu Sa'id Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn al-Abbas al-Tamimi al-Basri informed us; Abu Labid Muhammad ibn Idris al-Sami al-Sarakhsi informed us; Muhammad ibn Tha'labah - he is Ibn Sawa al-Kufi - narrated to us; my uncle - meaning Muhammad ibn Sawa - narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said while the bier of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh lay placed: The Throne shook at the death of Sa'd. Then the hypocrites spoke ill of his bier, saying: How light it is. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: The angels are carrying him along with them. As for the mention of the shaking of the Throne at the death of Sa'd, Muslim narrated it from the narration of Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas. Al-Tirmidhi brought it, from Abd ibn Humayd, from Abd al-Razzaq, and said: A sahih gharib hadith. And Ibn Hibban brought it in his book, from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Allaf, from Muhammad ibn Sawa, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah; and Allah knows best whether it is from Sa'id or Shu'bah."
"2245","Another narration. 2415 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Harun ibn Ma'ruf narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to me - ha. 2416 - And Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informed them: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us; Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us; Abdullah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Harun - he is Ibn Ma'ruf - narrated to us. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And I heard it myself from Harun more than once: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to me, that he heard Qatadah ibn Di'amah: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having performed ablution but leaving upon his foot a spot the size of a fingernail, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go back and perfect your ablution. The wording is one, except Abu Ya'la did not say: to him."
"2246","2417 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Harith informed them - while he was present: Abu Ahmad Abd al-Malik ibn al-Husayn al-Attar al-Muqri narrated to us; Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mahdi al-Hafiz narrated to us; Abd al-Malik ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Daqqaq narrated to us; Yunus ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us; Ibn Wahb informed us, from Jarir ibn Hazim: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having left a spot the size of a fingernail upon his foot, so he said: Go back and perfect your ablution. Abu Dawud brought it in his Sunan, from Harun ibn Ma'ruf. And Ibn Majah brought it, from Harmalah ibn Yahya - both of them - from Ibn Wahb. And Abu Dawud said: This hadith is not well known; none narrated it except Ibn Wahb. And he said: Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us; Hammad narrated to us; Yunus and Humayd informed us, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the meaning of the hadith of Qatadah. And Abu al-Hasan al-Daraqutni narrated it, from Abu Bakr al-Naysaburi, from Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb, from his uncle, and said: Jarir ibn Hazim alone narrated it, and he is trustworthy, and none narrated it from him except Ibn Wahb."
"2247","Another narration. 2418 - My maternal uncle, the jurist, the Imam Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us, that Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Ahmad ibn Salman informed them - at Baghdad: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us; al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shadhan informed us; Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn Darastawayh informed us; Ya'qub ibn Sufyan narrated to us; Abu Zafar Abd al-Salam ibn Mutahhar narrated to us; Musa ibn Khalaf narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That I sit with a people remembering Allah - mighty and majestic - after the morning prayer until the sun rises is dearer to me than freeing four from the children of Isma'il; and that I sit with a people remembering Allah, exalted, from the afternoon prayer until the sun sets is dearer to me than freeing four. Abu Dawud brought it in the Book of Knowledge, from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Abd al-Salam: Musa - a group praised him, while others criticized him."
"2248","2419 - And Abu Muslim al-Mu'ayyad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn al-Ikhwah informed us - at Isfahan - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Bakr Ya'qub ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Sayrafi informed us; Abu Amr al-Muzani al-Hafiz - by dictation - he is Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Buhayri - informed us: Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Musa informed us; Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Yahya ibn Durays al-Bajali narrated to us; Abd al-Salam ibn Mutahhar informed us; Musa ibn Khalaf narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That I sit with a people remembering Allah - mighty and majestic - from the morning prayer until the sun rises is dearer to me than freeing four necks."
"2249","Another narration. 2420 - Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Sa'id ibn al-Husayn ibn Shunayf - the trustee at Dar al-Qazz in Baghdad - informed us, that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them: the judge Abu Ya'la Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Farra informed us; Muhammad ibn Abdullah, the nephew of Yahya, informed us; Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi informed us; Abu Rawh Muhammad ibn Ziyad ibn Farwah al-Baladi narrated to us; Abu Shihab - whose name is Abd Rabbih ibn Nafi' al-Hannat - narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when death came to him was: Prayer, and what your right hands possess, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to gurgle it in his chest, with his tongue barely uttering it. And Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah al-Taymi narrated it."
"2250","2421 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad informed us; Ali ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The generality of the bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Prayer, prayer, and what your right hands possess, until he began to gurgle it in his chest, with his tongue barely uttering it. And Jarir ibn Hazim narrated it from him."
"2251","2422 - Abu al-Raja Abd al-Hadi ibn Hamad ibn Ali al-Hamadhani informed us - there - that Abu al-Fadl Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad ibn al-Ikhwah informed them: al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Talhah informed us; Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Mahdi informed us; the judge al-Husayn ibn Isma'il al-Mahamili informed us; Yusuf ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us; Jarir narrated to us; Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The last bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he gurgled it in his chest, his tongue barely uttering it, was: Prayer; fear Allah regarding what your right hands possess. And Mu'tamir narrated it from his father."
"2252","2423 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Abu al-Ash'ath narrated to us; al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, saying: I heard my father narrating from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The generality of the bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when death came to him was: Prayer, and what your right hands possess, until he began to gurgle it - or gurgle with it - in his chest, with his tongue not uttering it. Ibn Majah brought it, from Abu al-Ash'ath Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam."
"2253","2424 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us, that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them - while he was present: Muhammad ibn Shadhan informed us; Abdullah al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Asim ibn al-Nadr narrated to us; Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard my father narrating, saying: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The generality of the bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when death came to him was: Prayer, and what your right hands possess, until his chest began to gurgle with it, with his tongue not uttering it. And Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated it, from al-Taymi."
"2254","2425 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah informed them: al-Hasan informed us; Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us; al-Taymi narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The generality of the bequest of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when death came to him was: Prayer, and what your right hands possess, until the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to gurgle it in his chest, with his tongue barely uttering it. And Abthar ibn al-Qasim, Isa ibn Yunus, Shuja' ibn al-Walid, and Sufyan al-Thawri also narrated it from him. Al-Daraqutni said: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah and Abu Awanah narrated it, from Qatadah, from Safinah, from Umm Salamah. And Hammam said: from Qatadah, from Abu al-Khalil, from Safinah, from Umm Salamah. He said: And this is more correct, and Allah knows best."
"2255","Another narration. 2426 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Ja'far ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Thaqafi informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Bakr ibn Ahmad ibn Sa'dawayh al-Tahi al-Muqri al-Basri narrated to us; Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us; Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from his brother Khalid ibn Qays, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Bakr ibn Wa'il: From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Bakr ibn Wa'il: Embrace Islam and you shall be safe. None read it except a man from Banu Dubay'ah, so they are called Banu al-Katib."
"2256","2427 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur al-Khabbaz informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us; Nuh narrated to us, from his brother Khalid ibn Qays, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Bakr ibn Wa'il: Embrace Islam and you shall be safe. None was found who could read it except a man from Banu Dubay'ah, so they are called Banu al-Katib. Muslim has brought two hadiths with this chain."
"2257","Another narration. 2428 - Abu Shuja' Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad ibn Abi al-Ma'ali - known as Ibn al-Ma'ruf - the reciter, the tailor - at Baghdad - informed us, that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Ahmad al-Khayyat informed them: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqur informed us; Muhammad ibn Abdullah, the nephew of Mimi, informed us; Abdullah ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Abu Bakr narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the adhan of Bilal deceive you regarding your sahur, for there is something in his sight."
"2258","2429 - And Abu al-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us - in the western quarter of Baghdad - that Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informed them: Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us; Abu Bakr al-Qati'i informed us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me - ha. 2430 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Abdullah al-Adib al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Abu Bakr ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Abu Bakr narrated to us; both said: Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the adhan of Bilal prevent you from sahur, for there is something in his sight. The wording of both is one, except that Abu Bakr said: in his sight is something."
"2259","2431 - And Abu Tahir Barakat ibn Ibrahim ibn Tahir al-Qurashi informed us - at Damascus - that Abd al-Karim ibn Hamzah ibn al-Khadir informed them: Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Uthman al-Azdi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Abbas al-Ikhmimi informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Abbas - he is Ibn al-Faraj - narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ali - he is Ibn Muhriz - narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the adhan of Bilal prevent you, for there is something in his sight. Muslim narrated, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Muhammad ibn Bishr, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas, two hadiths. This hadith has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Ibn Mas'ud and Samurah ibn Jundub with the like of it, but they did not mention: for there is something in his sight."
"2260","Another narration. 2432 - Abu al-Muzaffar Abd al-Rahim ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Sam'ani al-Marwazi informed us - there - that Abu al-As'ad Hibat al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Abd al-Karim ibn Hawazin informed them: Abd al-Karim ibn Hawazin informed us; al-Khaffaf informed us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Sarraj informed us; Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrahim al-Azdi narrated to us; Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us; Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Join your rows together, bring them close to one another, and align the necks; by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I see Satan entering through the gaps in the row."
"2261","2433 - And Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to us; Affan narrated to us; Aban narrated to us; Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Join your rows together, bring them close to one another, and align the necks; by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I see Satan entering through the gaps in the row like a small lamb."
"2262","2434 - And Imam Ahmad said - also: Aswad narrated to us; Aban narrated to us; Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Join your rows together, bring them close to one another, and align the necks; by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I see the devils entering through the gaps in the row like small lambs. And Sa'id narrated it from Qatadah."
"2263","2435 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us; Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Nasih informed us; Musa ibn Harun ibn Abdullah al-Qazzaz narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Tha'labah ibn Sawa narrated to us; my uncle Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated to us; Sa'id narrated to us; Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Join your rows together, bring them close to one another, and align the shoulders and necks; by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I see Satan slipping through behind the rows like a small lamb."
"2264","2436 - And Abu Rashid Habib ibn Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Sufi informed us - by ijazah - that Ghanim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Burji informed them: Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Isbahani informed us; Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Sawwaf informed us; Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Azdi narrated to us; Muslim narrated to us; Aban narrated to us; Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Join your rows together, bring them close to one another, and align the necks; by the One in whose soul is in His hand, I see Satan entering through the gaps in the row like a small lamb. Abu Dawud brought it, from Muslim ibn Ibrahim. And al-Nasa'i brought it, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak, from Abu Hisham al-Makhzumi, from Aban. And Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban al-Busti narrated it, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzaymah, from Muhammad ibn Ma'mar, from Muslim ibn Ibrahim."
"2265","Another narration. 2437 - Abu Tahir Barakat ibn Ibrahim ibn Tahir al-Khushu'i informed us - at Damascus - that Abd al-Karim ibn Hamzah ibn al-Khadir al-Sulami informed them: Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Makki ibn Uthman al-Azdi al-Misri informed us; Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Abbas al-Akhmimi informed us; Muhammad ibn Isma'il - he is Ibn al-Faraj - narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ali - he is Ibn Muhriz - narrated to us; Muhammad - he is Ibn Bishr - narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which prayer is most excellent? He said: Lengthy standing in devotion. Ja'far ibn Awn followed him, from Sa'id."
"2266","2438 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi informed us - at Baghdad - that Abu Mansur Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Qazzaz informed them: al-Sharif Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Muhtadi Billah informed them; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Dust informed us; Isma'il ibn al-Abbas narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Hazim narrated to us; Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the most excellent prayer. He said: Lengthy standing in devotion."
"2267","2439 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Sa'd Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Sa'd al-Baghdadi, then al-Isbahani, informed them: Asim ibn al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Asim informed us; Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Mahdi informed us; Muhammad ibn Makhlad al-Duri informed us; Isma'il ibn Abi al-Harith narrated to us; Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us; Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which prayer is most excellent? He said: Lengthy standing in devotion. And Muslim has the like of it from the hadith of Jabir ibn Abdullah."
"2268","Another narration. 2440 - Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar ibn al-Saffar informed us - at Naysabur - that Wajih ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them: Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Muhammad al-Azhari informed us; Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Makhladi informed us; Abu Hamid - he is Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Hamid ibn Mansur al-Tusi - informed us; Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to me, from al-Hajjaj - he is Ibn al-Hajjaj - from Qatadah, from Anas, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: O Living, O Sustainer. Al-Nasa'i brought it, from Ahmad ibn Hafs, from his father."
"2269","2441 - And Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Hamzah ibn Abi Jamil al-Qurashi informed us - at Damascus - that Ma'ali ibn Hibat Allah al-Taghlibi informed them: Sahl ibn Bishr al-Isfarayini informed us; Ali ibn Munir al-Khallal informed us; Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Naysaburi informed us; Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Nasa'i informed us; Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us; Hafs narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim narrated to me, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: O Living, O Sustainer. Al-Nasa'i narrated it likewise also."
"2270","2442 - And Mu'awiyah ibn Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us - by permission - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Musa ibn Harun narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: O Living, O Sustainer. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Qatadah except al-Hajjaj; Ibrahim ibn Tahman alone narrated it."
"2271","Another narration, its meaning is in Sahih Muslim. 2443 - Abu Shuja' Muhammad ibn Abi Muhammad ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Muqri al-Khayyat informed us - at Baghdad - that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Ahmad al-Khayyat informed them: Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Naqur informed us; Muhammad ibn Abdullah, the nephew of Mimi, informed us; Abdullah - he is Ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi - narrated to us; Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us; Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from his brother Khalid ibn Qays, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, how many prayers has Allah obligated upon His servants? He said: Five prayers. He said: Is there anything before or after them? He said: Allah - mighty and majestic - obligated upon His servants five prayers. He said: Is there anything before or after them? He said: Allah obligated upon His servants five prayers. Then the man swore by Allah that he would neither add to them nor fall short, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he is truthful, he shall enter Paradise."
"2272","2444 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim al-Khabbaz informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us; Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us; Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from his brother Khalid ibn Qays, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, how many prayers has Allah obligated upon His servants? He said: Five prayers. He said: Is there anything before or after them? He said: Allah obligated upon His servants five prayers. He said: Is there anything before or after them? He said: Allah obligated upon His servants five prayers. Then the man swore he would neither add to them nor fall short, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he is truthful, he shall enter Paradise. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad, from Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik. And al-Nasa'i brought it in his Sunan, from Qutaybah ibn Sa'id - both of them - from Nuh ibn Qays, with the like of it. And Abu al-Hasan al-Daraqutni narrated it in his book, from Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Baghawi. And Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban brought it in his book, from Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Imran al-Jurjani, from Nasr. Abu al-Qasim al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Qatadah except Khalid ibn Qays; Nuh ibn Qays alone narrated it, and Allah knows best. Except that this hadith has come in Sahih Muslim close to it, from the hadith of Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, from Thabit, from Anas, who said: We were forbidden from asking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about anything, so it used to please us that an intelligent man from the desert folk would come and ask him while we listened. Then a man from the desert folk came and said: O Muhammad, your messenger came to us - the hadith."
"2273","Another narration. 2445 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us; Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan informed us - ha. 2446 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us - also - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us - both said: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Nafi' ibn Khalid al-Tahi narrated to us; Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Qays, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection as though it were a black-and-white ram, and it will be made to stand between Paradise and the Fire. Then it will be called out: O people of Paradise. And they will say: At Your service, our Lord, and ready to serve You. He said: Then it will be said to them: Do you recognize this? And they will say: This is death. Then it will be slaughtered as the sheep is slaughtered, so these will be secure, and the hope of those will be cut off. The wording of Ibn al-Muqri. And in the narration of Ibn Hamdan: Then a caller will call out; and in it: Do you recognize this? They said: Yes, this is death; and the rest of it is the like thereof."
"2274","2447 - And Abu Talib al-Khadir ibn Hibat Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Ali ibn Tawus informed us - at Damascus, more than once - that Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn al-Sulami al-Mawazini informed them, saying: Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn Abi Nasr informed us, saying: the judge Yusuf ibn al-Qasim ibn Yusuf al-Mayyanji informed us, saying: Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us; Nafi' ibn Khalid al-Tahi narrated to us; Nuh ibn Qays narrated to us; Khalid ibn Qays narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection as though it were a black-and-white ram, and it will be made to stand between Paradise and the Fire. Then a caller will call out: O people of Paradise. And they will say: At Your service, our Lord, and ready to serve You. He said: Then it will be said to them: Do you recognize this? He said: And they will say: Yes, our Lord, this is death. Then it will be slaughtered as the sheep is slaughtered, so these will be secure, and the hope of those will be cut off. And the like of it has been narrated in the Sahih from the hadith of Abdullah ibn Umar and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri."
"2275","Another narration. 2448 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abi Dharr al-Salkani informed them: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim informed us; Abu Bakr Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us; Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard my father narrating, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I turn to Allah in repentance seventy times a day."
"2276","2449 - And Abu al-Qasim Mahmud ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn al-Fadl - known as al-Haddad - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us - at Isfahan - that Mas'ud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us; Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Khurshidh informed us by his word; Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Isma'il al-Mahamili narrated to us; Abu al-Ash'ath narrated to us; al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: I heard my father narrating, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I turn in repentance in a day seventy times."
"2277","2450 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us; Mu'tamir narrated to us, saying: I heard my father narrating, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I turn in repentance in a day seventy times. Ibn Majah brought it, from Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam."
"2278","2451 - And this Zahir informed us, that Abu Abdullah al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Huraym - he is Ibn Abd al-A'la - narrated to us; Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: I turn in repentance in a day seventy times. Ibn Hibban brought it in his book, from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Huraym."
"2279","2452 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - while he was present: Abu Nu'aym informed us; Abu Muslim Muhammad ibn Ma'mar ibn Nasih al-A'la informed us; Musa ibn Harun ibn Abdullah ibn Mirqab al-Qazzaz narrated to us; Asim ibn al-Nadr al-Ahwal narrated to us; Mu'tamir narrated to us, saying: I heard my father; Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to say: I turn in repentance in a day seventy times."
"2280","2453 - And my maternal uncle, the Imam, the scholar Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudamah al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us, that Abu al-Fath Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi ibn Sulayman informed them: Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Khayrun informed us; al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shadhan informed us; Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn Darastawayh informed us; Ya'qub ibn Sufyan al-Basawi narrated to us; Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us; al-Mu'tamir narrated to us, saying: I heard my father; Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: I turn in repentance in a day seventy times. And Imran narrated it from Qatadah."
"2281","2454 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present: Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us; Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us; Isma'il ibn Abdullah narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us; Imran narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I seek Allah's forgiveness in a day seventy times. And al-Bukhari narrated the like of it from the hadith of Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah."
"2282","Another narration. 2455 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us; Abu Ali al-Sawwaf narrated to us; Bishr ibn Musa al-Asadi narrated to us; Affan narrated to us - meaning from Aban - from Qatadah - ha. 2456 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Zuhayr narrated to us; Affan narrated to us; Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us; Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never had bread and meat come together for his lunch and dinner except in times of scarcity. And Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated it from Aban."
"2283","2457 - My maternal uncle, the Imam, the jurist Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us, that Shuhdah bint Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Ibari informed them: Abu Ghalib Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Baqillani informed us; al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Shadhan informed us; Abu Sahl Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ziyad al-Qattan al-Mattuthi informed us; Abu Ishaq Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi narrated to us; Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us; Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never had bread and meat come together for his lunch or dinner except in times of scarcity. Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad, from Affan, with the like of it. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it, from al-Darimi, from Affan also."
"2284","Another narration. 2458 - Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Hamzah ibn Ali al-Sulami informed us - by reading to him while we listened - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad informed them - by ijazah: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Ali al-Maqdisi narrated to us - at Makkah: Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shu'ayb al-Nasa'i narrated to us - at al-Ramlah: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, exalted, will ask - ha."
"2285","2459 - And Ahmad ibn Hamzah al-Sulami informed us - also - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - by ijazah - and Yahya ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ghazzal informed them - by reading to him at Baghdad - saying: Hamad ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed us - both said: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Isbahani informed us; Abu Ahmad Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Jurjani narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Shirawayh narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us; my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas - ha."
"2286","2460 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Mustamli informed them: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kanjarudhi informed us; Abu Amr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan informed us; Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hanzali narrated to us; Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us; my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah will question every shepherd regarding what he was entrusted with, whether he preserved it or neglected it, until He will question a man regarding the members of his household. The wording is one, except that in the narration of Abdullah ibn Muhammad: or neglected. Al-Nasa'i brought it in his Sunan, from Ishaq, as we narrated it. It was said: None narrated it except Mu'adh from his father. And Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it in his book, from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Ishaq al-Hanzali. And he narrated right after it, from al-Hasan, from Ishaq, from Mu'adh, from his father, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Al-Daraqutni said: And the correct version is from Hisham, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, as mursal."
"2287","Another narration. 2461 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us, that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us; Abdullah ibn Ja'far ibn Ahmad ibn Faris informed us; Yunus ibn Habib narrated to us; Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us; Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Three men from among those before you went out seeking provisions for their families, when rain befell them, so they took shelter by a mountain, and a rock fell upon them. One of them said to the others: The trail has been effaced, the rock has fallen, and none knows your place except Allah - mighty and majestic - so call upon Allah with your most reliable deeds. One of them said: O Allah, if You know that I had two parents, and I used to milk for them in their vessel, and when I came to them while they were asleep, I would stand waiting until they woke, whenever they woke, disliking that drowsiness should stir in their heads, and when they woke they would drink; if You know that I did that only hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then relieve us. He said: So a third of the rock moved away. He said: And another said: O Allah, if You know that there was a woman who pleased me, but she refused to give herself to me until I offered her a reward, and when I took hold of her I left her to herself along with her reward; if You know that I did that only fearing Your punishment and hoping for Your mercy, then relieve us. He said: So another third moved away. And the third said: If You know that I hired a laborer to work for me for a day, and he worked, and when night came I gave him his wage but he disdained it and did not take it, so I took his wage and multiplied it for him, until it became much wealth; then he came to me seeking his wage, and I said: Take all of this, it is yours; and had I wished I would not have given him except his wage; if You know that I did that only hoping for Your mercy and fearing Your punishment, then relieve us. He said: So the last third moved away, and they went out walking."
"2288","2462 - And Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us; Ahmad ibn Ja'far al-Qati'i informed us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us; Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that three men from among the people of the past went forth seeking provisions for their families, when rain overtook them, so they entered a cave, and a rock, set apart, fell upon them, so that they saw no opening from it - and he mentioned the hadith at length with the like of it. 2463 - And Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: Abu Bahr narrated to us; Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - then he mentioned the like of it. And Imam Ahmad narrated it, from Bahz, from Abu Awanah, from Qatadah, from Anas: that three men - but he did not raise it. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Hatim said: I asked my father about a hadith narrated by Imran al-Qattan, from Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning the story of the cave, while Abu Awanah narrated it, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as marfu'. I said to my father: Which is correct? He said: Both hadiths are in my view sahih, because their wordings differ. My father said: Musaddad narrated to us; Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning the story of the cave. And this has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abdullah ibn Umar."
"2289","Another narration. 2464 - Abu Tahir Barakat ibn Ibrahim ibn Tahir al-Qurashi informed us - at Damascus - that Abu al-Husayn Ali ibn Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn ... informed them: Abu Nasr al-Husayn ibn Muhammad informed us. Al-Hasan ibn Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik."
"2290","2465 - And Umm Habibah A'ishah bint Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us - at Isfahan - that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu al-Futuh Mansur ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn al-Qasim informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali ibn Asim ibn Zadham informed us; Abdullah ibn Ibrahim al-Darir al-Qasri narrated to us - at Qasr Hubayrah: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: He is Allah, the One - equals a third of the Qur'an. The wording is one. Ibn Majah brought it, from al-Hasan al-Hulwani."
"2291","2466 - And Abu al-Tahir Mu'awiyah ibn Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us - in his book - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us; Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Hadrami narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us; Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say: He is Allah, the One - equals a third of the Qur'an. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Jarir ibn Hazim except Yazid ibn Harun. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and others."
"2292","Another narration. 2467 - My maternal uncle, the Imam, the scholar Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us, that Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Yusuf informed them: Abu Tahir Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Yusuf informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abdullah ibn Bishran informed us; the Hafiz Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad ibn Mahdi al-Daraqutni informed us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us, saying: Isa ibn Abi Harb narrated to me; Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us; Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, that a man stole a shield in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was valued at five dirhams, so he cut off his hand. And Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated it from Qatadah."
"2293","2468 - Abu Tahir Mu'awiyah ibn Ali ibn Mu'awiyah al-Sufi informed us - by ijazah - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them: Abu Nu'aym al-Isbahani informed us; Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Fahd al-Tarsi narrated to us; Abdullah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us; Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off the hand for a shield worth five dirhams. Al-Daraqutni said: Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad and Sa'id ibn Amir narrated it, from Ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off the hand. Others narrate it from Sa'id, that Abu Bakr cut off the hand. And Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated it, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Anas, as marfu' also. And likewise it was narrated from Amr ibn Marzuq, from Shu'bah; and the preserved version from Shu'bah is mawquf. And the correct version from Qatadah, from Anas, is: that Abu Bakr cut off the hand, not marfu'. I say: And Muhammad ibn Sulaym al-Rasibi narrated it, from Qatadah, from Anas, as marfu'."
"2294","Another narration. 2469 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi al-Darir - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Abu al-Qasim Ibrahim al-Khabbaz, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us; Muhammad - he is Ibn Mahdi - narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Messenger of Allah, when we are with you we see in ourselves what we love, but when we return to our families and mix with them we find ourselves changed. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you were to remain upon the state you are in when with me in solitude, the angels would shake hands with you until they shaded you with their wings before your eyes; but an hour and an hour. Al-Bukhari mentioned it in his Tarikh, saying: Amr ibn Marzuq said: from Imran, from Qatadah, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Hanzalah al-Usaydi, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Ma'mar said: from Qatadah, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with this. Musa narrated to me; Ghassan ibn Burzin narrated to us; Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This he mentioned in the biography of Hanzalah."
"2295","Another narration. 2470 - It was read to al-Amin Abu al-Majd al-Fadl ibn al-Husayn ibn Ibrahim ibn Sulayman al-Baniyasi - while we listened, at Damascus: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Husayn al-Sulami al-Mawazini informed you - by reading to him, and he acknowledged it: Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman ibn Abi Nasr informed us - by reading to him - saying: It was read to the judge Abu Bakr Yusuf ibn al-Qasim ibn Yusuf ibn Faris al-Mayyanji, saying: Abu Ya'la informed us; Muhammad ibn Zanjawayh Abu Bakr narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah curse the Jews; animal fat was forbidden to them, so they sold it and consumed its price."
"2296","2471 - And Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us - at Baghdad - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit and Qatadah, from Anas, who said: When wine was forbidden, he said: I was that day serving drink to them; I was serving eleven men. Then they commanded me and I poured it out, and the people poured out their vessels with what was in them, until the streets were nearly impassable because of its smell. Anas said: And their wine that day was nothing but unripe and ripe dates mixed together. He said: Then a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I had with me the wealth of an orphan, so I bought wine with it; will you permit me to sell it and return to the orphan his wealth? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah destroy the Jews; animal fat was forbidden to them, so they sold it and consumed its price. And he did not permit him to sell wine. From his statement: Then a man came - to the end - the two Shaykhs did not bring it in the Sahih, and Allah knows best."
"2297","2472 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali informed us; Muhammad ibn Mahdi and Abu Bakr said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar informed us, from Thabit and Qatadah and Aban - all of them - from Anas, who said: When wine was forbidden, he said: I was that day serving eleven men. He said: Then they commanded me and I poured it out, then the people poured out their vessels with what was in them, until the streets nearly became impassable because of its smell. Anas said: And their wine that day was nothing but unripe and ripe dates mixed together. Then a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I had with me the wealth of an orphan, so I bought wine; will you permit me to sell it and return to the orphan his wealth? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah destroy the Jews; animal fat was forbidden to them, so they sold it and consumed its price. And he did not permit him to sell wine. The wording of the hadith of Ibn Mahdi; and in the narration of Abu Bakr: So I bought wine with it; do you see that I may sell it? And in it: And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not permit him to sell wine. Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it in his Musnad, from Abd al-Razzaq, from Ma'mar, with the like of it. And it has a witness in the Sahihayn in the mention of the Jews, from the narration of Umar ibn al-Khattab - may Allah be pleased with him."
"2298","2473 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us; Ahmad ibn Bundar informed us; Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Azhar ibn Marwan narrated to us; Abd al-A'la narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when this verse - the verse of wine - was revealed: O people, Allah - mighty and majestic - has forbidden wine; so whoever has any of it with him, let him not sell it but pour it out."
"2299","Another narration. 2474 - Abu al-Qasim Hibat Allah ibn Ali ibn Su'ud ibn Thabit ibn Hashim al-Ansari al-Busiri informed us - at Fustat in Egypt - that Abu Ja'far Yahya ibn al-Mushrif ibn Ali ibn al-Khadir al-Tammar informed them: Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Sa'id ibn Ahmad ibn Nafis al-Muqri informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Bundar ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Bundar, the judge of Adhana - at Egypt - informed us, saying: Abu Tahir al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Fil al-Balisi informed us; Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us; Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us; Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never addressed us in a sermon except that he commanded us with charity and forbade us from mutilation."
"2300","2475 - And Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi informed us - at Baghdad - that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Muhammad al-Jawhari informed us; the judge al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Fahd al-Mawsili informed us, saying: Abu Ya'la al-Mawsili informed us; Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us; Abd al-Samad narrated to us; Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutilation. Al-Nasa'i brought it, from Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, from Abd al-Samad. And Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated it from Qatadah."
"2301","2476 - Abu Ali Abd al-Salam ibn Abi al-Khattab ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib informed us - at al-Harbiyyah - that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qazzaz informed them: Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Muslimah informed us; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us; Yahya - he is Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us; al-Qasim ibn Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated to us, saying: My father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah: Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutilation. Al-Daraqutni said, after mentioning the narration of Hisham: And he said: And Mu'adh ibn Hisham differed from them, narrating it from his father, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Hayyaj ibn Imran, from Samurah and Imran ibn al-Husayn. And likewise Hammam and Ma'mar narrated it from Qatadah. And he mentioned other than this. Then he said: And the closest of the two to correctness is what Mu'adh ibn Hisham said, from his father, with the corroboration of Ma'mar and Hammam, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Hayyaj ibn Imran, from Samurah and Imran ibn al-Husayn."
"2302","Another narration. 2477 - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Isma'il ibn al-Fadl ibn Ahmad al-Sarraj informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us; Abu al-Husayn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ma'dan al-Usfuri informed us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Rashid narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Zakariyya - from the people of Ubdas - narrated to us: Mu'tamir narrated to us, from his father - ha. 2478 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu al-Qasim Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Bazzar al-Baghdadi narrated to us - there: Ibrahim ibn Rashid al-Adami narrated to us; Ibrahim ibn Zakariyya - from the people of Ubdas - narrated to us; Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik - may Allah be pleased with him - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the bishop of Najran: Embrace Islam and you shall be safe. He said: I am a Muslim. He said: No; between you and that are three traits: your eating pork, your drinking wine, and your claiming another god along with Allah. The wording is that of Ibn al-Muqri, and the hadith of al-Usfuri ended at: three traits. Abu al-Hasan al-Daraqutni said: Ibrahim ibn Zakariyya narrated it, from Mu'tamir, from his father, from Qatadah, from Anas. And Ibn Wuhayb al-Ghazzi narrated it, from Ibn Abi al-Sari, from Mu'tamir, with this chain, adding in it: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: Then drinking the drink of thirsty camels. Others narrate it from Mu'tamir, from his father, from Qatadah, as mursal, without mentioning Anas in it. He said: And it is the correct one."
"2303","Another narration. 2479 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them - while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us; Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Ziyad al-Wasiti narrated to us; Shayban Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas - ha."
"2304","2480 - And Abu Hamid Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Thabit informed us - at Baghdad - that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Jawhari informed us; Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Nasr ibn Ahmad ibn Mukram al-Mu'addal informed us; Abdullah ibn Sulayman ibn al-Ash'ath narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasha'i narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Ziyad al-Thaqafi narrated to us; Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu Mu'awiyah al-Nahwi narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever learns knowledge to boast with it before the scholars, or to argue with it against the fools, or to turn the faces of people toward himself with it, shall be in the Fire. The wording is one, except that in the narration of al-Nasha'i: or to turn."
"2305","2481 - And Abu Hafs Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ma'mar al-Mu'addib informed us, that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Baqi al-Ansari informed them: Abd al-Samad ibn al-Ma'mun informed us; Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar al-Daraqutni informed us; Abu Hamid Muhammad ibn Harun al-Hadrami narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nasha'i narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Ziyad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi narrated to us; Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever learns knowledge to boast with it before the scholars, or to argue with it against the fools, or to turn the faces of people toward himself with it, shall be in the Fire. Al-Daraqutni said: Gharib from the hadith of Qatadah from Anas; Shayban ibn Abd al-Rahman alone narrated it from him, and none narrated it from him except Sulayman ibn Ziyad al-Thaqafi al-Wasiti."
"2306","Another narration. 2482 - Umm Habibah A'ishah bint Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us - at Isfahan - that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us; Abu Muhammad Abdullah ibn Yusuf al-Rassasi al-Mu'addib al-Isbahani narrated to us; Ahmad ibn Isam narrated to us; Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought forgiveness for the first row three times, and for the second row twice. Ahmad ibn Isam said: So I mentioned this hadith to Abu Mas'ud, and he said: It is sahih."
"2307","Another narration. 2483 - Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us; Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: O people, fear your Lord - up to His statement: but the punishment of Allah is severe - was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was on a journey of his. So he raised his voice with it until his Companions gathered to him, and he said: Do you know what day this is? The day when Allah - mighty and majestic - will say to Adam: Rise and send forth a contingent to the Fire: from every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire, and one to Paradise. That weighed heavily upon the Muslims, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be steadfast, draw near, and rejoice; by the One in whose hand is my soul, you among people are but like the mole on the flank of a camel, or like the mark on the foreleg of a beast. With you are two creations that were never in anything but that they multiplied it: Gog and Magog, and those who perished among the disbelieving jinn and men."
"2308","2484 - And Abu al-Izz ibn Mankidim ibn Muhammad al-Hamadhani informed us - there - that Nasr ibn al-Muzaffar ibn al-Husayn al-Barmaki informed them: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abi Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Mandah informed us; my father informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan narrated to us; Ahmad ibn al-Azhar ibn Mani' narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq ibn Hammam informed us; Ma'mar ibn Rashid informed us, from Qatadah and others, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: When O people, fear your Lord was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - then he mentioned the like of it."
"2309","2485 - And Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi informed us at Baghdad, that Abd al-Awwal ibn Isa informed them: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad informed us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Hammuyah informed us; Ibrahim ibn Khuzaym informed us; Abd ibn Humayd narrated to us; Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Ma'mar informed us, from Qatadah and Aban, from Anas ibn Malik - then he mentioned it, and in it: Allah, mighty and majestic, says to Adam, peace be upon him: O Adam, rise and send forth the contingent of the Fire. And Imam Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated it, from Abd al-Razzaq with his chain, with the like of it. This hadith has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri."
"2310","Another narration. 2486 - It was read to Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi - while we listened, at Damascus: Your grandfather, the Hafiz Abu al-Qasim Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl, informed you - by reading to him while you listened, and he acknowledged it: al-Sharif Abu Nasr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Zaynabi informed us - may Allah have mercy on him - at Baghdad: Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali ibn Khalaf informed us; Abdullah ibn Abi Dawud al-Sijistani narrated to us; Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us; Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from Anas - may Allah be pleased with him - from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Paradise and the Fire disputed. The Fire said: The tyrants and the arrogant shall enter me. And Paradise said: The poor and the wretched shall enter me. So Allah revealed to Paradise: You are My mercy; I shall settle in you whom I will. And He said to the Fire: You are My punishment; I shall take vengeance with you upon whom I will. And each of you shall have its fill. As for the Fire, they will be cast into it, and it will say: Is there any more? Then they will be cast into it, and it will say: Is there any more? Until He places His foot in it, and it will say: Enough, enough. Al-Hafiz Isma'il said: This is a sahih hadith. And the mention of the foot in it is among what must be believed in, without subjecting it to interpretation or asking how. In the Sahih - and as for the mention of the disputation of Paradise and the Fire, it was narrated in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah."
"2311","The remainder of the narration of Qatadah from Anas. 2487 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - may Allah have mercy on him - that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them: Ibrahim ibn Mansur al-Khabbaz informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us; Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us; Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Saminah al-Baghdadi narrated to us; Waki' narrated to us, from Shu'bah, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the house of A'ishah and saw meat, so he said: Roast some of it for us, for it has reached its lawful state. In al-Bukhari and Muslim: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought meat given in charity to Barirah, so he said: It is charity for her and a gift for us. And the wordings of this are other than the wordings of that."
"2312","Another narration. 2488 - Abu Ja'far al-Saydalani Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us; Abdullah ibn Ja'far informed us; Isma'il ibn Abdullah narrated to us; Uthman ibn Salih al-Misri narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us; Jarir ibn Hazim informed me - ha. 2489 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that Abu Abdullah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them: Ibrahim, the grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us; Abu Ya'la Ahmad ibn Ali informed us; al-Harith ibn Miskin narrated to us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Qatadah - ha. 2490 - And Abu Isma'il Dawud ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn Ahmad ibn Mashadhah informed us - at Isfahan - that Ghanim ibn Khalid ibn Abd al-Wahid informed them: Abu Sahl Hamad ibn Ahmad ibn Walkiz al-Sayrafi informed us; Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Muhammad informed us; Ahmad ibn Amr informed us; Yunus ibn Abd al-A'la narrated to us; Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two rams for al-Hasan and al-Husayn. The wording of Uthman and al-Harith. Yunus said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two rams for Hasan and Husayn. Ibn Hibban narrated it, from al-Hasan ibn Sufyan, from Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami, from Ibn Wahb. This hadith was mentioned to Imam Ahmad, who said: Yes; Jarir errs in the hadith of Qatadah. And Abu Hatim al-Razi said: Jarir erred in this hadith; it is rather Qatadah, from Ikrimah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed - as mursal."
"2313","Another narration. 2491 - Abu al-Futuh As'ad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Ijli, the Imam, the Mufti, informed us - at Isfahan - that Fatimah bint Abdullah al-Jawzdaniyyah informed them: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Ridhah informed us; Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us; Muhammad ibn Idris al-Halabi narrated to us; Sahl ibn Salih al-Antaki narrated to us; Waki' narrated to us, from Hammam ibn Yahya, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had four braids on his head."
"2314","Another narration. 2492 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali ibn Ubayd Allah al-Sufi informed us - at Baghdad - that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qazzaz informed them: Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn al-Ma'mun narrated to us; Ali - he is Ibn Umar al-Harbi - informed us; Ahmad ibn al-Hasan informed us; Abu Muhammad Khalaf ibn Salim narrated to us; Amr ibn Asim narrated to us; Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour shall not come until people boast to one another regarding mosques."
"2315","Another narration. 2493 - Abu Shakir Yahya ibn Yusuf ibn Ahmad al-Saqlatuni informed us - in his book - and my cousin, the jurist, the Imam Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us from him, that Abu al-Ma'ali Thabit ibn Bundar ibn Ibrahim al-Baqqal informed them: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shadhan informed us; Abu Amr Uthman ibn Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Daqqaq - known as Ibn al-Sammak - informed us; Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us; Affan narrated to us; Aban ibn Yazid informed us; Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: that a Jew invited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to barley bread and rancid melted fat, and he accepted."
"2316","2494 - And Abu Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Ma'ali al-Harimi informed us - at Baghdad - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us; Abdullah narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Abd al-Samad narrated to us; Aban narrated to us; Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas: that a Jew invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to barley bread and rancid melted fat, and he accepted. 2495 - And he said also: Affan narrated to us; Aban narrated to us. And in the narration of Affan: And Aban also said: A tailor."
"2317","Another narration. 2496 - Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Haddad informed them - while he was present: Abu Nu'aym Ahmad ibn Abdullah informed us; Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Humayd ibn Suhayl al-Mukharrimi al-Baghdadi narrated to us - at Baghdad: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Khaliq narrated to us; Sulayman ibn Tawbah al-Nahrawani narrated to us; Musa ibn Isma'il al-KhuttAli narrated to us; Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from his father, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Everything has an adornment, and the adornment of the Qur'an is a beautiful voice."
"2318","Another narration. 2497 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Abu Tahir Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu al-Dahdah Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Husayn al-Dimashqi narrated to us; Musa ibn Amir narrated to us; al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us; al-Awza'i narrated to us - ha. 2498 - Ibn al-Muqri said: And Abu Arubah informed us; Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us; Mu'ammal ibn al-Fadl informed us; al-Walid ibn Muslim informed us; al-Awza'i narrated to us. 2499 - And Umm Habibah A'ishah bint Ma'mar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Fakhir informed us - at Isfahan - that Sa'id ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them: Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us; Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us; Abu al-Dahdah Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Tamimi al-Dimashqi narrated to us; Abu Amir Musa ibn Amir ibn Khuraym narrated to us; al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us; al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, who said: A man was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they mentioned his strength in jihad and his striving in worship. Then the man came forth, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, I see in his face a touch of Satan. Then he came forth and greeted them, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Did you say to yourself, when you looked down upon us, that there is none among the people better than you? He said: Yes. And he went away, marked out a place of prayer, and lined up his feet in prayer. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which of you will rise to him and kill him? So Abu Bakr went, and found him praying. He said: So he deemed it grave to kill him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Which of you will rise to him and kill him? So Umar rose and said: I shall go to him. And he found him praying, and did the like of what Abu Bakr had done. Then he returned, and Ali said: I will. So he said: You, if you reach him. So he went, and found that he had departed. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the first horn to emerge from my nation; had he been killed, no two of my nation would have differed. Then he said: The Children of Isra'il split into seventy-one sects, and my nation shall split into seventy-two sects, all of them in the Fire except one, and it is the Jama'ah. The wording is one, except that in the narration of al-Thaqafi: first, and with him: in my nation."
"2319","Another narration. 2500 - And Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Mansur Mahmud ibn Isma'il al-Sayrafi informed them - while he was present: Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Shadhan informed us; Abdullah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us; Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us; Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us; al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us; al-Awza'i narrated to us; Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My nation shall split into seventy-three sects, all of them in the Fire except one, and it is the Jama'ah. Ibn Majah brought it in his Sunan, from Hisham ibn Ammar, thus abridged."
"2320","Another narration. 2501 - Abu al-Futuh Yusuf ibn al-Mubarak ibn Kamil al-Khaffaf informed us - at Baghdad - that Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Qazzaz informed them: Abd al-Samad ibn Ali ibn al-Ma'mun informed us; Ali - he is Ibn Umar al-Harbi - narrated to us; Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us; Khalaf ibn Salim narrated to us; Bahz narrated to us - ha. 2502 - And Abu Ahmad Abdullah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them: al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us; Ahmad ibn Ja'far informed us; Abdullah ibn Ahmad narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Bahz narrated to us; Abu al-Awwam al-Qattan narrated to us - Ahmad ibn Hanbal said: And he is Imran ibn Dawar, and he is blind - Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Ibn Umm Maktum over Madinah twice as his deputy, leading them in prayer while he was blind. The wording is the same."
"2321","2503 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Zuhayr narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (Ha: the chain transforms here; the matn continues in the following narration)."
"2322","2504 - And Abu al-Qasim Mahmud ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn al-Fadl al-Haddad informed us - at Isfahan - that Masud ibn al-Hasan al-Thaqafi informed them, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali al-Simsar informed us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid stated his word, Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us, al-Mukharrimi - meaning Muhammad ibn Abd Allah - narrated to us, Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Imran al-Qattan, from Qatada, from Anas - may Allah be pleased with him - that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Ibn Umm Maktum as deputy over Madina twice. He said: And I saw him on the day of al-Qadisiyya with a black banner. Their wording is one. Imam Ahmad narrated it from Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi. And Abu Dawud brought it in his Sunan from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Anbari and Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Mukharrimi - both - from Ibn Mahdi. And Imran al-Qattan - there is criticism regarding him. And the narration of Ibn Mahdi from him strengthens his case, and Allah knows best."
"2323","Another: 2505 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Isbahani informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar ibn Ahmad ibn Faris informed us, Yunus ibn Habib informed us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Imran narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer will be given in Paradise the strength of such-and-such of women. I said: O Messenger of Allah, and can he bear that? He said: He will be given the strength of a hundred."
"2324","2506 - And Abu Jafar informed us - also - that al-Hasan informed them - while present - Abu Nuaym informed us, Abu Amr Abd al-Malik ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Fadl al-Saqati narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah al-Basri narrated to us, Amr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man in Paradise will be given the strength of such-and-such of women. We said: O Messenger of Allah, and can he bear that? He said: He will be given the strength of a hundred. Al-Tirmidhi narrated it similarly in (Description of Paradise), from Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Mahmud ibn Ghaylan - both - from Abu Dawud, and said: A sahih gharib hadith, we do not know it from the hadith of Qatada from Anas except from the hadith of Imran al-Qattan. And Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, freedman of Thaqif, from Ubayd Allah ibn Jarir ibn Jabala, from Amr ibn Marzuq."
"2325","Another: 2507 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Abi al-Fath informed us - at Isfahan, may Allah have mercy on him - that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them - while present - Abu Nuaym al-Isbahani informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn Khalid ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Musa ibn Abi Sahl al-Misri narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr al-Kirmani narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divorced Hafsa, and the people were grieved by that, and her maternal uncle Uthman ibn Mazun and her brother Qudama entered upon her, and while they were with her grieving, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Hafsa and said: O Hafsa, Jibril came to me just now and said: Indeed Allah conveys peace to you and says to you: Take back Hafsa, for she is fasting, praying at night, and she is your wife in Paradise. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated this hadith from Shuba except Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr; Musa ibn Abi Sahl is alone in it. Al-Daraqutni said: Ubayd ibn Asbat and Muhammad ibn Thawab ibn Said narrated it from Asbat, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas. And others narrate it from Asbat, from Said, from Qatada, mursal, and that is the sahih. And likewise Said ibn Amir narrated it from Said, from Qatada, mursal, and that is the correct. I say: This narration which we narrated from the narration of Shuba is other than the narration of Said, and Allah knows best."
"2326","Another: 2508 - The Imam Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn al-Saffar informed us - at Naysabur - that Wajih ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us, Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Makhladi informed us, Abu Bakr - he is Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Isfarayini - narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Said ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ibn Kathir narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik (Ha: chain transforms here; matn follows in the next narration)."
"2327","2509 - And al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Asadi informed us - at Damascus - that his grandfather al-Husayn ibn Muhammad informed them, Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Nazif al-Farra informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn known as al-Sabuni narrated to us, Fahd ibn Sulayman al-Dalani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Awzai, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr and Umar: These two are the masters of the elderly of Paradise among the first and the last, except the Prophets and Messengers. Their wording is the same."
"2328","2510 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Mustamli informed them, Ishaq ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sabuni informed us, Abu al-Hasan - he is Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Musa - informed us, Abu Ishaq - he is Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Musa al-Hashimi - informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Qurashi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abu Bakr and Umar are the masters of the elderly of Paradise. Al-Tirmidhi brought it from al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah al-Bazzar, from Muhammad ibn Kathir, from al-Awzai with its chain, and said: A hasan gharib hadith from this angle. And al-Bukhari said: This is a munkar hadith. Al-Tirmidhi said: Muhammad only deemed objectionable this from the hadith of Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"2329","Another: 2511 - Abu Bakr al-Qasim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar al-Saffar informed us - at Naysabur - that Abu Bakr Wajih ibn Tahir ibn Muhammad al-Shahhami informed them, Abu Hamid Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Azhari informed us, Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Makhladi informed us, Abu Bakr - he is Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Muslim - informed us, Yusuf - meaning Ibn Said ibn Muslim - narrated to us, Ibn Kathir - he is Muhammad - narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Qatada, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will remain a group of my umma fighting upon the truth, victorious until the Day of Resurrection, and he gestured with his hand toward Syria. Imam Ahmad ibn Hanbal said: The burden is upon Muhammad ibn Kathir. He said: How many munkar narrations did he narrate? And al-Bukhari said: This is a munkar, mistaken hadith; it is only Qatada, from Mutarrif, from Imran."
"2330","Another: 2512 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us - there - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me, and that was at dawn: O Anas, I intend to fast, so feed me something. He said: So I brought him dates and a vessel of water after Bilal had called the adhan, and he said: O Anas, look for a person to eat with me. He said: So I called Zayd ibn Thabit, and he said: O Messenger of Allah, I drank a drink of sawiq and I intend to fast. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And I intend to fast. So he took sahur with him, then prayed two rakas, then went out and the prayer was established."
"2331","2513 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali al-Mawsili informed us, Muhammad ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I intend to fast, so do you have anything? He said: So I brought him a tray with dates and a vessel of water after Bilal had called the adhan, and he said: Look for a person to eat. So I went out and found Zayd ibn Thabit, and he mentioned the rest similarly. Something like this has been narrated in the Sahih, except that in this there are wordings not in that, and in this hadith is a fine clarification of what we have put forward in this book of ours that a Companion may narrate the hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and may narrate it with another wording from another Companion, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). For in Sahih al-Bukhari and Muslim is from the hadith of Anas ibn Malik, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that he took sahur with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Then we went out to prayer. Anas said: So I said to Zayd: How long was between that? He said: The recitation of fifty verses. And al-Bukhari narrated it from the hadith of Said ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Zayd ibn Thabit took sahur ... the hadith."
"2332","Another: 2514 - Abu al-Maali Muhammad ibn Safi ibn Abd Allah al-Naqqash informed us - at Baghdad - that Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Hajji al-Muqri - known as al-Mazrafi - informed them (Ha). 2515 - And Abu Hamid Abd Allah ibn Muslim ibn Thabit - known as Ibn Jawaliq - informed us - at Baghdad - that Yahya ibn Ali ibn al-Tarrah informed them, both said: Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Muhtadi Billah narrated to us - from his wording - he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf - he is Ibn Muhammad al-Allaf - informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad - he is Ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi - narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Awn al-Kharraz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood until his feet swelled, or he said: his shanks (Ha)."
"2333","2516 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Abd Allah ibn Awn al-Kharraz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Abdi narrated to us, from Misar, from Qatada, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood until his feet or his shanks swelled, so it was said to him: Has Allah not forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what followed? He said: Should I not be a grateful slave. Their wording is the same. Abu al-Hasan al-Daraqutni said: Muhammad ibn Bishr is alone in it from Misar, and none narrated it except Abd Allah ibn Awn. And al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Aswad followed him. I say: Al-Bukhari narrated it from Abu Nuaym and Khallad - both - from Misar, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqa, from al-Mughira ibn Shuba. Al-Daraqutni said: And that is the correct."
"2334","Another: 2517 - The Hafiz Abu Musa Abd Allah ibn Abd al-Ghani al-Maqdisi narrated to us - from his wording - he said: Abu Said Khalil ibn Ahmad ibn Thabit ibn Rawh al-Razi informed them - recitation to him - he said: Abu Ali al-Haddad informed us (Ha). 2518 - And Abu al-Ala Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Isbahani informed us - in his book - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Hafs informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us (Ha). 2519 - And Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn Abi Mansur ibn Muhammad ibn Yanal al-Sufi informed us, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Hamad ibn al-Hasan al-Duni informed them, Abu Nasr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Kassar informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn al-Sunni informed us, Abu Abd al-Rahman Ahmad ibn Shuayb ibn Ali al-Nasai informed us, Ahmad ibn Hafs ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Ibrahim - he is Ibn Tahman - narrated to me, from Said ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Anas - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: Nothing was more beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after women than horses. The wording is Ibn al-Sunni's. And al-Tabarani said: Nothing after women was more beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than horses. Thus al-Nasai brought it in his book."
"2335","Another: 2520 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Darir informed us - may Allah have mercy on him - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Musa - he is Ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Basri - narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman - he is Ibn Mahdi - narrated to us, from al-Muthanna, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when a severe wind blew, would say: O Allah, I ask You of the good of what it was commanded with, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what it was commanded with."
"2336","Another: 2521 - Al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali al-Harimi informed us - at Baghdad - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Husayn informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar al-Qatii informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to me, Said ibn Amir narrated to me, from Shuba, from Qatada, from Anas, that uncles of his testified before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to the sighting of the crescent, so he commanded the people to break fast and to go out to their Eid the next day. Abu Hatim al-Razi and Abu al-Hasan al-Daraqutni said: Said ibn Amir erred in it. I say: What is known is from the hadith of Abu Umayr ibn Anas, that uncles of his, and Allah knows best."
"2337","Another: 2522 - My maternal uncle, the jurist Imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi informed us - may Allah have mercy on him - that Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Yusuf informed them, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Yusuf informed them, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran informed us, the Hafiz Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar al-Daraqutni informed us, al-Qadi al-Husayn ibn Ismail narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Jarir ibn Jabala narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Aisha narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Anas: that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, did Allah not say: Divorce is twice, so why has it become three? He said: Then either retention in kindness or release in excellence."
"2338","2523 - And Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Tamimi al-Muaddib informed us - at Isfahan - that Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Ibrahim ibn Umar ibn al-Hasan ibn Yunus informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhakwani informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Musa ibn Mardawayh al-Hafiz informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Jarir ibn Jabala narrated to us, Ibn Aisha narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah mentioned divorce twice, so where is the third? He said: Then either retention in kindness or release in excellence."
"2339","Another: 2524 - Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us - there - that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them - recitation to him - al-Hakim Abu al-Hasan Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Ahmad al-Ismaili informed us, Abu Zakariyya Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Harb informed us, Abu Hatim Makki ibn Abdan ibn Bakr al-Naysaburi informed us - recitation to him - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn - he is Ibn Tarkhan - narrated to us, Umar ibn Sahl narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married fifteen women, consummated with eleven of them, and died leaving nine."
"2340","Another: 2525 - Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi al-Darir informed us - may Allah have mercy on him, at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Ibn Abi Samina - he is Muhammad ibn Yahya - narrated to us, Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Husayn al-Muallim, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The slave does not reach the reality of faith until he loves for people what he loves for himself of good. In it is an addition over what is in the Sahih: the mention of the reality of faith."
"2341","Another: 2526 - Abu al-Mutahhar Said ibn Rawh ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrawayh al-Salihani - at Isfahan informed us that Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Kanjarudhi informed us, Abu Amr and Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Hamdan al-Khayri informed us, Abu Ishaq Imran ibn Musa ibn Shuja al-Sakhtiyani informed me, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was aided with al-Saba, and Ad were destroyed by al-Dabur."
"2342","2527 - And Abu al-Futuh Asad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Ijli informed us - at Isfahan - that Fatima bint Abd Allah informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridha informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was aided with al-Saba, and Ad were destroyed by al-Dabur. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Qatada except Abu Awana; Muhammad ibn Aban is alone in it. Al-Daraqutni said: Muhammad ibn Aban al-Wasiti narrated it from Abu Awana, from Qatada, from Anas, and others narrate it from Abu Awana, from Qatada, mursal."
"2343","2528 - And Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Ahmad ibn Mahmud al-Thaqafi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, my father Mahmud informed us, Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was aided with al-Saba, and Ad were destroyed by al-Dabur, and al-Janub is from the wind of Paradise. And it has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, without mention of al-Janub."
"2344","Another: 2529 - Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Harbi informed us - at al-Harbiyya - that Hibat Allah ibn al-Husayn informed them, Abu Ali ibn al-Mudhhib informed us, Abu Bakr al-Qatii informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Bahz narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, Anas narrated to us that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I was walking in Paradise, I came upon a palace. He said: I said: To whom is this, O Jibril? - and I hoped it would be mine - He said: He said: For Umar. He said: Then I walked a while, and I came upon a palace better than the first palace. He said: So I said: To whom is this, O Jibril? - and I hoped it would be mine - He said: He said: For Umar, and in it are of the houris, O Abu Hafs, and nothing prevented me from entering it except your jealousy. He said: So Umar's eyes filled with tears, then he said: Over you I would not be jealous. And Humayd, al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, and Abu Imran al-Jawni narrated it from Anas similarly. And Misar narrated it from Qatada."
"2345","2530 - Abu Tahir Muawiya ibn Ali ibn Muawiya al-Sufi informed us - in his book - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad informed them, Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Hashim ibn Marthad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Ismail ibn Aban al-Warraq narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise, and I came upon a palace, so I said: To whom is this? So it was said: To Umar ibn al-Khattab. And it has preceded in the narration of Humayd from Anas, and it has a witness in the Sahih from the narration of Jabir ibn Abd Allah."
"2346","Another: 2531 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Muhammad ibn Yahya, he is Ibn Abi Samina, narrated to us, al-Khalil ibn Umar al-Abdi narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Richness is not from abundance of wealth, but richness is richness of the soul. Umar ibn Ibrahim was declared trustworthy by Ahmad and Yahya ibn Main. It has a witness in al-Bukhari from the hadith of Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra."
"2347","2532 - And my maternal uncle the jurist Imam Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Qudama, and my cousin the jurist Imam Abu Muhammad Abd al-Rahman ibn Ibrahim ibn Ahmad al-Maqdisis - may Allah have mercy on them and be pleased with them - informed us that Shuhda bint Ahmad ibn al-Faraj ibn Umar al-Ibari informed them, al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Talha al-Niali informed us, Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bishran informed us - he said: Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Amr ibn al-Bakhtari al-Razzaz informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik Abu Jafar al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Khalil ibn Umar ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Abdi narrated to us, Qatada narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, a speaker said: O Messenger of Allah, is richness abundance of wealth? He said: Say: Richness is richness of the soul. And it has preceded in the narration of Humayd from Anas."
"2348","Another: 2533 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while present - Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr ibn Abi Ali informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, al-Fudayl ibn al-Husayn Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us, al-Qattad, he is Abu Ismail Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Malik, narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, from Anas: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a dead young goat and said to them: Do you see this was worthless to its owners? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the world is more worthless to Allah than this is to its owners. And Muslim narrated something like this from the narration of Jabir ibn Abd Allah."
"2349","Another: 2534 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Sufi at Herat informed us that Tamim ibn Abi Said ibn Abi al-Abbas al-Jurjani informed them, Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Bahhathi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani informed us, Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban ibn Ahmad al-Busti informed us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Umayya at Tarsus informed us, Nuh ibn Habib al-Badhashi al-Qumasi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Gentleness was never in anything except it adorned it, and foulness was never in anything except it disgraced it. Thus Ibn Hibban brought it in his book."
"2350","Another: 2535 - Abu Ahmad Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ali ibn Ali al-Sufi at Baghdad informed us that Ismail ibn Ahmad ibn Umar al-Samarqandi informed them, the Sharif Abu Muhammad Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Ali informed us, he said: The Qadi Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Husayn informed us, recitation to him, the Qadi Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Unaysi narrated to us. 2536 - And Abu al-Wafa Mahmud ibn Abi al-Qasim ibn Umar, known as Hamaka, grandson of Muhammad ibn Abi Sad al-Baghdadi - in his book from Isfahan - informed us that Abu al-Ala Muhammad ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Muhammad al-Firsani informed them - in the year 495 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar informed us, Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Umar ibn Bashir al-Thaqafi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Sahl narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas who said: When: And warn your nearest kin was revealed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wept, then gathered his family and said: O sons of Abd Manaf, save yourselves from the Fire; O sons of Abd al-Muttalib, save yourselves from the Fire; O sons of Hashim, save yourselves from the Fire. Then he turned to Fatima and said: O Fatima bint Muhammad, save yourself from the Fire; I avail you nothing against Allah, except that you have kinship which I shall keep moist with its moisture."
"2351","2537 - And Shaykh Abu al-Qasim Ahmad ibn Abi al-Qasim informed us. Another: 2538 - Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Muaddib informed us that Ali ibn Tarrad ibn Muhammad al-Zaynabi informed them, Ali ibn Ahmad ibn al-Busri informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mukhallis informed us, al-Husayn ibn Ismail narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Basri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The dog, the donkey, and the woman cut off prayer. And it has preceded. And it has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayra."
"2352","Another: 2539 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them - while present - Abu al-Husayn Ahmad ibn Fadhshah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl al-Asfati narrated to us, Huraym ibn Uthman al-Rasibi narrated to us, Umar ibn Said narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Then when his Lord manifested to the mountain He made it crumbled. He said: He manifested to it with His little finger. What is well-known is from the narration of Thabit from Anas. And Abu Bakr ibn Mardawayh narrated it from al-Tabarani, from al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl, from Huraym ibn Uthman, from Muhammad ibn Sawaa, from Said ibn Abi Aruba."
"2353","Another: 2540 - Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad ibn Abi al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Asad al-Harawi informed us, with my recitation to him there; I said to him: Zahir ibn Tahir al-Shahhami informed you, recitation to him while you listened; he said: Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya informed us, he said: Abu Tahir Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Khuzayma informed us, my grandfather Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Ribi al-Qabasi narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Qatada, Thabit, and Humayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that they would hear from him a melody in Zuhr with Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High and Has there come to you the story of the Overwhelming. Thus Ibn Khuzayma brought it in his book."
"2354","2541 - And Abu Rawh Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Harawi informed us there that Tamim ibn Abi Said ibn Abi al-Abbas al-Jurjani informed them, Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Bahai informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani informed us, Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban ibn Ahmad al-Busti informed us, Ibn Qahtaba informed us, Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Qatada, Thabit, and Humayd, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that they would hear from him in Zuhr a melody with Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High and Has there come to you the story of the Overwhelming. Thus Ibn Hibban brought it in his book. And he narrated similar from Abu Bakr ibn al-Nadr ibn Anas, from his grandfather."
"2355","Another: 2542 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, by ijaza if not by hearing, Ibrahim ibn Mansur, grandson of Bahrawayh, informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Muhammad, he is Ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutayba, narrated to us, Muhammad, he is Ibn Abi al-Sari, narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Qatada. And Yahya ibn Abi Kathir mentioned it from Qatada, from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man prostrating while clearing his hair, he said: May Allah make your hair ugly. So one of them said in his hadith: So his hair fell out, and the other said: So his head became bald."
"2356","Another: 2543 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us that Zahir ibn Tahir informed them, Abu Yala Ishaq ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Sabuni informed us, Abu Said Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Razi informed us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: Whoever desires the life of this world and its adornment, to His saying: Those are they for whom there is nothing in the Hereafter but the Fire. He said: It was revealed concerning the Jews and Christians."
"2357","2544 - And the Imam Abu Ishaq Ibrahim ibn al-Muzaffar ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Burni at Mosul informed us that Abu Ali Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad al-Burji al-Attar informed them, Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Talha informed us, Abu Umar Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Mahdi informed us, Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Ismail al-Mahamili narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Yazid al-Bahrani narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas who said: Whoever desires the life of this world and its adornment, We shall pay them their deeds therein and they shall not be wronged therein - meaning: the Jews and Christians."
"2358","Another: 2545 - Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid informed us in his book from Isfahan that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, Abu Nuaym informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ibrahim ibn Hashim narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Arara narrated to us, he said: Muadh ibn Hisham handed us a book, he said: I heard it from my father, and in it was from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram in his Hajj during one of the two evening prayers. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Qatada except Hisham."
"2359","Another: 2546 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while present - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, Ismail ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Musa ibn Khalaf narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in the two rakas of Fajr: Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, One."
"2360","2547 - And the Imam Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Lanjani informed us - may Allah have mercy on him - that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn al-Abbas ibn Ali al-Rustumi informed them, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Tayyan informed us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Khurshid stated his word, Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Naysaburi informed us, Yazid ibn Sinan narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Musa ibn Khalaf narrated to me, my father narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in the two rakas of Fajr: Say: O disbelievers, and Say: He is Allah, One. Musa was praised by a group of Imams and others criticized him, and Allah knows best, and it has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Abu Hurayra."
"2361","Another: 2548 - Abu al-Tahir Ismail ibn Salih ibn Yasin informed us - at al-Shari - that Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Razi informed them, recitation to him, Abu Ahmad al-Abbas ibn al-Fadl ibn Jafar ibn al-Furat the minister at Egypt informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Muhandis informed us, Abu Bishr al-Dulabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Musa narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a sermon one day when the sun was about to set and said: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, what remains of your world compared to what has passed is only like what remains of this day of yours compared to what has passed of it, and we see of the sun only a little."
"2362","2549 - And Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while present - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, Ismail ibn Abd Allah Samuwayh narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Musa narrated to me, my father narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed his Companions when the sun was about to set and nothing remained of it except a small edge, and said: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), what remains of your world compared to what has passed is only like what remains of this day of yours compared to what has passed of it, and we see of the sun only a little."
"2363","Another: 2550 - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abi Abd Allah ibn Makki al-Nahrawani informed us - at Baghdad - that Abu Muhammad Sulayman ibn Masud ibn al-Husayn ibn Hamid al-Shahham informed them - recitation to him - Abu Ghalib Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Baqillani informed us, he said: Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Ibrahim ibn Shadhan informed us, he said: Abu al-Qasim Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hasan al-Qadi al-Hamadhani informed us - he came to us as a pilgrim, recitation to him - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor of the house has most right to the house."
"2364","2551 - And Zahir al-Thaqafi informed us, that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Ahmad ibn ... narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor of the house has most right to the house."
"2365","2552 - And Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Sufi al-Harawi informed us - there - that Tamim ibn Abi Said al-Jurjani informed them, Ali ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Bihai informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Harun al-Zawzani informed us, Abu Hatim Muhammad ibn Hibban ibn Ahmad al-Busti informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad informed us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The neighbor of the house has most right to the house. Thus Ibn Hibban brought it."
"2366","2553 - And Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Isbahani informed us, by ijaza, that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, Abu Nuaym informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus informed us, Said ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor of the house has most right to the house. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Qatada except Said; Isa ibn Yunus is alone in it. Al-Daraqutni said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated it from Said, from Qatada, from Anas, and erred in it; others narrate it from Said, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura. And likewise Shuba and others narrated it from Qatada, and that is the correct. I say: And ... narrated it. Al-Nasai narrated it from Ishaq."
"2367","Another: 2554 - Abu Mansur al-Dahhak ibn Ghanim ibn Hamad ibn Ali al-Isbahani informed us - in writing - that Ghanim ibn Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Burji informed them, Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Sawwaf informed us, Abbas ibn Ibrahim al-Qaratisî narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about coitus interruptus, and he said: Do you create it? Do you provide for it? Leave it in its resting place, for it is only what was decreed for it. Al-Daraqutni said: Muadh ibn Hisham narrates it from his father, from Qatada, from Anas; Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated it from him thus. And the mention of Anas in it is an error. What is preserved is from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Abu Said al-Khudri."
"2368","Another: 2555 - Abu al-Husayn Abd al-Haqq ibn Abd al-Khaliq ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir ibn Yusuf informed us - in writing - and my maternal uncle the Imam, scholar Abu Muhammad Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi - may Allah have mercy on him - informed us from him that Abu Tahir Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Qadir informed them, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Bishran informed us, Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Umar ibn Ahmad al-Daraqutni al-Hafiz informed us, Abu Talib al-Hafiz Ahmad ibn Nasr ibn Talib informed us, Abu Hamza Idris ibn Yunus al-Farra narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Said ibn Jidar narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik - that Jibril, peace be upon him - came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Makka when the sun declined, and commanded him to call the people to prayer when it was obligated upon them. So Jibril, peace be upon him, stood in front of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the people stood behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So he prayed four rakas in which he did not recite aloud; the people followed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in prayer, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) followed Jibril - peace be upon him. Then he waited until the time of Asr entered, and he prayed with them four rakas in which he did not recite aloud; the Muslims followed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) followed Jibril. Then he waited until the sun set, and he prayed with them three rakas, reciting aloud in two rakas and not aloud in the third. Then he waited until a third of the night had gone, and he prayed with them four rakas, reciting aloud in the first two and not aloud in the last two. Then he waited until dawn rose, and he prayed with them two rakas reciting aloud in them. Thus al-Daraqutni brought it in his Sunan."
"2369","Another: 2556 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while present - Abu Nuaym informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us, Baqiyya narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, he said: Qatada narrated to me, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stopped at a place, would not depart from it until he prayed Zuhr. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Shuba except Baqiyya. I say: And ... narrated it from Anas."
"2370","Another: 2557 - Zahir ibn Ahmad informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Ali informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Naqid narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ubayd Allah Abu Ayyub al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Mamar, from Qatada, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man put on sandals standing. And al-Tirmidhi narrated it from Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Abi al-Husayn al-Simnani, from Sulayman, and said: A gharib hadith, and he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail said: This is not sahih."
"2371","Another: 2558 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - at Isfahan - that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, al-Hasan ibn al-Bazzar narrated to us, Shababa narrated to us, from al-Mughira ibn Muslim, from Matar, from Qatada, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking standing, eating standing, from al-Jallala, and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin. In the Sahih is the prohibition of drinking standing."
"2372","Another: 2559 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr informed us - at Isfahan - that Mahmud ibn Ismail informed them - while present - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, the Qadi Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Maymun narrated to us, Abu Ayyub Sulayman ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Musab ibn Ibrahim al-Qaysi narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Indeed Allah has protected my umma from uniting upon misguidance."
"2373","Another: 2560 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad informed me - at Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while present - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu Muslim Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Nasih al-Dhuhli informed us, Musa ibn Harun ibn Abd Allah ibn Marwan al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Hajjaj al-Sarraf narrated to us, Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he passed on a road of Madina, was recognized by the scent of perfume."
"2374","Another: 2561 - Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Jafar ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Thaqafi informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridha informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us (Ha). 2562 - And Abu Tahir Muawiya ibn Ali ibn Muawiya al-Sufi informed us - by ijaza - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, al-Abbas ibn Hamdan, he is al-Isbahani, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa, he is al-Damaghani, narrated to us, Amr ibn Humran narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on al-Khumra. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it except Hisham, and none narrated it from Hisham except Amr ibn Humran."
"2375","Another: 2563 - Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Isbahani informed us - in his book - that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, Abu Nuaym informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Musa ibn Harun narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Rahawayh narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl informed us, Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, that a funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he stood, so it was said: It is the funeral of a Jew. So he said: We only stood for the angels. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Qatada except Hammad."
"2376","Another: 2564 - Abu Jafar al-Saydalani informed me - at Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu Muslim Muhammad ibn Mamar ibn Nasih al-Dhuhli informed us, Musa ibn Harun ibn Abd Allah ibn Marwan al-Qazzaz narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thalaba ibn Sawaa narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sawaa informed us, Hammam informed us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The sleeve of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was to his wrist."
"2377","Another: 2565 - Asad ibn Mahmud ibn Khalaf al-Ijli, the Imam Abu al-Futuh - at Isfahan - informed us that Fatima bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyya informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridha informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Zuhri al-Isbahani narrated to me, Ismail ibn Yazid narrated to us, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of your religion is its easiest. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Qatada except Sallam; Ismail ibn Yazid is alone in it."
"2378","Another: 2566 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Sadaqa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us, Baqiyya ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: When we stopped at a place we glorified Allah until we untied the saddles. Shuba said: Glorification with the tongue. Al-Tabarani said: None narrated it from Shuba except Baqiyya. I say: Hamza ibn Amr al-Dabbi narrated this hadith from Anas like the narration of Qatada, and it has preceded in his biography. And al-Daraqutni said: Meaning the preserved is what Hamza al-Dabbi narrated from Anas."
"2379","Another: 2567 - The Imam Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Maali ibn Ghanima ibn Abi Ghalib al-Faqih, known as Ibn al-Hillawi, informed us - with my recitation to him at Baghdad - I said to him: Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Nasr ibn al-Zaghuni informed you - recitation to him while you listened, so he acknowledged it - he said: al-Husayn ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Talha al-Maali informed us, the Qadi Abu al-Qasim al-Hasan ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn al-Mundhir informed us - recitation to him - he said: Abu al-Hasan Ali ibn Muhammad ibn al-Zubayr al-Kufi informed us - recitation to him - Ismail, he is Ibn Ali ibn Ismail al-Khutabi, narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Habib al-Marwazi al-Khadib Abu Bakr narrated to us, Affan narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How can I enjoy while the companion of the Trumpet has taken the horn and bent his back, looking toward the Throne as though his eyes are two brilliant stars, never blinking out of fear of being commanded before that."
"2380","Another: 2568 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while present - Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ahmad informed us, Ahmad ibn Bundar ibn Ishaq al-Shaar informed us, Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Maymun narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, Musab ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most merciful of my umma is Abu Bakr, and the most knowledgeable of them of the lawful and unlawful is Muadh ibn Jabal."
"2381","Another: 2569 - Abu al-Qasim Mahmud ibn Muhammad ibn Mahmud ibn al-Fadl al-Haddad informed us - at Isfahan, may Allah have mercy on him - that Masud ibn al-Hasan ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl informed them, al-Mutahhar ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Buzani informed us, Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Khurshid stated his word, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Isa al-Khawwas narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Mughira al-Jawhari narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Salih narrated to us, Musa ibn Khalaf narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was exhorting his Companions when three men passed by; one of them came and sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the second walked a little and sat, and as for the third he went on. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you about these three? As for this one who came and sat with us, he repented, so He turned to him; and as for the one who walked and sat, he was shy, so Allah was shy of him; and as for the one who passed on his way, he was independent, so Allah was independent of him, and Allah is Rich, Praiseworthy. And this hadith has a witness in the Sahihayn from the narration of Abu Waqid al-Harith ibn Awf al-Laythi - may Allah be pleased with him."
"2382","2570 - Another: Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Muqri informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Aruzzi narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Said narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas who said: The two clans of the Ansar, al-Aws and al-Khazraj, boasted. Al-Aws said: Among us is the one washed by the angels: Hanzala ibn al-Rahib; and among us is the one at whose death the Throne of the Merciful shook: Sad ibn Muadh; and among us is the one protected by wasps: Asim ibn Thabit ibn al-Aqlah; and among us is the one whose testimony was accepted as the testimony of two men: Khuzayma ibn Thabit. So the Khazrajis said: Among us are four who gathered the Quran, whom none other gathered: Zayd ibn Thabit, Abu Zayd, Ubayy ibn Kab, and Muadh ibn Jabal."
"2383","2571 - And Abd al-Muizz ibn Muhammad al-Sufi informed us - at Herat - that Tamim ibn Abi Said ibn Abi al-Abbas al-Jurjani informed them - recitation to him - Abu Amir al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ali al-Nasawi al-Qumasi informed us - recitation to him - Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Asim ibn Zadham informed us, Abu Aruba al-Husayn ibn Abi Mashar al-Harrani informed us, Ibrahim ibn Said narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Said, from Qatada, from Anas, who said: The two clans al-Aws and al-Khazraj boasted. Al-Aws said: Among us is the one washed by the angels: Hanzala ibn Abi Amir; and among us is the one protected by wasps: Asim ibn Thabit ibn al-Aqlah; and among us is the one for whom the Throne shook: Sad ibn Muadh; and among us is the one whose testimony was accepted as the testimony of two men: Khuzayma ibn Thabit. So the Khazrajis said: Among us are four who gathered the Quran, whom none other gathered: Ubayy ibn Kab, Muadh ibn Jabal, Zayd, and Abu Zayd - may Allah be pleased with them all. It is mentioned in the Sahih. And the hadith of Anas mentions in it the shaking of the Throne and the mention of the four who gathered the Quran; as for the mention of Asim and that wasps protected him, al-Bukhari narrated it from the narration of Abu Hurayra."
"2384","2572 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Isbahani informed us - there - that Fatima bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyya informed them - recitation to her - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridha informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from Anas who said: The two clans al-Aws and al-Khazraj boasted. Al-Aws said: Among us are four, and al-Khazraj said: Among us are four. Al-Aws said: Among us is the one for whom the Throne of the Merciful shook: Sad ibn Muadh. And among us is the one whose testimony equaled the testimony of two men: Khuzayma ibn Thabit. And among us is the one washed by the angels: Hanzala ibn al-Rahib. And among us is the one whose flesh wasps protected: Asim ibn Thabit ibn al-Aqlah. And al-Khazraj said: Among us are four who gathered the Quran in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), whom none other gathered: Ubayy ibn Kab, Muadh ibn Jabal, Zayd ibn Thabit, and Abu Zayd. I say: ... Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Shayba - there is criticism of him - but I brought it as a witness."
"2385","Al-Qasim ibn Uthman Abu al-Ala al-Hadrami, from Anas. 2573 - Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur al-Khabbaz informed us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna informed us, Mahmud ibn Khidash narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Uthman Abu al-Ala al-Basri narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that a man of Banu Zuhra met Umar before he became Muslim, and he was wearing his sword, and said: Where are you heading, O Umar? He said: I want to kill Muhammad! He said: How can you be safe among Banu Hashim and Banu Zuhra after killing Muhammad? He said: I see you have only become a Sabian and left your religion which you are upon? He said: Shall I not point you to something astonishing, O Umar? Your brother-in-law and your sister have become Sabians and left their religion which they are upon. He said: So he walked to them angrily - Ishaq said: meaning enraged - until he drew near the door. He said: And with them was a man called Khabbab reciting to them Sura Ta-Ha. He said: When Khabbab heard Umar's sound he entered under a bed of theirs. He said: What is this murmur I heard at your place? They said: Nothing but talk we were talking between us. He said: Perhaps you have become Sabians and left your religion which you are upon? So his brother-in-law said: O Umar, what if the truth is in other than your religion? He said: So he turned on his brother-in-law and trampled him severely. He said: So his sister pushed him from her husband, so he struck her face and her face bled. He said: So she said to him: What if the truth is in other than your religion? I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. He said: So Umar said: Show me this book you were reading. He said: And Umar used to read books. He said: So his sister said: No, you are impure; give us a covenant with Allah that you will return it to us, and stand, wash, and perform wudu. He said: So he did. He said: So Umar read: Ta-Ha, We did not send down the Quran upon you to distress you, to His saying: There is no god but I, so worship Me and establish prayer for My remembrance. Indeed the Hour is coming, I almost conceal it. Umar said: Guide me to Muhammad. He said: When Khabbab heard Umar's saying, Guide me to Muhammad - peace be upon him - he came out to him and said: Rejoice, O Umar, for I hope you are the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Thursday evening: O Allah, strengthen the religion with Umar ibn al-Khattab or with Amr ibn Hisham. He said: They said: He is in the house at the foot of al-Safa where revelation comes to him. He said: So Umar set out with Hamza ibn Abd al-Muttalib and some of the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the door. When Hamza saw the people's fear of Umar, he said: Yes, this is Umar; if Allah intends good for him he will become Muslim and follow the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and if otherwise, killing him will be easy for us. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to him, took hold of his garment and sword straps, and said: Will you not desist, O Umar, until Allah brings upon you of disgrace and punishment what He brought upon al-Walid ibn al-Mughira? O Allah, guide Umar ibn al-Khattab; O Allah, strengthen the religion with Umar. So Umar said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he became Muslim, then said: I shall go out, O Messenger of Allah."
"2386","2574 - And with it Abu Yala informed us, he said: And Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us, Ishaq al-Azraq narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Uthman al-Basri narrated to us, from Anas who said: Umar went out wearing his sword, and he mentioned similar or close to it."
"2387","2575 - Abu Yala said: And Abd al-Rahman ibn Marif narrated to us - at Basra - Ishaq ibn Yusuf Abu Muhammad al-Azraq narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Uthman Abu al-Ala al-Hadrami narrated to us, from Anas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on Thursday evening: O Allah, strengthen the religion with Umar ibn al-Khattab or with Amr ibn Hisham. He said: So Umar wore his sword, and a man of Banu Zuhra met him, and he mentioned similar or close to it. Al-Daraqutni narrated part of it from Abd Allah, from al-Hasan ibn al-Junayd, and from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Adami, from Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Munadi - both - from Ishaq al-Azraq."
"2388","2576 - And Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Ala ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Isbahani informed us - in his book - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Abi Awf - meaning al-Muaddal - narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nashali narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Uthman Abi al-Ala al-Basri, from Anas ibn Malik - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated on Thursday evening and said: O Allah, strengthen Islam with Umar ibn al-Khattab or with Amr ibn Hisham, so Umar awoke on Friday and became Muslim. Al-Tabarani said: Al-Qasim is alone in it. Perhaps one who says: How did he bring this hadith, when this hadith was at Makka and Anas was at Madina? So we say: Something like this has been narrated in the Sahih; Muslim narrated from the narration of Thabit, from Anas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) consulted when the approach of Abu Sufyan reached him. And in it: the mention of the black boy whom they seized."
"2389","Another: 2577 - Abu al-Ala Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Raja ibn Abd al-Wahid - known as Lafalaji, al-Isbahani, in his book - informed us that al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them, Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Abi Awf - he is al-Muaddal - narrated to us, Ismail ibn Isa al-Wasiti Saman narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Uthman Abu al-Ala al-Basri narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding wiping over the khuffs: three days for the traveler, and for the resident a day until night. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Ali ibn Abi Talib."
"2390","Another: 2578 - Abu Tahir Muawiya ibn Ali ibn Muawiya al-Sufi informed us - by ijaza - that Abu Ali al-Haddad informed them, Abu Nuaym al-Hafiz informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Ahmad ibn Abi Awf narrated to us, Ismail ibn Isa al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Uthman Abu al-Ala al-Basri narrated to us, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The first of what the slave will be reckoned for on the Day of Resurrection is prayer; if it is sound, the rest of his deeds are sound, and if it is corrupt, the rest of his deeds are corrupt."
"2391","2579 - And Abu al-Faraj Yahya ibn Mahmud ibn Said al-Thaqafi informed us - at Damascus, recitation to him - that his grandfather al-Hafiz Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl informed them, Abd al-Razzaq ibn Abd al-Karim al-Hasanabadhar informed us, Ahmad ibn Musa al-Hafiz informed us, Uthman ibn Muhammad al-Uthmani informed us, al-Numan ibn Ahmad al-Wasiti narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Khalaf ibn Zakariyya al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Ishaq - meaning al-Azraq - narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Uthman Abi al-Ala, from Anas ibn Malik - may Allah be pleased with him - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the first of what the slave will be reckoned for is his prayer; if his prayer is sound, the rest of his deeds are sound, and if his prayer is corrupt, the rest of his deeds are corrupt. He said: And he used to say: Align the shoulders in prayer, for Satan slips through the rows as kids slip through, and the right row is better than the left."
"2392","Limaza ibn Zabbar al-Jahdami Abu Labid, from Anas. 2580 - Abu al-Tahir al-Mubarak ibn Abi al-Maali informed us - at Baghdad - that Hibat Allah ibn Muhammad informed them, al-Hasan ibn Ali informed us, Ahmad ibn Jafar informed us, Abd Allah ibn Ahmad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Kamil - meaning al-Muzaffar ibn Mudrik - narrated to us, Said ibn Zayd narrated to us, al-Zubayr ibn Khirrit narrated to us, Abu Labid Limaza ibn Zabbar narrated to us, he said: Horses were sent out in the time of al-Hajjaj, and we said: If only we went to the race. He said: So we went to it, then we said: If only we went - and in a copy: inclined - to Anas ibn Malik and asked him: Did you race in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: So we went to him and asked him, and he said: Yes, he raced upon a horse of his called Sabaha, and it outran the people, and he rejoiced at that. Thus Imam Ahmad narrated it in his Musnad. And he also narrated it from Affan ibn Muslim, from Said ibn Zayd, from al-Zubayr."
"2393","2581 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Said ibn Abi al-Raja al-Sayrafi informed them, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ahmad informed us, Ubayd Allah ibn Yaqub informed us, my grandfather Ishaq ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Mani narrated to us, Yazid narrated to us, Said ibn Zayd informed us, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Khirrit, from Abu Labid, who said: I said to Anas: O Abu Hamza, did you race in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) race? He said: Yes, by Allah, he raced upon a horse called Sabaha, and it came first, and he rejoiced at that. Al-Daraqutni narrated it from Ali ibn Abd Allah ibn Mubashshir, from Ahmad ibn Sinan, from Yazid ibn Harun, from Said ibn Zayd. And from Ali also, from Ahmad ibn Sinan, from Affan ibn Muslim, from Said ibn Zayd, from al-Zubayr."
"2394","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi from Anas. 2582 - Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl informed us - at Isfahan - that Fatima bint Abd Allah al-Jawzdaniyya informed them, Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ridha informed us, Abu al-Qasim Sulayman ibn Ahmad al-Tabarani informed us, Muhammad ibn Imran al-Naqit al-Basri narrated to us, Abda ibn Abd Allah al-Saffar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Ruasi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: A man of Banu Kilab came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the stud fee of the stallion, and he forbade him. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, we lend and are honored? So he permitted him in the honorarium. Al-Tirmidhi brought it from Abda al-Saffar. And al-Nasai brought it from Isma ibn al-Fadl - both - from Yahya ibn Adam. And al-Tirmidhi said: A hasan gharib hadith, we do not know it except from the hadith of Ibrahim ibn Humayd. And al-Daraqutni said: Gharib from the hadith of Hisham, from Muhammad; Ibrahim is alone in it from him."
"2395","Muhammad ibn Abi Ismail, from Anas. 2583 - Abu al-Abbas Ahmad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Baqa al-Muqri informed us - at Baghdad - that Abu Mansur Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Khayrun informed them, Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muslima informed us, he said: It was read to the chief Abu al-Qasim Isa ibn the minister Ali ibn Isa ibn Dawud ibn al-Jarrah - while I listened - he said: It was read to Abu al-Qasim Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Baghawi, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from his brother Muhammad ibn Ali, from Muhammad ibn Abi Ismail, who said: I entered upon Anas ibn Malik and saw in his house a cup of wood, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to drink in it and perform wudu from it."
"2396","2584 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad ibn Hamid al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Adib al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ahmad ibn Ali ibn al-Muthanna al-Mawsili informed us, Uthman ibn Abi Shayba narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali - his brother - from Muhammad ibn Abi Ismail, who said: I entered upon Anas, and saw in his house a cup of wood; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to drink in it and perform wudu."
"2397","Muhammad ibn Sirin from Anas. 2585 - Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Ali al-Hasan ibn Ahmad al-Haddad informed them - while present - Abu Nuaym Ahmad ibn Abd Allah informed us, Abd Allah ibn Jafar informed us, Ismail ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama al-Harrani narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Abu Bakr - may Allah be pleased with him - brought his father Abu Quhafa to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makka, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Abu Bakr: Had you left the old man in his house I would have come to him, in honor of Abu Bakr. So he became Muslim while his head and beard were white like thaghama, so he said: Change this and avoid black for it."
"2398","2586 - And Abu al-Majd Zahir ibn Ahmad al-Thaqafi informed us - at Isfahan - that Abu Abd Allah al-Husayn ibn Abd al-Malik al-Khallal informed them, Ibrahim ibn Mansur informed us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim informed us, Abu Yala al-Mawsili informed us, al-Hasan ibn Abi Shuayb al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Ibn Sirin, who said: Anas was asked about the dyeing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned it and said at its end: And Abu Bakr brought his father Abu Quhafa to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makka, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had you left the old man in his house we would have come to him in honor of Abu Bakr. He said: So he became Muslim while his beard and head were like thaghama. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Change them and avoid black for him. Imam Ahmad brought it in his Musnad from Muhammad ibn Salama al-Harrani. And Abu Hatim Ibn Hibban brought it in his book from Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Thaqafi, from al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shuayb. It has a witness in the Sahih from the hadith of Jabir ibn Abd Allah."
"2399","Another: 2587 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Nasr al-Saydalani informed us - at Isfahan - that Mahmud ibn Ismail al-Sayrafi informed them - while present - Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Shadhan informed us, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Qabbab informed us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abi Asim informed us, Ayyub al-Wazzan narrated to us, Urwa ibn Marwan narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Amr, from Ayyub, from Ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to his family one day at midday and said: Do you have anything? They said: No. He said: Then I am fasting. Then he entered another time at midday and said: I am fasting if you have nothing. So they brought him something and he ate."
"2400","Another: 2588 - Abu al-Fath Abd Allah ibn Ahmad ibn Abi al-Fath al-Kharaqi informed us in his book, that his father Abu al-Abbas Ahmad informed them, Abu Mansur Abd al-Razzaq ibn Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ahmad ibn Jafar al-Khatib informed us, Abu Bakr Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Furak al-Qabbab narrated to us, Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Yahya ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Said al-Shaybani narrated to us, Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salama, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My intimate friend came to me smiling. He said: O Muhammad, I saw something astonishing. I said: My intimate friend, what did you see? He said: I saw kinship attached to the Throne calling every day three times: Indeed whoever joins me, I join him; indeed whoever cuts me, I cut him. So we looked into that kinship among fifteen forefathers."
